minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7040_0002_1363_55_SB_1865 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 1396.09 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "Rasulullah saw an old man walking supported by his two sons... Allah is not in need of this old man's torturing himself, and then he ordered him to ride" ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Translation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7040_1363_55_1396_09 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_SB_1865 ;
    minaret:startTime 1363.55 .

minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7040_0003_1442_61_SB_2860 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 1492.01 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "A horse may be kept for one of three reasons: for a man it may be a source of reward... whatever its rope allows it to eat will be regarded as a good rewardable deed... even its dung will be considered amongst his good deeds..." ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Translation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7040_1442_61_1492_01 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_SB_2860 ;
    minaret:startTime 1442.61 .

minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7040_0004_3050_77_SB_1562 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 3067.29 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "Aisha said: We set out with Allah's Messenger in the months of Hajj, and in the nights of Hajj, and at the time and places of Hajj, and in a state of Hajj" ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Translation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7040_3050_77_3067_29 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_SB_1562 ;
    minaret:startTime 3050.77 .

minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7040_0005_3068_21_SB_1545 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 3129.27 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "Rasulullah with his Sahaba they started from Medina for Makkah... while in Dhul Hulaifah... on the 25th of Dhu al-Qa'dah and when he reached Makkah it was the 4th of Dhu al-Hijjah" ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Translation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7040_3068_21_3129_27 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_SB_1545 ;
    minaret:startTime 3068.21 .

minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7040_0006_3262_93_SB_5089 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 3267.11 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "اَللّٰهُمَّ مَحِلِّيْ حَیْثُ حَبَسْتَنِیْ" ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Quotation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7040_3262_93_3267_11 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_SB_5089 ;
    minaret:startTime 3262.93 .

minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7040_0007_3267_11_SB_5089 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 3276.41 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "O Allah, I will exit ihram wherever You stop me" ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Translation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7040_3267_11_3276_41 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_SB_5089 ;
    minaret:startTime 3267.11 .

minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7040_0008_3392_29_SB_1564 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 3421.83 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "Rasulullah performed Hajj and Umrah together, so it was Qiran. But Rasulullah, he wished for Tamattu'. He said: 'And if I were to know my affair before what I had to do, I would not have brought with me the sacrificial animals...'" ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Translation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7040_3392_29_3421_83 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_SB_1564 ;
    minaret:startTime 3392.29 .

minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7041_0000_407_28_SM_1297 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 440.2 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "خُذُوا عَنِّي مَنَاسِكَكُمْ — Jabir reported: I saw Rasulullah flinging pebbles while riding his camel on the day of Nahr, saying: Learn your rituals from me, for I do not know whether I would be performing Hajj after this Hajj of mine" ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Translation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7041_407_28_440_2 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_SM_1297 ;
    minaret:startTime 407.28 .

minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7041_0001_467_62_AD_1919 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 507.52 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "Yazid bin Shaiban said: We were standing in Arafat in a place far from the place of standing... Ibn Mirba' al-Ansari came and said: I am the messenger of Rasulullah... Stay where you are for it is a place of ritual, for you are following the legacy of your father Ibrahim" ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Translation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7041_467_62_507_52 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_AD_1919 ;
    minaret:startTime 467.62 .

minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7041_0002_747_46_IbnMajah_2890 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 776.16 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "Rasulullah performed Hajj on an old saddle, wearing a cloak that was worth only four dirhams or less. Then he said: Allahumma hijjatun la riya'a fiha wala sum'ah — O Allah, a Hajj in which there is no showing off nor reputation sought" ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Translation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7041_747_46_776_16 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_IbnMajah_2890 ;
    minaret:startTime 747.46 .

minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7041_0003_1049_34_AD_1862 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 1079.72 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "Rasulullah said: If anyone breaks a bone or leg or becomes lame, he has come out of ihram and must perform Hajj the following year" ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Translation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7041_1049_34_1079_72 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_AD_1862 ;
    minaret:startTime 1049.34 .

minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7041_0004_1238_62_SM_1963 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 1257.94 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "Rasulullah said: Sacrifice only a grown-up animal unless it is difficult for you, in which case sacrifice a ram of more than six months of age" ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Translation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7041_1238_62_1257_94 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_SM_1963 ;
    minaret:startTime 1238.62 .

minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7041_0005_1283_68_SB_2731 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 1333.98 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "When Rasulullah made a peace deal with Quraysh... Um Salamah gave advice: Go out and do not say a word to anyone until you sacrifice your camel and call your barber to shave your head. When he did that, the Sahaba got up and offered their sacrifices" ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Translation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7041_1283_68_1333_98 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_SB_2731 ;
    minaret:startTime 1283.68 .

minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7041_0006_1358_82_SB_1806 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 1378.62 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "Abdullah bin Umar set out for Makkah intending to perform Umrah during the time of fitnah... and said: If I should be prevented from reaching the Kaaba, I would do the same as Rasulullah did in the year of Hudaybiyyah" ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Translation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7041_1358_82_1378_62 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_SB_1806 ;
    minaret:startTime 1358.82 .

minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7041_0007_1504_22_SB_1560 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 1534.58 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "Hafsa said: Ya Rasulullah, why have the people finished their Ihram after performing Umrah but you have not? He replied: I have matted my hair and garlanded my hady, so I will not finish my Ihram till I have slaughtered my animal" ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Translation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7041_1504_22_1534_58 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_SB_1560 ;
    minaret:startTime 1504.22 .

minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7041_0008_1615_82_SB_1571 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 1640.6 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "Imran bin Husayn said: The verse of Tamattu' was revealed in Allah's Book, so we performed it with Rasulullah, and nothing was revealed in the Quran to make it illegal nor did Rasulullah prohibit it till he died" ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Translation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7041_1615_82_1640_6 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_SB_1571 ;
    minaret:startTime 1615.82 .

minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7041_0009_1681_24_SB_1736 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 1726.3 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "Rasulullah stopped near Jamarat at Mina... A man said: I forgot and got my head shaved before slaughtering. He said: There is no harm, go and slaughter now... Whenever he was asked about anything performed before or after, his reply was: Do it now, there is no harm" ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Translation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7041_1681_24_1726_3 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_SB_1736 ;
    minaret:startTime 1681.24 .

minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7041_0010_2041_2_SB_1814 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 2067.64 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "Ka'b bin Ujrah reported that Rasulullah said to him regarding his head lice: Have your head shaved, then either fast three days, or feed six poor persons, or slaughter one sheep as a sacrifice" ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Translation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7041_2041_2_2067_64 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_SB_1814 ;
    minaret:startTime 2041.2 .

minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7041_0011_2310_48_SB_1997 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 2350.22 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "Aisha and Ibn Umar said: Nobody was allowed to fast on the days of Tashreeq except those who could not afford the sacrificial animal" ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Translation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7041_2310_48_2350_22 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_SB_1997 ;
    minaret:startTime 2310.48 .

minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7041_0012_2384_98_SB_1998 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 2515.58 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "Ibn Umar said: During the Farewell Hajj, Rasulullah performed Umrah and Hajj and drove a hady... Whoever has driven the sacrificial animal should not finish their Ihram till he completes his Hajj, and whoever has not should do Tawaf, Sa'ee, cut hair, and finish Ihram" ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Translation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7041_2384_98_2515_58 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_SB_1998 ;
    minaret:startTime 2384.98 .

minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7041_0013_2798_42_SB_1521 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 2808.18 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "Whoever performs Hajj to this House and does not commit any obscenity nor any sin will come out as sinless as a newborn child" ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Translation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7041_2798_42_2808_18 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_SB_1521 ;
    minaret:startTime 2798.42 .

minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7041_0014_2964_78_SB_1773 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 2974.6 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "The reward of Hajj Mabroor is nothing except Jannah" ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Translation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7041_2964_78_2974_6 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_SB_1773 ;
    minaret:startTime 2964.78 .

minaret:HadithOccurrence_HAJJLT22-7041_0015_3107_58_JT_1956 a minaret:HadithOccurrence ;
    minaret:endTime 3136.06 ;
    minaret:evidenceText "Your smile for your brother is charity, commanding good and forbidding evil is charity, giving directions to a person who is lost is charity, guiding a man with bad sight is charity, and removing a stone, thorn, or bone from the path is charity" ;
    minaret:hasUsageType minaret:Translation ;
    minaret:occursIn minaret:SegmentGroup_HAJJLT22-7041_3107_58_3136_06 ;
    minaret:refersTo minaret:Hadith_JT_1956 ;
    minaret:startTime 3107.58 .

