    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0012 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 11 ;
    minaret:startTime 120.06 ;
    minaret:text "وَمِنْ سَیِّئٰتِ اَعْمَالِنَا، مَنْ یَّهْدِهِ اللّٰهُ فَلَا مُضِلَّ لَهٗ، وَمَنْ یُّضْلِلْهُ فَلَا هَادِیَ لَهٗ، وَاَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَّاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِیْكَ لَهٗ،" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0014 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 161.98 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0015 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 14 ;
    minaret:startTime 152.02 ;
    minaret:text "Insha'Allah let's begin our session. Today's session will be more like an orientation day. The name of the course is 'Hajj: Journey of a Lifetime' because it is, SubhanAllah, a very" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0015 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 171.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0016 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 15 ;
    minaret:startTime 161.98 ;
    minaret:text "beautiful journey, and it is a journey of a lifetime for some, and Alhamdulillah some people are able to go over and over again. May Allah accept everyone's efforts and may Allah accept" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0016 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 181.66 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0017 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 16 ;
    minaret:startTime 171.64 ;
    minaret:text "everyone's wishes and desires to go for Hajj as well, Ameen. Because not everyone is able to go, but Alhamdulillah we all, being believers, we wish to go there, right? But SubhanAllah," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0017 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 192.7 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0018 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 17 ;
    minaret:startTime 181.66 ;
    minaret:text "someone was mentioning something very powerful: that there are three types of people when it comes to Hajj. There are three types of people when it comes to Hajj: one type, they can afford and they also want to go;" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0018 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 203.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0019 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 18 ;
    minaret:startTime 193.56 ;
    minaret:text "second type, they cannot afford, but they still want to go; third type, they can afford, but they don't go, they delay it, they" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0019 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 213.38 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0020 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 19 ;
    minaret:startTime 203.44 ;
    minaret:text "don't really, really want to go, SubhanAllah. So may Allah save us from becoming from the third category, Ameen. So Alhamdulillah for this opportunity that we are able to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0020 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 223.04 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0021 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 20 ;
    minaret:startTime 213.38 ;
    minaret:text "go, and Alhamdulillah after two years Hajj has opened up—not fully, but Alhamdulillah it has opened up for many people, Alhamdulillah. So you can say" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0021 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 233.06 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0022 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 21 ;
    minaret:startTime 223.04 ;
    minaret:text "slightly a door has opened. Alhamdulillah there is hope that Insha'Allah in coming years it's going to be back to normal or even Insha'Allah better for everyone. So Alhamdulillah when we" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0022 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 241.48 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0023 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 22 ;
    minaret:startTime 233.06 ;
    minaret:text "have got this opportunity, when we know that Hajj is open, that Insha'Allah we should increase in our du'as so that we can actually get there." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0023 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 247.68 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0024 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 23 ;
    minaret:startTime 242.04000000000002 ;
    minaret:text "And whenever Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala gives us the opportunity, we should just avail it right away before it's too late." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0024 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 258.56 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0025 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 24 ;
    minaret:startTime 248.39999999999998 ;
    minaret:text "So let's begin by praising Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala that we are still alive. Let's praise Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala that we are Muslims. Let's praise Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala that Alhamdulillah He enabled" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0025 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 271.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0026 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 25 ;
    minaret:startTime 258.56 ;
    minaret:text "us to join this session, because Insha'Allah when we learn about Hajj, the goal is that we love Hajj more, and when we are going to yearn for Hajj more, Insha'Allah the du'as are going to come from our hearts, right?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0026 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 282.18 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0027 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 26 ;
    minaret:startTime 272.21999999999997 ;
    minaret:text "All right, so let's praise Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala: اَللّٰهُمَّ لَكَ الْحَمْدُ حَتّٰی تَرْضٰی، وَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ اِذَا رَضِیْتَ، وَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ بَعْدَ الرِّضٰی. O Allah, for You is praise" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0027 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 291.8 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0028 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 27 ;
    minaret:startTime 282.18 ;
    minaret:text "until You're pleased with our praise, and for You is praise when You are pleased, and for You is praise after You're pleased. اَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ كَثِیْرًا." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0028 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 301.82 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0029 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 28 ;
    minaret:startTime 291.8 ;
    minaret:text "اَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ عَدَدَ مَا خَلَقَ. And Alhamdulillah we are going to begin with this beautiful du'a because this is such a beautiful du'a and very powerful du'a which talks about" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0029 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 307.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0030 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 29 ;
    minaret:startTime 301.82 ;
    minaret:text "four important things. We're asking Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala for four things in this du'a: بَرَكَات (barakat)," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0031 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 328.98 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0032 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 31 ;
    minaret:startTime 319.86 ;
    minaret:text "From Your blessings, Your mercy, Your favors, and Your sustenance. Ameen. May Allah accept this du'a for all of us. Isn't it a beautiful du'a?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0032 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 339.14 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0033 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 32 ;
    minaret:startTime 329.24 ;
    minaret:text "It covers pretty much everything, SubhanAllah. So Insha'Allah with this we are going to Insha'Allah hope that Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala blesses us and also blesses us in our knowledge about" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0033 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 350.18 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0034 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 33 ;
    minaret:startTime 339.14 ;
    minaret:text "Hajj, Ameen. So the question is: why do you want to learn about Hajj? Like why this year? Why in 2022? Why do you want to learn about Hajj?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0034 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 360.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0035 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 34 ;
    minaret:startTime 350.54 ;
    minaret:text "Very good, Sister Afreen. Sister Afreen is saying to perform the Hajj persona—beautiful. Anything else? Why do you want to learn about Hajj?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0035 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 372.92 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0036 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 35 ;
    minaret:startTime 360.8 ;
    minaret:text "So it becomes accepted. May Allah accept it from all the people who actually go and perform it, Ameen. To learn the right way so Allah accepts her Hajj—very good, Alhamdulillah. Any other reason?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0036 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 383.9 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0037 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 36 ;
    minaret:startTime 373.5 ;
    minaret:text "For Hajj Mabroor, yes. To perform it like the Prophet Sallallahu Alayhi wa Sallam. For the acceptance. To know the importance in the right way—perfect." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0037 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 395.84 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0038 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 37 ;
    minaret:startTime 385.78 ;
    minaret:text "Alhamdulillah. To know the wisdom behind this ibadah, so we can follow the way of Rasulullah Sallallahu Alayhi wa Sallam, so our effort and time is not wasted. Beautiful, well done." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0038 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 406.16 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0039 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 38 ;
    minaret:startTime 395.84 ;
    minaret:text "Masha'Allah, all of you have really good ideas about why to go for Hajj. No one said that we want to be called Hajis; no one said that because, you know, everyone in my family they've" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0039 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 415.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0040 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 39 ;
    minaret:startTime 406.16 ;
    minaret:text "already been there, it was only me who was left. Alhamdulillah, that's good. So it seems like Alhamdulillah we are on the right page. Insha'Allah we're going to kind of tweak our intention a bit more Insha'Allah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0063 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 660.66 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0064 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 63 ;
    minaret:startTime 650.74 ;
    minaret:text "Insha'Allah in this course we will learn about different steps of Hajj, how to perform them, and also what are the rewards of each step, SubhanAllah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0064 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 670.66 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0065 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 64 ;
    minaret:startTime 660.66 ;
    minaret:text "So that is going to help us when we perform Hajj to enjoy Hajj, because a lot of times people take it as a burden, people take it as a chore or just a to-do list" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0065 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 680.5 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0066 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 65 ;
    minaret:startTime 670.66 ;
    minaret:text "item on their list when they're doing Hajj. But we want to do better, Insha'Allah. We don't want to do, you know, all the rituals of Hajj, all the rites of Hajj, just as" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0066 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 690.48 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0067 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 66 ;
    minaret:startTime 680.5 ;
    minaret:text "chores; we actually want to enjoy each and every step, and we will enjoy once we have knowledge about it, Insha'Allah. So we will know about every step of Hajj, and we will" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0067 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 700.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0068 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 67 ;
    minaret:startTime 690.48 ;
    minaret:text "try to perform it according to the Sunnah, Insha'Allah. We'll also learn about the do's and don'ts of Hajj, and then Insha'Allah we will prepare for Hajj before we go there. Even if" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0068 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 710.66 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0069 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 68 ;
    minaret:startTime 700.44 ;
    minaret:text "you're not going this year, we can still start preparing for it, because the more we are prepared, the better it is for us; the more we know, the more we will be able to, Insha'Allah," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0069 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 720.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0070 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 69 ;
    minaret:startTime 710.66 ;
    minaret:text "have confidence when we're performing our Hajj. And people won't be able to confuse us, because a lot of times when you end up there with no knowledge or little knowledge, a lot of people are there to confuse" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0070 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 730.6 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0071 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 70 ;
    minaret:startTime 720.76 ;
    minaret:text "you because there are so many opinions, there's so many people, there's so many different backgrounds, and they just share whatever they have heard. A lot of times they also don't have knowledge," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0071 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 738.22 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0072 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 71 ;
    minaret:startTime 730.6 ;
    minaret:text "and then they baffle you easily when you don't know enough. So Insha'Allah in this course you're going to know, so that we are not baffled," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0072 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 748.82 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0073 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 72 ;
    minaret:startTime 738.86 ;
    minaret:text "Insha'Allah. And it is the promise of Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala that He will give us Jannah for Hajj Mabroor, and Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala's promises are" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0073 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 756.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0074 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 73 ;
    minaret:startTime 748.82 ;
    minaret:text "true. So Insha'Allah keep this in mind when you're going, and Insha'Allah you will come back sin-free as a newborn." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0074 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 766.3 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0075 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 74 ;
    minaret:startTime 757.22 ;
    minaret:text "You will be just like a newborn baby with no sins on your record, SubhanAllah. So that is our biggest motivation when we go for Hajj, Alhamdulillah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0075 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 777.2 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0076 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 75 ;
    minaret:startTime 767.38 ;
    minaret:text "Hajj is an important part of our deen, so we should prepare for it spiritually and heartily, wholeheartedly Insha'Allah, right? So we should prepare our body," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0076 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 787.12 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0077 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 76 ;
    minaret:startTime 777.2 ;
    minaret:text "we should prepare our finances, we should prepare our soul, we should prepare our intellect, we should prepare our heart, and Insha'Allah go well prepared for" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0077 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 797.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0078 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 77 ;
    minaret:startTime 787.12 ;
    minaret:text "Hajj, Insha'Allah. So now we are going to look at some of the tips given by Sister Shazia Nawaz: that how to prepare for Hajj. So there are eleven in total. So I hope" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0078 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 810.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0079 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 78 ;
    minaret:startTime 797.02 ;
    minaret:text "you have received your workbook from your course portal. So Insha'Allah download the workbook and Insha'Allah start jotting down all the points. If you don't have the workbook because you're not part of the course, it's okay, you can write down on a piece of paper." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0079 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 822.68 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0080 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 79 ;
    minaret:startTime 811.36 ;
    minaret:text "All right, ready everyone? How many points were there again? Eleven in total. So let's just begin. Beautiful! First one: make du'a for ikhlas," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0080 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 833.6 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0081 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 80 ;
    minaret:startTime 823.48 ;
    minaret:text "right? We have talked about that we should keep a check on our intention: it should be sincere, it should be khalis. Now we need to make du'a for it as well, because" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0081 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 843.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0082 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 81 ;
    minaret:startTime 833.6 ;
    minaret:text "our efforts are not enough; our efforts cannot take us anywhere. We always need Allah's help. So Insha'Allah first thing, ask Allah for help: make" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0082 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 851.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0083 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 82 ;
    minaret:startTime 843.58 ;
    minaret:text "du'a for ikhlas. There are so many du'as for ikhlas; Insha'Allah we're going to cover another one tomorrow, but today we're going to look at this beautiful one, because this talks about" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0083 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 862.18 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0084 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 83 ;
    minaret:startTime 852.2200000000001 ;
    minaret:text "our goal as well as we have learned about it earlier: only for Allah, right? So our goal is that we want to see Allah. So what is this beautiful du'a?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0085 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 881.0 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0086 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 85 ;
    minaret:startTime 871.02 ;
    minaret:text "What does that mean? 'O Allah, indeed I ask You for the sweetness of looking upon Your Face and a longing to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0086 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 888.42 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0087 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 86 ;
    minaret:startTime 881.0 ;
    minaret:text "meet You, in a manner that does not entail a calamity that will bring about harm or a trial that will cause deviation.'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0087 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 901.74 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0088 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 87 ;
    minaret:startTime 889.08 ;
    minaret:text "Insha'Allah Sister Shazia Nawaz is going to explain this du'a to us towards the end of the session, Insha'Allah. So if you have any questions, you can keep those questions till the end. Point number two: in order to prepare for" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0088 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 910.38 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0089 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 88 ;
    minaret:startTime 902.6800000000001 ;
    minaret:text "Hajj, we should start observing our fara'id—mandatory prayers—and nawafil" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0089 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 921.0 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0090 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 89 ;
    minaret:startTime 911.1600000000001 ;
    minaret:text "properly. So not just observe them, but also observe them on time, follow all the prerequisites, and do everything properly. Start off with" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0090 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 930.88 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0091 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 90 ;
    minaret:startTime 921.0 ;
    minaret:text "proper wudu, Insha'Allah, and get in the mode of prayers. And SubhanAllah a lot of us, we do pray, but Insha'Allah now we need to move it up a" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0091 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 941.16 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0092 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 91 ;
    minaret:startTime 930.88 ;
    minaret:text "notch, we need to make it better. Especially when we are going for Hajj, we are going to a very beautiful place, we are going to visit sacred masajid: we" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0092 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 951.14 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0093 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 92 ;
    minaret:startTime 941.16 ;
    minaret:text "will be in Makkah, we will be in Madinah, Masjid al-Haram, Masjid an-Nabawi. So Insha'Allah we should try our best to pray beautifully and on time. A" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0093 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 961.24 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0094 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 93 ;
    minaret:startTime 951.14 ;
    minaret:text "lot of times it has been seen that people, they actually reach there, but whatever happens, sometimes they get sick or sometimes, you know, they don't have enough motivation to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0094 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 972.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0095 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 94 ;
    minaret:startTime 961.24 ;
    minaret:text "go to the masjid to pray. That's something which is very sad, because we know about the rewards, right? The reward of praying in Masjid al-Haram is like praying 100,000 prayers elsewhere," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0095 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 983.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0096 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 95 ;
    minaret:startTime 973.36 ;
    minaret:text "and the reward of praying in Masjid an-Nabawi is like praying 1,000 prayers elsewhere, SubhanAllah. The reward is that massive, so we" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0096 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 993.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0097 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 96 ;
    minaret:startTime 983.44 ;
    minaret:text "should not just take it lightly and not go to the masjid and thinking, 'We are still in the sacred bounds in our hotel room, so we'll still pray here.' If there's a genuine" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0097 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1003.56 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0098 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 97 ;
    minaret:startTime 993.54 ;
    minaret:text "problem, that's a different story. But if you're able to walk, if you're able to, you know, go down to the masjid, please do that; don't be lazy about it." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0098 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1012.16 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0099 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 98 ;
    minaret:startTime 1003.56 ;
    minaret:text "And Insha'Allah for that we should start making du'as right away: that may Allah grant us the ability to pray all five prayers in the sacred masajid when we are there," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0099 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1023.16 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0100 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 99 ;
    minaret:startTime 1013.12 ;
    minaret:text "whenever we are there, all five prayers in the masajid. Because what's the point of going there and still not getting all that reward which we can easily avail," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0100 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1033.06 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0101 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 100 ;
    minaret:startTime 1023.16 ;
    minaret:text "Insha'Allah? So make a plan for it and make du'as for it. And another tip which will help you is that Insha'Allah when you are going to be there," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0101 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1043.16 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0102 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 101 ;
    minaret:startTime 1033.06 ;
    minaret:text "whenever Insha'Allah, let's make du'a that we get there soon. So if you're not going for Hajj this year, you can Insha'Allah plan for an Umrah trip, all right Insha'Allah. So whenever you get there," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0102 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1054.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0103 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 102 ;
    minaret:startTime 1043.6399999999999 ;
    minaret:text "then Insha'Allah this is our goal: that we're going to pray all five prayers in the masjid. So the tip is that when you're going to go to the masjid from your hotel room, you're going to wear your abaya and hijab, isn't it?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0103 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1061.28 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0104 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 103 ;
    minaret:startTime 1054.46 ;
    minaret:text "Or if you're brothers, you're gonna dress up accordingly. So how about, if you're going for Hajj and Umrah," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0104 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1071.28 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0105 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 104 ;
    minaret:startTime 1061.28 ;
    minaret:text "before you go there, like if you're going for Hajj this year, this is the time to Insha'Allah start preparing for it: so wear your abaya and hijab before salah anyways so that you" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0105 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1081.8 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0106 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 105 ;
    minaret:startTime 1071.28 ;
    minaret:text "get in the mode of it, so that you know that: okay, I'll have to do it five times a day when I'm there, or even more, because sometimes you'll just go for tawaf, sometimes you will just go for tahajjud, sometimes you" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0106 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1090.2 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0107 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 106 ;
    minaret:startTime 1081.8 ;
    minaret:text "will just go for prayers, just like that Insha'Allah. So get in that mode, that before you pray, you actually prepare yourself." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0107 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1098.48 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0108 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 107 ;
    minaret:startTime 1090.2 ;
    minaret:text "So this way when you reach there, it won't be some extra task for you; you will already be kind of in routine for that." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0108 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1109.6 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0109 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 108 ;
    minaret:startTime 1099.46 ;
    minaret:text "And point number three is: get in the habit of reciting the Qur'an after every prayer. Why after every prayer? Because Insha'Allah in masajid there you will have a lot of time: you won't have to worry about" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0109 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1119.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0110 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 109 ;
    minaret:startTime 1109.6 ;
    minaret:text "cooking food, you won't have to worry about serving anyone, you won't have to worry about work. So Alhamdulillah all the time you will have is for worship, so what is better" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0110 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1129.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0111 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 110 ;
    minaret:startTime 1119.62 ;
    minaret:text "than reciting the Qur'an, right? Alhamdulillah. So when you are done with your tawaf, when you're done with your nawafil, what are you going to do? Instead of sitting and chitchatting, Insha'Allah open" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0111 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1139.66 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0112 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 111 ;
    minaret:startTime 1129.58 ;
    minaret:text "your Mushaf and start praying. It's a good idea to have your own Mushaf Insha'Allah, even though in both masajid or in any masjid you go there, you will find Insha'Allah a" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0112 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1149.56 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0113 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 112 ;
    minaret:startTime 1139.66 ;
    minaret:text "lot of Mushafs there; you can find the copies of the Qur'an there, you can easily grab them and recite. But if you have your own, then Insha'Allah you won't have to run around looking for them," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0113 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1161.08 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0114 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 113 ;
    minaret:startTime 1149.56 ;
    minaret:text "and you won't have to find the place where you stopped before, because you will have some type of bookmark Insha'Allah. So all of this will help you. So why recite a lot of Qur'an?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0114 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1171.98 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0115 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 114 ;
    minaret:startTime 1161.76 ;
    minaret:text "Because Insha'Allah for every letter you're getting ten rewards, and there's so many other benefits—you know all about them. If you are memorizing the Qur'an, then Alhamdulillah that's another beautiful opportunity" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0115 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1181.96 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0116 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 115 ;
    minaret:startTime 1171.98 ;
    minaret:text "for you there, that you can just start reviewing it, and then Insha'Allah whatever you review you can Insha'Allah recite that in your salah in order to strengthen your memorization. Point" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0134 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1386.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0135 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 134 ;
    minaret:startTime 1373.58 ;
    minaret:text "question: do they give you food there? Yes, if you go with Hajj groups they arrange food for you, otherwise there are so many restaurants, people can order their own food as well whatever they like, and Allah knows best." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0154 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1566.74 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0155 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 154 ;
    minaret:startTime 1554.54 ;
    minaret:text "Hajj mode. Start living the Hajj before you get there. Start imagining yourself there. Start planning your days there. And you will be able to plan your days when you know what to do on what day, isn't it?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0155 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1576.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0156 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 155 ;
    minaret:startTime 1567.26 ;
    minaret:text "Otherwise how would you know what to do? It's not going to be a normal day when Hajj days begin, it'd be a total different routine. But how will you schedule yourself beforehand?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0156 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1586.26 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0157 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 156 ;
    minaret:startTime 1577.42 ;
    minaret:text "You will only be able to do it once you know what happens on which day. And why should we just get in the Hajj mode now? Because we know that" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0158 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1617.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0159 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 158 ;
    minaret:startTime 1602.58 ;
    minaret:text "three months are the Hajj months: Shawwal, Dhu al-Qa'dah, and Dhu al-Hijjah. So if anyone wants to go for Hajj, they can leave in Shawwal and it counts, SubhanAllah, right? And they can also get in the mode of Ihram in Shawwal, that also counts for them." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0159 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1627.42 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0160 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 159 ;
    minaret:startTime 1618.44 ;
    minaret:text "And when we are going for Hajj, what are we supposed to do? We should start packing, isn't it? So what do you think is the most important thing to pack, anyone?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0160 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1638.6 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0161 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 160 ;
    minaret:startTime 1628.6000000000001 ;
    minaret:text "What should you pack first? Okay, interesting. You have attended some of the sessions already with us, Alhamdulillah. Yes, the first two" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0180 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1807.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0181 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 180 ;
    minaret:startTime 1806.74 ;
    minaret:text "'My" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0182 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1831.04 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0183 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 182 ;
    minaret:startTime 1821.26 ;
    minaret:text "any new home, any new move, any new city, any new country. But Insha'Allah if you're going for Hajj and Umrah, then make this du'a there for that" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0183 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1840.08 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0184 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 183 ;
    minaret:startTime 1831.04 ;
    minaret:text "beautiful place as well, that may Allah make it mubarak for you. It's already mubarak, Alhamdulillah, sacred lands are mubarak, but may Allah make them mubarak for you as well." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0184 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1846.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0185 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 184 ;
    minaret:startTime 1840.08 ;
    minaret:text "Ameen, and for all of us, Ameen. Point number eight: so you got all of the points" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0185 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1859.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0186 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 185 ;
    minaret:startTime 1846.36 ;
    minaret:text "down so far, 1 to 7? Yes, Alhamdulillah. Okay, if anyone can type them here, that'd be really nice. Okay, let's move on to point number eight: write your will before going on Hajj, your" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0210 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2126.6 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0211 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 210 ;
    minaret:startTime 2116.5600000000004 ;
    minaret:text "May Allah accept our Hajj, because that's very important. A scholar once mentioned: 'Hajj is either accepted or rejected; there's no third thing.' It's not that you get" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0211 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2136.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0212 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 211 ;
    minaret:startTime 2126.6 ;
    minaret:text "a 50% grade or 50% reward for a Hajj: it's either accepted or totally rejected. Can you believe that? It's that" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0212 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2146.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0213 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 212 ;
    minaret:startTime 2136.72 ;
    minaret:text "big of a deal. So we need to be very cautious about it. Point number 10: we need to prepare our hearts, our tongues, our eyes, our ears, and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0213 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2152.08 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0214 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 213 ;
    minaret:startTime 2146.78 ;
    minaret:text "all the organs to fulfill the conditions of Hajj. There are many ways to do it: one is, of" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0214 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2155.04 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0215 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 214 ;
    minaret:startTime 2152.08 ;
    minaret:text "course, health-wise: so prepare your heart, tongue, eyes," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0215 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2165.38 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0216 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 215 ;
    minaret:startTime 2155.04 ;
    minaret:text "ears, keep them healthy: start eating healthy, start walking, start doing some extra exercise so that your body is ready to handle" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0216 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2175.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0217 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 216 ;
    minaret:startTime 2165.38 ;
    minaret:text "that. And if you're not used to heat, then please turn off the air cons and try living in heat a bit, because it's going to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0217 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2185.04 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0218 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 217 ;
    minaret:startTime 2175.02 ;
    minaret:text "be really hot this year and Insha'Allah next year as well, because Hajj is during the summer months, you know during this time. Maybe after 10 years or so it's going to be colder," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0218 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2191.96 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0219 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 218 ;
    minaret:startTime 2185.04 ;
    minaret:text "but right now if you want to perform Hajj this year, next year, or the year after, it's still going to be during the summer months. So Insha'Allah we have" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0219 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2215.04 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0220 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 219 ;
    minaret:startTime 2191.96 ;
    minaret:text "to be mindful about that, prepare for that so that it doesn't become a shocking experience for us. So remember that it's going to be hot there, and then of course arrange some things for that: so you can take some spray bottles with you, you can keep yourself hydrated there so that you don't get sick there. So Insha'Allah keep your body ready and have enough resources ready with you, the ones who can help you with heat as well," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0220 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2225.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0221 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 220 ;
    minaret:startTime 2215.04 ;
    minaret:text "and also it will be extra effort on your part when we do perform Hajj. So Insha'Allah we need to be prepared for that. So that was the physical aspect. So what about spiritually?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0221 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2236.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0222 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 221 ;
    minaret:startTime 2225.02 ;
    minaret:text "Prepare your heart spiritually. So your heart should think good things about people, good thoughts about Allah, and should have a well-wishing attitude." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0222 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2245.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0223 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 222 ;
    minaret:startTime 2236.62 ;
    minaret:text "And you know, your heart should be filled with the love of Hajj as well. Then your tongue should utter only good. So if you are in the habit of using bad words, this is the time" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0223 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2261.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0224 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 223 ;
    minaret:startTime 2245.94 ;
    minaret:text "to cut it off, because it will be really hard at Hajj to control your tongue then if you're in the habit of saying bad words. So Insha'Allah work on that. If you are sort of glued to screen for whatever reason, like you're addicted to watch something, then Insha'Allah" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0224 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2271.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0225 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 224 ;
    minaret:startTime 2261.52 ;
    minaret:text "we need to stop watching that; if our ears are used to listening to something which is not halal, then Insha'Allah we need to cut down on that as well. So it is music," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0225 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2281.96 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0226 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 225 ;
    minaret:startTime 2271.54 ;
    minaret:text "and it is also gossip and backbiting and anything which is unnecessary. So Insha'Allah cut down on all of that and Insha'Allah prepare yourself properly" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0226 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2287.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0227 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 226 ;
    minaret:startTime 2281.96 ;
    minaret:text "for Hajj, Insha'Allah. Last point from the preparation points, and that" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0227 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2291.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0228 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 227 ;
    minaret:startTime 2287.72 ;
    minaret:text "is: seek knowledge" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0245 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2492.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0246 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 245 ;
    minaret:startTime 2476.0 ;
    minaret:text "can do for someone Insha'Allah. And Alhamdulillah, Alhamdulillah, we have this precious app, it's called 'Hajj and Umrah', it's by Al-Huda International, it's an amazing app. It's also in English, right? So the screenshot right now you can see is of Urdu, but it's also in English. The best part about this is it's" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0246 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2502.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0247 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 246 ;
    minaret:startTime 2492.78 ;
    minaret:text "very simple: it's no extra text, it's only what to do, what to do, what to do. It's like literally a checklist sort with all the du'as—all the du'as you would need, all" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0247 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2515.04 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0248 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 247 ;
    minaret:startTime 2502.78 ;
    minaret:text "of them are here. So this is usually very handy for anyone who has it. So Insha'Allah first step: if you're going or anyone who's going, please tell them about this app; it's totally free, no ads, Alhamdulillah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0248 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2525.68 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0249 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 248 ;
    minaret:startTime 2515.64 ;
    minaret:text "And it's a good idea to keep a copy of the Qur'an with you, a Mushaf with you, but also it's a good idea to keep a Qur'an app on your phone, because what if you forget to bring" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0249 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2535.66 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0250 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 249 ;
    minaret:startTime 2525.68 ;
    minaret:text "your bag someday, or you know, things were really heavy and then you just had your phone on you? So Insha'Allah it's a good idea to have the Qur'an, because whenever you're waiting for" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0250 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2545.8 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0251 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 250 ;
    minaret:startTime 2535.66 ;
    minaret:text "something—waiting for food, waiting for some lineup to go for Umrah, or waiting for your group for some ziyarah or whatnot—then Insha'Allah just open" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0251 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2559.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0252 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 251 ;
    minaret:startTime 2545.8 ;
    minaret:text "the app and start reciting. That's not the time to chitchat, because it has been seen a lot of people, they waste a lot of their energy and time in talking to people, because when they meet new people they get excited and they want to know their stories. And of" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0252 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2565.96 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0253 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 252 ;
    minaret:startTime 2559.58 ;
    minaret:text "course people have their life stories to tell, and then all your time can go wasted in people's life stories. If you really like them, that's" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0253 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2579.92 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0254 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 253 ;
    minaret:startTime 2565.96 ;
    minaret:text "great: take their numbers, when you come back home you can call them, ask about their life stories. But that's not the time when you're there to learn about their life stories, Insha'Allah. And some people waste a lot of their time observing others," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0254 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2581.86 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0255 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 254 ;
    minaret:startTime 2580.48 ;
    minaret:text "like their only job is to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0255 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2594.82 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0256 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 255 ;
    minaret:startTime 2581.86 ;
    minaret:text "observe others: what are they wearing, what are they eating, oh where did they get this from, where did they buy this from, and all of that, and guessing: this person's from that country, maybe from that country. That is like, SubhanAllah, really" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0256 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2604.66 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0257 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 256 ;
    minaret:startTime 2594.82 ;
    minaret:text "total waste of time: it doesn't help at all. It doesn't help you, it doesn't help that person, it doesn't help anyone around you. So Insha'Allah protect your" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0257 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2617.48 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0258 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 257 ;
    minaret:startTime 2604.66 ;
    minaret:text "eyes and keep your eyes on something which is beneficial. So that's why install some amazing du'a apps on your phone as well. So once you're done your recitation of the Qur'an, you can just open apps. These du'a apps are amazing." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0258 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2626.68 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0259 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 258 ;
    minaret:startTime 2618.96 ;
    minaret:text "You all must know about it, right? Many of you already know about it, you already have it. How many of you don't know about it?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0259 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2640.84 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0260 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 259 ;
    minaret:startTime 2627.42 ;
    minaret:text "You all do know about it, right? So in this amazing app, we have it in book form as well, but also an app. So in the app you can also access it through your phone: so there are du'as of protection there, adhkar after salah" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0260 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2644.96 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0261 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 260 ;
    minaret:startTime 2640.84 ;
    minaret:text "are there, istighfar du'as are there, and also your morning evening adhkar are there, so it's" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0261 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2655.1 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0262 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 261 ;
    minaret:startTime 2644.96 ;
    minaret:text "such a beautiful handy app. And this 'Dua Kijiye' app, even though it's in Urdu, but du'as are in Arabic, so you can just read all the du'as; if you know a little bit of Arabic, you will understand what" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0262 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2664.14 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0263 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 262 ;
    minaret:startTime 2655.1 ;
    minaret:text "you're asking Allah for. And it's a very good collection of du'as; it has pretty much everything you would ever need, SubhanAllah. So maybe one day in Mina you" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0263 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2674.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0264 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 263 ;
    minaret:startTime 2664.14 ;
    minaret:text "can just make all of these du'as. And Qur'anic and Masnoon Du'as app has, you know, pretty much all the Qur'anic du'as and a lot of masnoon du'as, Alhamdulillah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0264 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2684.86 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0265 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 264 ;
    minaret:startTime 2674.62 ;
    minaret:text "There's another du'a app, it's called 'Du'ain'—it's just du'as, right? So every time you open this app, new du'as pop up, SubhanAllah. So it's a very good way to keep yourself" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0265 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2697.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0266 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 265 ;
    minaret:startTime 2684.86 ;
    minaret:text "focused, and you can Insha'Allah keep asking Allah. And you know, du'a is worship, so it's a very easy act of worship I would say. So Insha'Allah whenever you make any du'as, you are in the state of worship." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0266 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2712.7 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0267 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 266 ;
    minaret:startTime 2698.54 ;
    minaret:text "So what's the benefit of beneficial apps? They are going to serve as time-savers for you Insha'Allah, right? You're not going to waste time, because you know you can also make a schedule that: every day I'm going to open all of these apps and read this many du'as Insha'Allah. And it's very" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0267 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2726.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0268 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 267 ;
    minaret:startTime 2712.7 ;
    minaret:text "convenient: you won't have to carry a lot of things with you, and you can just have one phone with all these apps, Insha'Allah. Thank you Sister Shazia, so the link for apps is here, we can also download all of them from here. So Alhamdulillah," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0268 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2736.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0269 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 268 ;
    minaret:startTime 2726.54 ;
    minaret:text "this makes us reach this point when we will talk a bit about Hajj in the light of the Qur'an, and then tomorrow we'll go full-fledged on it and we're going to do" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0323 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3263.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0324 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 323 ;
    minaret:startTime 3251.9 ;
    minaret:text "first: 'Let me enjoy the life first'—that's such a wrong attitude. We should not live life like this: that let me do everything wrong now and then maybe eventually I will go for Hajj and I'll be all sin-free." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0324 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3278.1 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0325 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 324 ;
    minaret:startTime 3264.08 ;
    minaret:text "That's the wrong intention, that's the wrong approach, we should not even think like that. And if a person is not able to go for Hajj, that person can go for Umrah, because according to many ulama Umrah is also mandatory." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0325 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3289.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0326 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 325 ;
    minaret:startTime 3279.32 ;
    minaret:text "If you're able to afford an Umrah, don't wait for Hajj, go for Umrah. And Alhamdulillah, just wanted to take this opportunity and mention our upcoming" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0326 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3299.38 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0327 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 326 ;
    minaret:startTime 3289.46 ;
    minaret:text "Umrah journey with Al-Huda Insha'Allah, Al-Huda US. So Insha'Allah we are going in November, so if anyone wants to go for Umrah with Al-Huda and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0327 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3309.48 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0328 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 327 ;
    minaret:startTime 3299.38 ;
    minaret:text "Darussalam, then Insha'Allah you can contact us and you can visit the site hajj.alhudanline.org and you will see 'Umrah 2022' right there on the website. You" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0328 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3323.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0329 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 328 ;
    minaret:startTime 3309.48 ;
    minaret:text "can Insha'Allah find the details there. And Insha'Allah if you're willing to go for Hajj or Umrah, you can start saying your Labbaik, and Insha'Allah you can make du'as and you can make your intentions pure only for Allah. We ask Allah to grant all of us Hajj" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0329 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3325.3 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0330 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 329 ;
    minaret:startTime 3323.78 ;
    minaret:text "Mabroor." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0330 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3330.16 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0331 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 330 ;
    minaret:startTime 3325.3 ;
    minaret:text "Jazakumullahu Khairan Katheera for paying attention, and Insha'Allah looking forward to see all of you tomorrow in class." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0001 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 30.0 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0002 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 1 ;
    minaret:startTime 14.0 ;
    minaret:text "لَبَّیْكَ اَللّٰهُمَّ لَبَّیْكَ، لَبَّیْكَ لَا شَرِیْكَ لَكَ لَبَّیْكَ، اِنَّ الْحَمْدَ، وَالنِّعْمَةَ لَكَ وَالْمُلْكَ، لَاشَرِیْكَ لَكَ۔" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0002 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 40.12 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0003 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 2 ;
    minaret:startTime 30.0 ;
    minaret:text "اَللّٰهُمَّ لَبَّیْكَ، لَبَّیْكَ لَا شَرِیْكَ لَكَ لَبَّیْكَ، اِنَّ الْحَمْدَ، وَالنِّعْمَةَ لَكَ وَالْمُلْكَ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0003 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 50.2 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0004 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 3 ;
    minaret:startTime 40.12 ;
    minaret:text "لَاشَرِیْكَ لَكَ۔ اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَةُ اللهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهُ. Welcome back, Alhamdulillah, we" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0004 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 59.92 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0005 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 4 ;
    minaret:startTime 50.2 ;
    minaret:text "are going to, Insha'Allah, begin our proper fiqh of Hajj subject from today. Yesterday was our orientation day; I hope you know what we are going to do in this course." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0005 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 69.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0006 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 5 ;
    minaret:startTime 59.92 ;
    minaret:text "So let's just begin, Insha'Allah, properly: اِنَّ الْحَمْدَ لِلّٰهِ، نَحْمَدُهٗ وَنَسْتَعِیْنُهٗ وَنَسْتَغْفِرُهٗ، وَنَعُوْذُ بِاللّٰهِ مِنْ شُرُوْرِ اَنْفُسِنَا" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0006 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 79.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0007 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 6 ;
    minaret:startTime 69.76 ;
    minaret:text "وَمِنْ سَیِّئٰتِ اَعْمَالِنَا، مَنْ یَّهْدِهِ اللّٰهُ فَلَا مُضِلَّ لَهٗ، وَمَنْ یُّضْلِلْهُ فَلَا هَادِیَ لَهٗ، وَاَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَّاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0007 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 90.1 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0008 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 7 ;
    minaret:startTime 79.94 ;
    minaret:text "اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِیْكَ لَهٗ، وَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُهٗ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ۔ اَعُوْذُ بِاللّٰهِ مِنَ الشَّیْطٰنِ الرَّجِیْمِ۔ بِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِیْمِ۔" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0008 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 99.08 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0009 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 8 ;
    minaret:startTime 90.1 ;
    minaret:text "رَبِّ اشْرَحْ لِیْ صَدْرِیْ ۙ وَیَسِّرْ لِیْۤ اَمْرِیْ ۙ وَاحْلُلْ عُقْدَةً مِّنْ لِّسَانِیْ ۙ یَفْقَهُوْا قَوْلِیْ۔ آمِينَ۔" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0009 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 113.18 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0010 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 9 ;
    minaret:startTime 99.08 ;
    minaret:text "for this course, so Insha'Allah..." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0010 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 124.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0011 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 10 ;
    minaret:startTime 113.88 ;
    minaret:text "our goal is that we will learn about Hajj, but not just learn about what is Hajj and what are the rites and rituals of Hajj; we" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0011 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 131.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0012 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 11 ;
    minaret:startTime 124.36 ;
    minaret:text "will also, Insha'Allah, focus on why do we do all of these steps? What's the wisdom behind the steps of Hajj?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0012 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 142.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0013 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 12 ;
    minaret:startTime 131.64 ;
    minaret:text "What are the benefits of these steps? And we'll also learn about the history of these locations, Insha'Allah. So, Muslims, they all love to go for Hajj, isn't it?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0013 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 150.7 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0014 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 13 ;
    minaret:startTime 142.7 ;
    minaret:text "Muslims brought up in believing families kind of know about the basics of our deen including Hajj. We all wish to see the Kaaba," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0014 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 160.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0015 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 14 ;
    minaret:startTime 151.04 ;
    minaret:text "we all wish to go do tawaf. It is a genuine wish of every believing heart to be there. So, the ones who can go, they don't stop;" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0024 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 266.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0025 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 24 ;
    minaret:startTime 256.64 ;
    minaret:text "Such amazing ayat! They talk about many different things, and Insha'Allah we are going to kind of get into a bit of the tafseer of these ayat before we actually, Insha'Allah, get down to the fiqh aspects." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0025 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 276.56 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0026 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 25 ;
    minaret:startTime 266.52 ;
    minaret:text "So, while we are talking about Hajj, Hajj to the House of Allah is a great act of worship which Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala has prescribed for His" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0026 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 286.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0027 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 26 ;
    minaret:startTime 276.56 ;
    minaret:text "servants, for His worshippers. This act of worship is a combination of many religious and worldly benefits. Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala has made it a means of entering" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0027 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 296.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0028 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 27 ;
    minaret:startTime 286.76 ;
    minaret:text "Jannah and forgiveness of our sins and acts of disobedience. Hajj is a journey of faith, and it's a spiritual training—it's a" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0028 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 306.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0029 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 28 ;
    minaret:startTime 296.52 ;
    minaret:text "tarbiyah. It's an opportunity to improve ourselves. In this journey, one gets the true concept of worship of Allah, and the believer is adorned with" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0029 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 316.48 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0030 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 29 ;
    minaret:startTime 306.46 ;
    minaret:text "the high morals of Islam. In this journey, the souls are purified, the heart attains taqwa, and Muslims return with healthy and pure souls. May" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0030 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 326.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0031 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 30 ;
    minaret:startTime 316.48 ;
    minaret:text "Allah make us among those! In this journey, the souls are purified and hearts attain taqwa; may Allah make us among those. Hajj is, in reality, a journey" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0031 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 336.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0032 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 31 ;
    minaret:startTime 326.46 ;
    minaret:text "on the path of Allah, a journey of passion, a journey of love, a journey of devotion. And at the same time, it's a fundamental part" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0032 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 346.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0033 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 32 ;
    minaret:startTime 336.52 ;
    minaret:text "of Islam, it's a pillar of Islam. Hajj is one of the best ways and means of worshipping Allah. It is a collective worship; if we analyze it, it is a combination" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0033 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 360.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0034 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 33 ;
    minaret:startTime 346.58 ;
    minaret:text "of all acts of worship, SubhanAllah, because in it is prayers, in it is charity, and sometimes even fasting is involved in Hajj rituals. Hajj is an act of worship which is physical," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0034 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 370.6 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0035 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 34 ;
    minaret:startTime 360.72 ;
    minaret:text "financial, spiritual, and emotional in nature. Why is it the best type of worship? Because a" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0035 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 380.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0036 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 35 ;
    minaret:startTime 370.6 ;
    minaret:text "Haji spends one's time, one's efforts, one's wealth, and sacrifices his comfort and ease, and then goes and submits to Allah. On the other" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0036 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 390.5 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0037 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 36 ;
    minaret:startTime 380.46 ;
    minaret:text "hand, as soon as we intend to travel for Hajj, the condition of our hearts—it changes, it begins to change." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0037 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 400.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0038 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 37 ;
    minaret:startTime 390.5 ;
    minaret:text "We get excited, and we start craving more for it. One's attention is directed towards Allah; the same thought overwhelms this person" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0038 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 410.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0039 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 38 ;
    minaret:startTime 400.36 ;
    minaret:text "and this person's heart and mind, that soon this journey of passion will begin. All the attention" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0039 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 420.5 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0040 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 39 ;
    minaret:startTime 410.36 ;
    minaret:text "and interest of the one intended to go for Hajj gets focused on this one point. This journey always reminds one of the hereafter; there" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0040 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 430.18 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0041 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 40 ;
    minaret:startTime 420.5 ;
    minaret:text "are many occasions where one really feels the gathering of the hereafter when a person is at Hajj. The reckoning, the hardships—all of these" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0041 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 442.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0042 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 41 ;
    minaret:startTime 430.18 ;
    minaret:text "remind a person of the hereafter, the Day of Resurrection, SubhanAllah. May Allah make us among those who witness these holy lands! May Allah enable us to go there over and over again, Ameen." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0069 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 723.82 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0070 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 69 ;
    minaret:startTime 714.0600000000001 ;
    minaret:text "And when we talk about Baitullah, it was the very, very first house, as we have learned about it before, that angels actually built it at the time of Adam, and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0070 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 734.1 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0071 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 70 ;
    minaret:startTime 723.82 ;
    minaret:text "we learn it from this verse which we have actually listened to the recitation of in the beginning of this session—the verse from Surah Ali Imran. So, let's try to understand" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0071 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 744.4 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0072 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 71 ;
    minaret:startTime 734.1 ;
    minaret:text "this verse a bit so that we can understand about Hajj and its history and its beginning. So, we learn: اِنَّ اَوَّلَ بَیْتٍ—indeed the first house. So," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0072 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 754.28 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0073 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 72 ;
    minaret:startTime 744.4 ;
    minaret:text "Kaaba is called the first house, Baytullah is called the first house, and it is the first place of worship on the face of this earth, and it's the first" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0073 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 766.9 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0074 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 73 ;
    minaret:startTime 754.28 ;
    minaret:text "masjid—so, first masjid where we go do sajda, first place of worship for anyone to worship, and first house built. What's the proof? Sahih Muslim, hadith number 520:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0076 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 799.96 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0077 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 76 ;
    minaret:startTime 790.24 ;
    minaret:text "earth; second masjid: Al-Masjid al-Aqsa. In this verse we learn that Makkah is called Bakkah. So, what's the reason behind it?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0077 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 809.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0078 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 77 ;
    minaret:startTime 799.96 ;
    minaret:text "One understanding is that it's just another name of Makkah. But why is it called Bakkah? What is the meaning? There are two meanings." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0078 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 822.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0079 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 78 ;
    minaret:startTime 809.62 ;
    minaret:text "One is that Bakkah—it bends the necks of the oppressors and tyrants, the arrogant ones, so that they come to Baytullah and they show humility and they weep, SubhanAllah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0079 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 835.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0080 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 79 ;
    minaret:startTime 823.46 ;
    minaret:text "Even the most arrogant ones, they show humility there. Another meaning of Bakkah is that people are often gathered here and it is crowded in Makkah, that's why it's called Bakkah. So, these are the two" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0128 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1370.16 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0129 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 128 ;
    minaret:startTime 1362.86 ;
    minaret:text "One, it's a gathering of all Muslims, so Muslims gather there, they learn from each other," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0129 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1382.74 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0130 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 129 ;
    minaret:startTime 1370.16 ;
    minaret:text "and it becomes a means of guidance for each other. And SubhanAllah, by looking at others you feel that how you don't know much," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0130 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1392.96 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0131 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 130 ;
    minaret:startTime 1383.6200000000001 ;
    minaret:text "and looking at others and their desire, their worship, their efforts, and their zeal and energy to worship Allah, then you're reminded that you're nothing," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0131 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1403.56 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0132 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 131 ;
    minaret:startTime 1393.8600000000001 ;
    minaret:text "SubhanAllah. So when you look at others, you learn from them. So these amazing gatherings, they are beneficial for us—the Umrah gatherings, the Hajj gatherings—" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0132 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1414.24 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0133 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 132 ;
    minaret:startTime 1403.56 ;
    minaret:text "and it's a qibla for all Muslims, so it's a direction we all follow. So that's why it's a guide, it's hudan in that sense as well." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0133 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1424.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0134 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 133 ;
    minaret:startTime 1415.02 ;
    minaret:text "Also more guidance we get when we go for Umrah and Hajj: our iman increases and we also get more guidance." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0134 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1435.38 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0135 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 134 ;
    minaret:startTime 1425.3999999999999 ;
    minaret:text "Sometimes because there are lectures going on there and we benefit from them, but not all the time. It's not always the lectures or the knowledge which is there, which is amazing, Alhamdulillah," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0135 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1449.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0136 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 135 ;
    minaret:startTime 1435.38 ;
    minaret:text "it's not always that. It's just, you know, SubhanAllah this beautiful experience of servitude, spending everything for Allah: your energy, your effort, your time, dedicating your time, dedicating your life, everything, SubhanAllah, and then learning from the people around you." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0136 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1460.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0137 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 136 ;
    minaret:startTime 1450.54 ;
    minaret:text "And then in Makkah there are ayat bayyinat, clear proofs, open proofs for all of us. What are these proofs? We're going to Insha'Allah cover six of them, so please jot them down." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0137 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1468.06 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0138 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 137 ;
    minaret:startTime 1460.62 ;
    minaret:text "First one: the biggest proof is that this amazing house of Allah is built on a very barren land, nothing usually grows there, SubhanAllah. And" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0138 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1481.06 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0139 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 138 ;
    minaret:startTime 1468.06 ;
    minaret:text "Zamzam—Zamzam water is a very big miracle, and when you look at the properties of this water and you do a bit of research, you'll be just mind-blown about it. And then security:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0139 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1491.3 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0140 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 139 ;
    minaret:startTime 1481.62 ;
    minaret:text "security of Makkah is just amazing. Even today people when it's time for salah, they leave their shops open and they go and pray—no one steals their stuff, SubhanAllah!" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0140 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1501.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0141 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 140 ;
    minaret:startTime 1491.96 ;
    minaret:text "It's that beautiful. And the fruits, as we have talked about before: nothing grows there, but you can find every food there," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0141 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1512.32 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0142 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 141 ;
    minaret:startTime 1502.3200000000002 ;
    minaret:text "from grapes to mangoes, from different countries from all over the world. And not just fruits, the fruits from all types, different cuisines, different tastes," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0142 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1522.24 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0143 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 142 ;
    minaret:startTime 1512.32 ;
    minaret:text "and the kind of food people enjoy there, they don't even get to enjoy there wherever they come from; they get to enjoy more food there, SubhanAllah, even though, you know," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0143 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1533.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0144 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 143 ;
    minaret:startTime 1522.24 ;
    minaret:text "a lot of people are there, but they don't run out of food, SubhanAllah! That's the barakah of Makkah. And also the Safa and Marwa—they are big signs, they are clear" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0144 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1542.06 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0145 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 144 ;
    minaret:startTime 1533.9 ;
    minaret:text "proofs, isn't it, SubhanAllah? They're still there. When you see Safa and Marwa there, where you're reminded of the story of Hajar," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0145 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1556.08 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0146 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 145 ;
    minaret:startTime 1542.98 ;
    minaret:text "and then you are amazed at how much she put in effort and how hard it is to run through these two mountains. And you know, now it's very easy to walk through it or run through it, but back in" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0146 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1568.08 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0147 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 146 ;
    minaret:startTime 1556.08 ;
    minaret:text "those days it was just very hard. And the sixth sign is Maqam Ibrahim, where you can still see the footprints of Ibrahim Alayhi Salaam—you can still see them." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0147 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1578.5 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0148 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 147 ;
    minaret:startTime 1568.08 ;
    minaret:text "So, these were just few ayat which we have talked about, few signs which are open clear signs for believers, for people, for the world." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0148 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1592.24 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0149 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 148 ;
    minaret:startTime 1578.5 ;
    minaret:text "Now, there's a very beautiful tarbiyah tip by Dr. Farhat Hashmi: she said that if you ever are struggling with your children's tarbiyah, then what you can do is take your children" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0149 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1605.0 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0150 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 149 ;
    minaret:startTime 1592.24 ;
    minaret:text "to Baitullah, and they will be amazed by all of this. They will, Insha'Allah, feel more connected with their deen, they will get" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0150 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1614.98 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0151 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 150 ;
    minaret:startTime 1605.0 ;
    minaret:text "more guidance, they will see all of these amazing sha'air from their own eyes, all of these amazing sights. All of the history will come alive in front" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0151 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1625.9 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0152 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 151 ;
    minaret:startTime 1614.98 ;
    minaret:text "of them, all the stories you have been telling them, you know, they will experience them. But not once in a while—take them as many times as you can, because every time we go there, we learn so much from that, SubhanAllah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0152 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1635.22 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0153 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 152 ;
    minaret:startTime 1630.22 ;
    minaret:text "So, after this part of the ayah which mentions the clear proofs," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0153 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1645.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0154 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 153 ;
    minaret:startTime 1635.94 ;
    minaret:text "Maqam Ibrahim is mentioned specifically. Why is it mentioned specifically? Because that's a big sign, because we have learned from the Qur'an that Ibrahim and Ismail" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0154 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1655.1 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0155 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 154 ;
    minaret:startTime 1645.54 ;
    minaret:text "they built the Kaaba, right? And then we see the footsteps, you know, you can literally see them, SubhanAllah. So, it is a very" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0155 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1667.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0156 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 155 ;
    minaret:startTime 1655.1 ;
    minaret:text "enlightening moment, it's like you can actually feel that yes, Ibrahim was there and he built it. All of this gives you a lot of iman boost. And what" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0156 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1684.08 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0157 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 156 ;
    minaret:startTime 1667.94 ;
    minaret:text "is the virtue of Maqam Ibrahim? Let's see: Rasulullah Sallallahu Alayhi wa Sallam said: 'Black stone and Maqam Ibrahim are rubies of Jannah, they are yaqut of Jannah. If children of Adam" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0157 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1694.14 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0158 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 157 ;
    minaret:startTime 1684.08 ;
    minaret:text "wouldn't have touched it with sins, it would have illuminated whatever is between east and the west, and not any disabled and sick would touch it except would be cured,' SubhanAllah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0158 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1702.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0159 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 158 ;
    minaret:startTime 1694.14 ;
    minaret:text "So, this is the virtue of Maqam Ibrahim and also Black Stone. And we also have learned that Maqam Ibrahim is mentioned" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0160 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1724.16 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0161 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 160 ;
    minaret:startTime 1714.42 ;
    minaret:text "every tawaf, we pray behind Maqam Ibrahim to fulfill this. And whoever enters Makkah: وَمَنْ دَخَلَهٗ كَانَ اٰمِنًا ؕ Whoever" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0161 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1734.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0162 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 161 ;
    minaret:startTime 1724.16 ;
    minaret:text "enters Makkah is safe—safe from what? Safe from all evils, SubhanAllah, because Makkah is a cradle of peace and security," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0162 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1744.68 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0163 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 162 ;
    minaret:startTime 1734.36 ;
    minaret:text "peace and security, and you feel it, SubhanAllah. And Ibrahim actually made this du'a: وَاِذْ قَالَ اِبْرٰهٖمُ رَبِّ اجْعَلْ هٰذَا بَلَدًا اٰمِنًا. When" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0164 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1764.6 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0165 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 164 ;
    minaret:startTime 1754.46 ;
    minaret:text "concern was that we don't do shirk; he wanted safety not for worldly reasons, he wanted safety for worship reasons," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0165 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1772.56 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0166 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 165 ;
    minaret:startTime 1764.6 ;
    minaret:text "and Allah knows best. And we also learn about two other qualities of Baytullah from Surah Al-Baqarah, that it is called" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0166 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1783.3 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0167 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 166 ;
    minaret:startTime 1772.56 ;
    minaret:text "مَثَابَةً and أَمْنًا. Masaba is a place where people return, and that's why, SubhanAllah, people keep returning." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0167 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1791.3 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0168 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 167 ;
    minaret:startTime 1783.3 ;
    minaret:text "Anytime we go there, we just want to come back again. It's very hard to leave those sacred lands, it's very hard to leave" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0168 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1801.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0169 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 168 ;
    minaret:startTime 1791.3 ;
    minaret:text "Kaaba; people who go there, they want to keep going back, SubhanAllah. Masaba: a place of return, SubhanAllah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0169 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1813.04 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0170 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 169 ;
    minaret:startTime 1801.36 ;
    minaret:text "And Amna is security. How is Makkah a place of safety and security? We're going to cover six points, but I really want all of you to jot down only the four" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0170 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1822.18 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0171 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 170 ;
    minaret:startTime 1813.04 ;
    minaret:text "points first—the first four points only at this point, because we are going to touch the other points if you get a chance in this course. First point:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0171 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1837.4 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0172 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 171 ;
    minaret:startTime 1822.78 ;
    minaret:text "sacred place till Qiyamah. Makkah is going to stay sacred till Qiyamah; we need to remember that it's a sanctuary till the Day of Resurrection. Rasulullah, he said that on the day of conquest of Makkah:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0172 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1849.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0173 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 172 ;
    minaret:startTime 1837.4 ;
    minaret:text "'There is no migration now, there is no hijra now, but there is jihad and good intentions. And when you are called for jihad, you should come out at once.' Rasulullah also" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0173 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1860.42 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0174 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 173 ;
    minaret:startTime 1850.4399999999998 ;
    minaret:text "said on the day of conquest of Makkah: 'Allah has made this town, this Makkah, a sanctuary since the day He created the heavens and the" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0174 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1870.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0175 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 174 ;
    minaret:startTime 1860.42 ;
    minaret:text "earth. So, it is a sanctuary by Allah's decree till the Day of Resurrection,' SubhanAllah. So, since beginning till end, it is a sacred and safe" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0175 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1877.8 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0176 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 175 ;
    minaret:startTime 1870.52 ;
    minaret:text "place; it is a safe zone not only for people, but also for animals and plants. And you're going to love this hadith, Insha'Allah:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0176 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1888.48 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0177 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 176 ;
    minaret:startTime 1878.5 ;
    minaret:text "Narrated Ibn Abbas: 'On the day of the conquest of Makkah, Rasulullah said: Allah has made this town a sanctuary;" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0177 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1896.0 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0178 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 177 ;
    minaret:startTime 1888.48 ;
    minaret:text "its thorny bushes should not be cut, its game should not be chased'—like you're not supposed to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0178 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1907.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0179 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 178 ;
    minaret:startTime 1896.7 ;
    minaret:text "hunt there—'and its fallen things should not be picked up except by the one who would announce it publicly,' right? So, if you see anything dropped, you're not supposed to pick it" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0179 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1917.48 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0180 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 179 ;
    minaret:startTime 1907.44 ;
    minaret:text "up unless you're able to get this back to the owner or you know how to get it to the authorities so that they can get that item back to the person" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0180 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1926.98 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0181 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 180 ;
    minaret:startTime 1918.06 ;
    minaret:text "who owns it or who dropped it. And then third point: anyone leaving for the House of Allah" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0181 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1937.16 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0182 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 181 ;
    minaret:startTime 1926.98 ;
    minaret:text "is in Allah's protection. That's another beautiful point, SubhanAllah. So, we learn from a narration: 'Three are under Allah's guarantee:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0182 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1945.82 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0183 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 182 ;
    minaret:startTime 1937.16 ;
    minaret:text "a man who goes to the masjid from the masajid of Allah, and the soldier who leaves in the way of Allah, and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0183 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1956.7 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0184 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 183 ;
    minaret:startTime 1945.82 ;
    minaret:text "a person who leaves for Hajj.' When we leave for Hajj, we are under Allah's guarantee, like He is going to take care of us, SubhanAllah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0184 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1966.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0185 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 184 ;
    minaret:startTime 1956.7 ;
    minaret:text "First, SubhanAllah. And then fourth point: safety from Dajjal's fitna. We all are scared about Dajjal, isn't it? So, SubhanAllah Makkah is safe" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0185 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1981.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0186 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 185 ;
    minaret:startTime 1966.62 ;
    minaret:text "from Dajjal, Masjid al-Haram is safe from Dajjal. So, let's look at the narration now: Rasulullah said: 'There will be no town which Dajjal will not enter except Makkah and Medina, and there will" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0186 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1996.66 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0187 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 186 ;
    minaret:startTime 1981.02 ;
    minaret:text "be no entrance road of both Makkah and Medina but the angels will be standing in rows guarding it against him.' And then Medina will shake with its inhabitants thrice," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0187 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2007.22 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0188 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 187 ;
    minaret:startTime 1996.66 ;
    minaret:text "earthquakes will come, and Allah will expel all the disbelievers and the Munafiqeen from it. So, only the pure people will stay in Medina, SubhanAllah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0188 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2018.2 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0189 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 188 ;
    minaret:startTime 2007.22 ;
    minaret:text "So, they will not run away and they will stay safe from Dajjal. So, let's move on to the next part of this ayah where we learned that we are supposed to do Hajj for Allah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0222 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2366.5 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0223 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 222 ;
    minaret:startTime 2360.32 ;
    minaret:text "Now, let's just do some definitions. We have covered them yesterday as well briefly, but Insha'Allah today we're going to touch base" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0223 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2382.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0224 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 223 ;
    minaret:startTime 2366.5 ;
    minaret:text "those same definitions, so please jot them down if you can. So, the definition of Hajj or the meaning of Hajj linguistically is: to intend to go to a respectable thing again and again." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0224 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2397.84 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0225 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 224 ;
    minaret:startTime 2382.9 ;
    minaret:text "Hajj is the masdar of Hajj, and this is what it means: to intend to go to a respectable thing again and again. And in Sharia, in terminology, the" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0225 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2409.22 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0226 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 225 ;
    minaret:startTime 2397.84 ;
    minaret:text "definition of Hajj is: the act of performing the prescribed acts of worship by attending certain places on the days" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0226 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2430.38 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0227 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 226 ;
    minaret:startTime 2409.22 ;
    minaret:text "prescribed by the Sharia. Insha'Allah we're going to learn about the days, we're going to learn about the places, and we also are going to learn about the acts; but for now, just know the definition: the act of performing the prescribed acts of worship by attending certain places, by visiting certain places on the days prescribed by the Sharia." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0227 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2439.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0228 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 227 ;
    minaret:startTime 2431.42 ;
    minaret:text "And the one who performs Hajj is called 'Hajj' in Arabic." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0228 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2449.88 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0229 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 228 ;
    minaret:startTime 2439.66 ;
    minaret:text "In Urdu, in other languages, you must have heard the term 'Hajji', right? But it's Hajj in Arabic. Hajj is fine too, depends which language you're using to speak." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0229 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2462.68 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0230 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 229 ;
    minaret:startTime 2449.88 ;
    minaret:text "And what's the plural of Hajj? There are two plurals: one is Hujjaj and one is Hajeej, both mean the ones who are performing Hajj." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0230 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2473.2 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0231 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 230 ;
    minaret:startTime 2462.68 ;
    minaret:text "And Hajj was obligated in 9th Hijri, and Abu Bakr, he was sent as the" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0231 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2483.68 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0232 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 231 ;
    minaret:startTime 2473.2 ;
    minaret:text "lead for the first Hajj group after it became mandatory, right? So, Hajj was obligated in 9th Hijri, and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0232 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2493.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0233 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 232 ;
    minaret:startTime 2483.68 ;
    minaret:text "Muslims did perform Hajj that year, and Abu Bakr, he was leading them, SubhanAllah. Rasulullah, he did not go this" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0233 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2503.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0234 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 233 ;
    minaret:startTime 2493.78 ;
    minaret:text "year, and we're going to learn about the reason in a bit. And when Muslims reached there and they performed Hajj, it was announced in the 9th Hijri that no one will" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0234 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2513.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0235 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 234 ;
    minaret:startTime 2503.64 ;
    minaret:text "perform Hajj naked after this day, no one will perform Hajj without clothes because this is what Mushrikeen would do, and no Mushrikeen will perform Hajj next year after" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0235 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2523.4 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0236 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 235 ;
    minaret:startTime 2513.72 ;
    minaret:text "this. And Rasulullah, he performed his first and last Hajj in 10th Hijri, and it was a shirk-free" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0236 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2539.88 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0237 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 236 ;
    minaret:startTime 2523.4 ;
    minaret:text "Hajj. Why? Because there were no idols there anymore near Kaaba—if you remember the history, Mushrikeen had placed a lot of idols around Kaaba," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0237 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2549.6 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0238 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 237 ;
    minaret:startTime 2539.88 ;
    minaret:text "so they were removed. And also Mushrikeen were not allowed to come for Hajj this year. So, it was a shirk-free Hajj, and no sinful" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0238 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2559.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0239 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 238 ;
    minaret:startTime 2549.6 ;
    minaret:text "actions were involved in this Hajj. Rasulullah taught people Hajj with his actions and his words, and we call this Hajj 'Hajjat al-Wada'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0239 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2569.82 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0240 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 239 ;
    minaret:startTime 2559.72 ;
    minaret:text "—the farewell Hajj, the only Hajj, Hajjat al-Wada'. And you must have heard about the khutbah which is very famous—the sermon of Hajjat al-Wada'—which" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0240 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2576.06 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0241 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 240 ;
    minaret:startTime 2569.82 ;
    minaret:text "is quoted over and over again because it has beautiful teachings for all of us, Insha'Allah if time permits we can also go over it." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0241 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2596.08 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0242 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 241 ;
    minaret:startTime 2576.06 ;
    minaret:text "Let's just talk about a few things we have already covered yesterday. I'm just going to quickly go over them, just jot down the title parts, right? Just know the main headings, Insha'Allah. Hajj is an obligation, and it's a very important obligation," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0242 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2606.12 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0243 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 242 ;
    minaret:startTime 2596.08 ;
    minaret:text "it's a command of Allah, and also Rasulullah Sallallahu Alayhi wa Sallam, he emphasized it. And if a person wants to perform more Hajj," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0243 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2618.26 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0244 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 243 ;
    minaret:startTime 2606.12 ;
    minaret:text "they can, and Insha'Allah we will cover that narration in a bit as well. And don't delay Hajj if Allah has given you enough, and if you fulfill all three conditions of istita'ah," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0244 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2626.6 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0245 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 244 ;
    minaret:startTime 2618.26 ;
    minaret:text "then Insha'Allah go and don't delay it for petty reasons or for worldly reasons. And once Hajj becomes an obligation, do it before anything else." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0245 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2634.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0246 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 245 ;
    minaret:startTime 2626.6 ;
    minaret:text "And Hajj does not get waived—this is something we haven't discussed yesterday, so let's talk about that. A man said, 'My" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0246 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2647.1 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0247 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 246 ;
    minaret:startTime 2634.64 ;
    minaret:text "father has died, and he did not perform Hajj; shall I perform Hajj on his behalf?' Rasulullah Sallallahu Alayhi wa Sallam said: 'Don't you think that if your father owed a debt," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0247 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2657.08 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0248 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 247 ;
    minaret:startTime 2647.1 ;
    minaret:text "you would pay off?' The man said, 'Yes.' He said, 'That debt owed to Allah is more deserving of being paid off,'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0248 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2666.88 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0249 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 248 ;
    minaret:startTime 2657.08 ;
    minaret:text "SubhanAllah, right? So, if a person dies, his salah is not supposed to be prayed by anyone, but his Hajj or her Hajj is supposed to be performed by the heirs," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0249 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2676.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0250 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 249 ;
    minaret:startTime 2666.88 ;
    minaret:text "just like fasting is, right? Fasting doesn't just get waived for the previous years; if a person has missed some fast, these fasts are to be made up by the heirs," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0250 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2686.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0251 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 250 ;
    minaret:startTime 2676.72 ;
    minaret:text "by the family. So, Insha'Allah something to remember. So, it's better that we perform our mandatory Hajj before we die so that it doesn't become a burden for the people after us." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0251 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2697.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0252 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 251 ;
    minaret:startTime 2686.54 ;
    minaret:text "And Hajj is a very important pillar of our deen. Let's talk about the importance of Hajj. First of all, why is it important? Because it's a command of Allah," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0252 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2710.8 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0253 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 252 ;
    minaret:startTime 2697.94 ;
    minaret:text "that's why it's important. It is called the rope of Islam, strong bond of Islam—that's why it's important. Let's look at this beautiful narration about rope of Islam or strong bond of Islam:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0253 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2719.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0254 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 253 ;
    minaret:startTime 2710.8 ;
    minaret:text "Sahaba mentioned that we were sitting with Rasulullah, so one of them mentioned that we were sitting with Rasulullah and he asked:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0254 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2730.5 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0255 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 254 ;
    minaret:startTime 2719.36 ;
    minaret:text "'Which bond of Islam is the strongest?' Sahaba said, 'The salah.' He said, 'Good.' 'And what next?' They said, 'Zakah.' He said, 'Good.' 'And what next?'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0255 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2745.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0256 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 255 ;
    minaret:startTime 2730.5 ;
    minaret:text "They said, 'Fast of Ramadan.' He said, 'Good.' 'And what next?' And they said, 'Hajj.' He said, 'Good.' And this narration goes on, but SubhanAllah it shows the basic pillars of Islam right here." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0256 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2751.7 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0257 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 256 ;
    minaret:startTime 2745.02 ;
    minaret:text "And Hajj and Umrah, they are the identity of a Muslim. No one else goes for Hajj and Umrah, right," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0257 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2761.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0258 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 257 ;
    minaret:startTime 2751.7 ;
    minaret:text "that you won't be confused if someone tells you that, 'I went for Hajj,' you won't be like, 'Maybe this person is a Muslim or not?' You won't be, because only Muslims do that," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0258 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2771.66 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0259 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 258 ;
    minaret:startTime 2761.64 ;
    minaret:text "SubhanAllah. Even Umar narrates from his father Umar and from Rasulullah about the question of Jibreel which he asked about Islam," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0259 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2791.68 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0260 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 259 ;
    minaret:startTime 2771.66 ;
    minaret:text "so Rasulullah responded to that question with this answer: 'Islam is that you bear witness that there is no god except Allah and Muhammad is the messenger of Allah Sallallahu Alayhi wa Sallam, and that you establish prayer, you pay zakah, you perform Hajj," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0260 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2801.66 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0261 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 260 ;
    minaret:startTime 2791.68 ;
    minaret:text "you perform Umrah, and perform ghusl of janabah, and perform complete wudu, and fast in Ramadan.' Jibreel asked, 'Do I become a Muslim when I do that?'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0261 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2809.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0262 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 261 ;
    minaret:startTime 2801.66 ;
    minaret:text "Rasulullah said, 'Yes,' SubhanAllah. So, all of these are the signs of a believer, all of these are the things Muslims do." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0262 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2824.16 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0263 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 262 ;
    minaret:startTime 2809.44 ;
    minaret:text "And Hajj is exclusively for Muslims, especially after the Hajj of 9th Hijri, so starting from 10th Hijri only Muslims performed Hajj, SubhanAllah. And Sahaba would include Hajj in major good deeds." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0263 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2835.14 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0264 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 263 ;
    minaret:startTime 2824.16 ;
    minaret:text "Let's look at this narration about Abu Huraira: he quoted Rasulullah saying: 'When the Muslim slave performs the due of Allah and the due of his master," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0264 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2845.2 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0265 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 264 ;
    minaret:startTime 2835.14 ;
    minaret:text "he will have two rewards,' right? So, double reward for a Muslim who is not free. Abu Huraira said: 'By the One in Whose hand my soul is in," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0265 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2855.34 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0266 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 265 ;
    minaret:startTime 2845.2 ;
    minaret:text "if jihad for the sake of Allah, Hajj, and kindness to my mother had not come in the way, I would have liked death to come to me while I was a slave.'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0266 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2865.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0267 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 266 ;
    minaret:startTime 2855.34 ;
    minaret:text "Why? Because he wanted double ajr. But because he knew that Hajj and kindness to the mother and striving in the way of Allah is more rewardable," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0267 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2875.22 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0268 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 267 ;
    minaret:startTime 2865.36 ;
    minaret:text "so he was okay with this, SubhanAllah. Another narration to show Sahabah's love for Hajj and the kind of importance they would give to Hajj:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0268 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2885.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0269 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 268 ;
    minaret:startTime 2875.22 ;
    minaret:text "we learn about Abu Musa al-Ashari that a man asked him, 'O Abu Musa, I used to perform Hajj, that is, I used to perform when I was like younger or stronger," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0269 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2895.16 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0270 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 269 ;
    minaret:startTime 2885.02 ;
    minaret:text "but now I'm weak and old, is there any action that is equal to Hajj? Like what else should I do? Like I cannot really do Hajj because I'm weak and old, what do I do?'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0270 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2907.0 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0271 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 270 ;
    minaret:startTime 2895.16 ;
    minaret:text "Abu Musa said: 'Do you have the power to free 70 believing slaves from the children of Ismail, and do you know of anything which is like going for Hajj, camping there and leaving from there?'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0271 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2931.08 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0272 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 271 ;
    minaret:startTime 2907.0 ;
    minaret:text "And then he said, 'I can't find any action like it,' SubhanAllah. There's nothing like Hajj, we cannot say, 'Okay, if you can't do Hajj you do this,' SubhanAllah. This was the answer of Abu Musa al-Ashari Radiyallahu Anhu, and Allah knows best. And not only just Sahaba, but also our salaf as-salihin," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0272 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2941.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0273 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 272 ;
    minaret:startTime 2931.7000000000003 ;
    minaret:text "they also would give Hajj a lot of importance and they would perform a lot of Hajj as well. Let's look at this narration about Ta'us: Ta'us was asked, 'Nafl Hajj" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0273 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2955.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0274 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 273 ;
    minaret:startTime 2941.54 ;
    minaret:text "after the fard Hajj, is it better or charity is better? Like what should I do? Should I go for Hajj or give charity?' And SubhanAllah, such a valid question, because even today people ask this, isn't it?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0274 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2966.18 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0275 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 274 ;
    minaret:startTime 2956.12 ;
    minaret:text "So, he responded: 'Where is the place to go and camp in Makkah? Where is the place to stay up late at night? Where is the place where you can go around the House of Allah?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0275 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2976.26 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0276 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 275 ;
    minaret:startTime 2966.18 ;
    minaret:text "Where is the place you can pray in it? Where is the place where you can stand on Arafat, gather and throw stones?' What does it mean by all of this?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0276 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2987.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0277 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 276 ;
    minaret:startTime 2976.26 ;
    minaret:text "He was questioning him to make him think that there's nothing like that. Where else can you perform all of these acts of worship? Where else can you do tawaf? Where else can you find Arafat? Where else can you actually stone jamarat?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0277 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2997.92 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0278 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 277 ;
    minaret:startTime 2987.72 ;
    minaret:text "You can't, right? No matter where you try to do tawaf, it doesn't count; no matter which part of the earth you're going to go throw stones at someone or something," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0278 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3007.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0279 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 278 ;
    minaret:startTime 2997.92 ;
    minaret:text "it's not going to be counted as worship, SubhanAllah. So, you cannot ignore or think that there is something else you can do instead of Hajj and it's still better." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0279 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3017.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0280 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 279 ;
    minaret:startTime 3007.78 ;
    minaret:text "So, Hajj is a very heavy good deed, SubhanAllah. May Allah enable all of us to go there over and over again! So, about Ta'us—the same person who gave this answer, right," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0280 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3027.48 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0281 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 280 ;
    minaret:startTime 3017.72 ;
    minaret:text "pay attention—about the same person, when he passed away, Ibn Shozab said: 'I attended the funeral of Ta'us in Makkah in 106 after Hijri." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0281 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3037.5 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0282 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 281 ;
    minaret:startTime 3027.48 ;
    minaret:text "I heard people saying, 'O Abdurrahman'—that's the name of Ta'us—'O Abdurrahman, may Allah have mercy on you, you have performed 40 Hajj,' SubhanAllah!" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0282 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3047.7 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0283 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 282 ;
    minaret:startTime 3037.5 ;
    minaret:text "The one who said this, he actually did it. So, this is however our salaf were: if he said there's nothing better than Hajj, he actually was performing a lot of Hajj," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0283 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3055.22 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0284 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 283 ;
    minaret:startTime 3047.7 ;
    minaret:text "and that's what he believed in, and that's what he did, SubhanAllah. So, the words and actions, they match, and this is how" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0284 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3062.66 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0285 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 284 ;
    minaret:startTime 3055.78 ;
    minaret:text "we should be, Insha'Allah. May Allah make us among those who are truthful in their actions and also on their tongue!" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0285 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3073.84 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0286 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 285 ;
    minaret:startTime 3063.8 ;
    minaret:text "And let's talk about some virtues, but before we get there, just wanted to share a few facts about how many Hajj people would perform back then. If Allah gives us the opportunity," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0286 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3083.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0287 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 286 ;
    minaret:startTime 3073.84 ;
    minaret:text "we should also avail any opportunity, Insha'Allah, which comes our way. So, we learn that not only Ta'us performed 40 Hajj, but there were some Sahaba" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0287 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3093.7 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0288 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 287 ;
    minaret:startTime 3083.78 ;
    minaret:text "they performed more than 60 Hajj, and there were some Tabi'in and Taba Tabi'in, they performed more than 40 Hajj, SubhanAllah. And Ibn Masood" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0288 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3103.88 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0289 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 288 ;
    minaret:startTime 3093.7 ;
    minaret:text "he was heard saying: 'There are two acts of worship in which I wish that everyone gets a share, like everyone gets to experience" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0289 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3113.88 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0290 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 289 ;
    minaret:startTime 3103.88 ;
    minaret:text "two things: and one was to travel for Hajj, second was to do Umrah,' SubhanAllah. This was his wish, that everyone should experience that and everyone should, Insha'Allah, have a share in it" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0290 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3124.34 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0291 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 290 ;
    minaret:startTime 3113.88 ;
    minaret:text "because it's very rewardable and it's very spiritual journey, and you change and you become better, SubhanAllah. Let's talk about the virtues of Hajj quickly." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0003 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 43.92 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0004 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 3 ;
    minaret:startTime 32.12 ;
    minaret:text "And may Allah enable us to perform all of these rites beautifully whenever we get a chance to do so, Ameen. So Insha'Allah today, we'll have a look at the verses about Hajj in Surah Al-Hajj." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0004 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 50.18 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0005 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 4 ;
    minaret:startTime 44.28 ;
    minaret:text "Then we will go over the commands and matters mentioned in these ayat. So let's listen to the ayat first." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0010 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 75.86 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0011 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 10 ;
    minaret:startTime 74.06 ;
    minaret:text "Ameen, Ameen." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0016 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 91.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0017 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 16 ;
    minaret:startTime 89.94000000000001 ;
    minaret:text "Ameen, Ameen." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0024 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 136.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0025 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 24 ;
    minaret:startTime 135.54 ;
    minaret:text "Ameen." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0028 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 152.24 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0029 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 28 ;
    minaret:startTime 149.96 ;
    minaret:text "Ameen, Ameen." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0034 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 181.08 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0035 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 34 ;
    minaret:startTime 175.74 ;
    minaret:text "Ameen, Ameen, Ameen, Ameen, Ameen, Ameen." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0042 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 261.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0043 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 42 ;
    minaret:startTime 252.76 ;
    minaret:text "So let's understand what these verses are actually telling us about. So if you look at the background of these verses, it's gonna, Insha'Allah, make it easier for us to understand." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0043 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 271.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0044 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 43 ;
    minaret:startTime 262.0 ;
    minaret:text "So in these verses, Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala is rebuking the mushrikeen of Makkah. Why? Because they prevented Muslims from entering Baytullah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0044 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 283.42 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0045 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 44 ;
    minaret:startTime 271.78 ;
    minaret:text "Ibrahim Alayhi Salam built this house, and he was commanded to keep the House of Allah clean and pure for the people who wanted to offer prayers in it, and this invitation was open for everyone." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0045 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 292.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0046 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 45 ;
    minaret:startTime 283.6 ;
    minaret:text "So that's why they are reprimanded. So people are welcome to come to Hajj so that they may get some religious benefits and also some worldly benefits." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0046 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 303.32 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0047 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 46 ;
    minaret:startTime 292.84 ;
    minaret:text "So if we just look at the overall picture of these verses, we learn that Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala says: 'O Ibrahim, explain to the people that Hajj is an obligation upon them.'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0047 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 313.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0048 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 47 ;
    minaret:startTime 303.48 ;
    minaret:text "They will respond to your inspiration in spite of their various circumstances, and they will come on foot and also on rides, SubhanAllah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0048 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 324.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0049 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 48 ;
    minaret:startTime 313.96 ;
    minaret:text "And even if their rides are lean and weak, they will still come. These rides will come from every remote area so that pilgrims will be present from, you know, different places." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0049 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 337.4 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0050 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 49 ;
    minaret:startTime 325.02 ;
    minaret:text "For what? For their religious and worldly benefits. And also, they will mention the name of Allah. When they will reach there, they will mention the name of Allah, not just as dhikr, but also on the animals: camels, cows, and goats." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0050 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 345.42 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0051 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 50 ;
    minaret:startTime 337.7 ;
    minaret:text "Why would they mention the name of Allah on all of these animals? To slaughter them. And when will they do this? In the 10 days of Dhul-Hijjah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0051 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 352.84 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0052 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 51 ;
    minaret:startTime 345.94 ;
    minaret:text "And then we also learn that it's allowed for the people who are slaughtering these animals to even enjoy the meat of that." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0052 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 361.38 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0053 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 52 ;
    minaret:startTime 353.04 ;
    minaret:text "So eat from these slaughtered animals yourself and also feed the needy and also the ones who are very poor, the ones who are starving." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0053 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 368.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0054 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 53 ;
    minaret:startTime 362.02 ;
    minaret:text "Then the pilgrims should complete the remaining rulings of Hajj, and then they can just exit Ihram or leave Ihram." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0054 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 379.26 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0055 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 54 ;
    minaret:startTime 369.6 ;
    minaret:text "And then they can cut their nails, they can shave their hair, and they can fulfill whatever is left from their obligations. If they have made any vows, they should complete them." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0055 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 387.8 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0056 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 55 ;
    minaret:startTime 379.66 ;
    minaret:text "And they can just do their final tawaf, and they are, SubhanAllah, done. So if you think about it, this was the summary of all these verses." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0056 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 401.3 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0057 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 56 ;
    minaret:startTime 388.24 ;
    minaret:text "So it kind of covers the Hajj from the beginning till end, SubhanAllah. So what is our goal? Our goal, Insha'Allah, is to have a look at what Allah has mentioned about Hajj in the Qur'an first." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0057 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 415.48 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0058 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 57 ;
    minaret:startTime 402.32 ;
    minaret:text "Right? Sunnah explains Hajj beautifully and scholars categorize it amazingly. But first we will have a look at these verses so that we know what Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala tells us, that Insha'Allah we are going to build on it." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0058 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 421.5 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0059 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 58 ;
    minaret:startTime 415.6 ;
    minaret:text "We are going to add, Insha'Allah, other sources as well in order to enrich ourselves in this beautiful subject." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0059 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 434.18 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0060 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 59 ;
    minaret:startTime 422.36 ;
    minaret:text "And SubhanAllah what we learn is from these ayat that Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala, He picked, He assigned the land for Ibrahim. وَاِذْ بَوَّأْنَا—the word bawwana means we assigned." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0060 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 444.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0061 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 60 ;
    minaret:startTime 434.52 ;
    minaret:text "So Allah picked the land for Ibrahim to build upon it. And something cool is that the foundations of the Kaaba, they were already there. Foundations of the Kaaba were already there." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0061 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 455.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0062 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 61 ;
    minaret:startTime 444.94 ;
    minaret:text "He just built upon that. And this place in Makkah was picked by Allah, and this House of Allah had already been there before that." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0062 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 466.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0063 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 62 ;
    minaret:startTime 455.84 ;
    minaret:text "Because it was the first house of Allah on the earth. And it is clear that Adam Alayhi Salam and even other prophets, they used to worship there along with their families and the righteous ones." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0063 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 478.34 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0064 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 63 ;
    minaret:startTime 467.38 ;
    minaret:text "And it was long before Ibrahim Alayhi Salam. So foundations were there on a hill at the time of Ibrahim Alayhi Salam, on which Ibrahim Alayhi Salam and his son Ismail Alayhi Salam, they built the Kaaba." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0064 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 491.42 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0065 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 64 ;
    minaret:startTime 478.72 ;
    minaret:text "So this is what we know about it. And then Insha'Allah there is a very beautiful narration which kind of hints towards that. So let's have a look: Rasulullah Sallallahu Alayhi wa Sallam said: 'May Allah bestow mercy on Ismail's mother.'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0071 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 572.0 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0072 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 71 ;
    minaret:startTime 561.48 ;
    minaret:text "So from this narration from Sahih al-Bukhari, what do we know? The foundations were already there. So the Kaaba was built far before Ibrahim Alayhi Salam as well. That's a fact to remember." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0072 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 581.86 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0073 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 72 ;
    minaret:startTime 572.24 ;
    minaret:text "And it's at a height and at a hilltop. How do we know that today? Like is there any proof? Yes. If you think about the door of the Kaaba, it's at a height, isn't it?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0073 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 592.84 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0074 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 73 ;
    minaret:startTime 582.1 ;
    minaret:text "People need some stairs in order to get in the Kaaba. So if anyone wants to go in the Kaaba, they have to climb some stairs to enter. This shows that Kaaba is on a hill." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0074 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 605.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0075 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 74 ;
    minaret:startTime 593.48 ;
    minaret:text "And why was Kaaba built? The purpose behind building the Kaaba: the first one is to lay the foundations of pure tawheed, oneness of Allah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0090 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 773.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0091 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 90 ;
    minaret:startTime 762.62 ;
    minaret:text "That's the ibadah we cannot do at home; you can pray at home, you can pray at any part of this world, but when it comes to tawaf, you can only do it there. And SubhanAllah, another beautiful point about" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0091 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 779.84 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0092 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 91 ;
    minaret:startTime 774.28 ;
    minaret:text "tawaf is, there is a narration Rasulullah mentioned that" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0093 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 800.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0094 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 93 ;
    minaret:startTime 790.64 ;
    minaret:text "the rulings are pretty much the same. So we should, Insha'Allah, respect tawaf, and we should consider it as an act of worship, and we should not use that opportunity while we are" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0094 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 810.48 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0095 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 94 ;
    minaret:startTime 800.58 ;
    minaret:text "doing tawaf to Facebook Live, people! It has been seen that people actually when they go there, they forget about their ibadah, they're so amazed by Kaaba that they forget about that they're" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0095 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 820.56 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0096 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 95 ;
    minaret:startTime 810.48 ;
    minaret:text "actually doing an act of worship: they start taking selfies or they start, you know, doing tawaf with their video call on with their family and friends. That kind of goes against the" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0096 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 830.18 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0097 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 96 ;
    minaret:startTime 820.56 ;
    minaret:text "respect of Kaaba, that also goes against the act of worship, because when you're praying, can you take your selfies? When you're praying, can you Facebook Live there?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0097 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 840.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0098 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 97 ;
    minaret:startTime 830.7 ;
    minaret:text "You don't, right, SubhanAllah? So Insha'Allah we need to remember those points for tawaf. If you really, really, really want to take a picture after you're done your acts of worship, you can" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0098 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 846.5 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0099 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 98 ;
    minaret:startTime 840.72 ;
    minaret:text "also take a picture of Kaaba—no problem, Insha'Allah, and Allah knows best. And also" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0099 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 856.84 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0100 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 99 ;
    minaret:startTime 847.0600000000001 ;
    minaret:text "make this house pure and clean for the people who pray, because you know prayers in Masjid al-Haram, as we have learned earlier, prayers in" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0100 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 866.9 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0101 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 100 ;
    minaret:startTime 856.84 ;
    minaret:text "Masjid al-Haram, they're also very rewardable, and people, they love to pray there. So Insha'Allah if it's clean, it's easier for them to pray. And Alhamdulillah Alhamdulillah Masjid is very clean" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0101 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 876.8 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0102 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 101 ;
    minaret:startTime 866.9 ;
    minaret:text "and it's cleaner than before after COVID because of the, you know, Alhamdulillah extreme efforts to keep everyone healthy and safe, and Alhamdulillah for that." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0102 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 886.88 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0103 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 102 ;
    minaret:startTime 876.8 ;
    minaret:text "So Insha'Allah whenever we go, whenever we get a chance to go to Makkah, we will make sure that we will do a lot of tawafs, because tawafs cannot be done elsewhere, and Insha'Allah" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0103 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 896.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0104 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 103 ;
    minaret:startTime 886.88 ;
    minaret:text "we should pray every prayer in the masjid so that we can secure all of these rewards. And SubhanAllah the Kaaba was built for one" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0104 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 906.86 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0105 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 104 ;
    minaret:startTime 896.76 ;
    minaret:text "purpose—what was that? Pure tawheed, right? To establish pure tawheed. It's not for any political reason. So Insha'Allah we need to remember that we should not turn Kaaba into" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0105 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 916.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0106 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 105 ;
    minaret:startTime 906.86 ;
    minaret:text "anything or this journey into anything which is of some lesser reason than tawheed, Insha'Allah. And we also learn from another verse of the Qur'an" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0106 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 927.8 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0107 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 106 ;
    minaret:startTime 916.72 ;
    minaret:text "that Ibrahim and Ismail were given the command to purify the Kaaba for another four set of categories. So three of them are same," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0107 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 938.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0108 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 107 ;
    minaret:startTime 928.52 ;
    minaret:text "but وَالْعٰكِفِیْنَ is added. Who are these people who do i'tikaf? I'tikaf—do you know what kind of ibadah is this? Anyone has ever done i'tikaf?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0108 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 946.32 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0109 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 108 ;
    minaret:startTime 938.58 ;
    minaret:text "So i'tikaf is one of the confirmed Sunnah of Prophet Muhammad, and he used to do it regularly." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0109 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 952.42 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0110 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 109 ;
    minaret:startTime 947.0400000000001 ;
    minaret:text "And SubhanAllah he would dedicate ten days of his Ramadan to spend in the masjid." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0110 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 963.08 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0111 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 110 ;
    minaret:startTime 953.0 ;
    minaret:text "He would sleep there, he would stay there, he would worship there, he would spend all his time there. So i'tikaf is something which is beautiful. So Insha'Allah whenever you get a chance, do that." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0111 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 973.95 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0112 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 111 ;
    minaret:startTime 963.08 ;
    minaret:text "And that's why it has been seen that Alhamdulillah every Ramadan a lot of people, they go to Baytullah and they do i'tikaf there in Makkah. So also" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0112 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 983.97 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0113 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 112 ;
    minaret:startTime 973.95 ;
    minaret:text "purify the House of Allah for the people who are going to do i'tikaf there. So all of these categories of people doing all of these amazing acts of worship, they are also very" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0142 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1270.25 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0143 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 142 ;
    minaret:startTime 1260.31 ;
    minaret:text "So ضَامِرٍ is referring to camels because back in the day camels were used as rides, but even today if you think about it, a lot of people they use rides to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0143 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1280.47 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0144 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 143 ;
    minaret:startTime 1270.25 ;
    minaret:text "reach Makkah and some people even walk. So what does it mean by walking? Walking could be that some people, they live in Makkah, they can just walk to Kaaba, to Baytullah," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0144 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1290.83 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0145 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 144 ;
    minaret:startTime 1281.01 ;
    minaret:text "and some people, they take rides. So there are some different opinions about this: some scholars say because rijalan is mentioned first, so" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0145 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1300.85 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0146 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 145 ;
    minaret:startTime 1290.83 ;
    minaret:text "walking is preferred; others say not necessarily, because Rasulullah, he did his Hajj on a ride, he came on a" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0146 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1310.97 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0147 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 146 ;
    minaret:startTime 1300.85 ;
    minaret:text "ride, so that's Sunnah, so that's more rewardable. And Allah knows best, both opinions are there, whatever is easy, Insha'Allah we can do that. So if we can walk" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0147 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1320.91 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0148 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 147 ;
    minaret:startTime 1310.97 ;
    minaret:text "to Kaaba—amazing; if we cannot, then we can also ride there, you know, we can take a plane first, then maybe a car, a taxi, or a bus" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0148 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1330.95 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0149 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 148 ;
    minaret:startTime 1320.91 ;
    minaret:text "or a train. So Insha'Allah rides are fine. And also for the rituals, right? You know, sometimes it's very hard for people to do all the rituals on foot because of their age" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0149 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1343.23 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0150 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 149 ;
    minaret:startTime 1330.95 ;
    minaret:text "or health, they can also do it on wheelchair—no problem, it's allowed. And they can also use those carts they have—that is also allowed, and Allah knows best." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0157 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1422.37 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0158 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 157 ;
    minaret:startTime 1412.29 ;
    minaret:text "And whatever we use in the way of Allah, that is also sacred, that is also rewardable. Like if we are going to use our ride to do tawaf, if we are going to use our" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0158 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1432.25 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0159 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 158 ;
    minaret:startTime 1422.37 ;
    minaret:text "ride to reach Makkah, then Insha'Allah whatever money, whatever ride, whatever is in the way of Allah, it's something which is going to be rewardable for" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0159 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1442.09 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0160 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 159 ;
    minaret:startTime 1432.25 ;
    minaret:text "us, you know, it will become a good deed on our scales. What's the proof for that? The proof is from this famous hadith to do with three types of horses. So Rasulullah" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0165 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1497.75 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0166 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 165 ;
    minaret:startTime 1492.01 ;
    minaret:text "watering it, SubhanAllah. So what do we learn from this? So if you're using our car, and if" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0166 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1506.93 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0167 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 166 ;
    minaret:startTime 1497.75 ;
    minaret:text "the fuel goes in, that fuel is also going to be weighed on the Day of Judgment. So even if it's not for Hajj, in the way of Allah—like going to the masjid, going to different halaqat to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0167 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1527.99 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0168 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 167 ;
    minaret:startTime 1506.93 ;
    minaret:text "learn, going to attend Jumu'ah khutbah. A lot of times people, you know, they complain that now because the gas prices are so high, I rather stay home, but SubhanAllah, all of this will be counted towards your good deeds. Whatever you are going to put in your car, whatever services you do of your car, all of this will be good deeds for you, so Insha'Allah be happily" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0168 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1538.07 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0169 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 168 ;
    minaret:startTime 1527.99 ;
    minaret:text "and willingly use yourself and your ride in the way of Allah. And after this call, what will happen? People will come to you, O Ibrahim," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0169 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1544.77 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0170 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 169 ;
    minaret:startTime 1538.07 ;
    minaret:text "from where? مِنْ كُلِّ فَجٍّ عَمِيقٍ—from every deep valley. What does that mean by every deep valley?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0170 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1547.17 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0171 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 170 ;
    minaret:startTime 1544.77 ;
    minaret:text "الْفَجُّ is" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0171 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1554.41 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0172 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 171 ;
    minaret:startTime 1547.17 ;
    minaret:text "the cleft between two hills, a cleft between two hills, or you can say a passage between two hills. And 'ameeq' word" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0172 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1557.75 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0173 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 172 ;
    minaret:startTime 1554.41 ;
    minaret:text "referring to the paths leading to Baytullah. And 'ameeq' word" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0173 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1562.77 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0174 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 173 ;
    minaret:startTime 1557.75 ;
    minaret:text "means, you know, from far away or from deep places." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0174 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1578.19 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0175 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 174 ;
    minaret:startTime 1563.41 ;
    minaret:text "From far away or from deep places. So people will come from different far-off lands, and SubhanAllah this is something which was not known at that time, even at the time of Rasulullah—Muslims were not all over the place yet," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0175 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1589.11 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0176 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 175 ;
    minaret:startTime 1578.81 ;
    minaret:text "SubhanAllah! So what do we learn? That it's sort of like a prophecy, right? That it's something which is now very obvious: people from" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0176 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1599.13 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0177 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 176 ;
    minaret:startTime 1589.11 ;
    minaret:text "all over the world come to Baytullah, SubhanAllah. And if you look at the image of it, you know, different valleys, people are coming, and you know the way they're walking towards the Kaaba," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0177 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1605.03 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0178 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 177 ;
    minaret:startTime 1599.13 ;
    minaret:text "it's just mind-blowing, it's just beautiful, SubhanAllah. So it's happening what Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala said, it's happening now." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0178 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1615.87 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0179 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 178 ;
    minaret:startTime 1605.57 ;
    minaret:text "And when people will come, what will happen? They will witness a lot of benefits, they will experience a lot of benefits. What are some of the benefits? So let's look at four of them:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0179 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1627.97 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0180 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 179 ;
    minaret:startTime 1615.87 ;
    minaret:text "they will see unity of Muslim Ummah, right? Even if we don't understand each other there, everyone is united in doing everything, and that's something which is so beautiful, isn't it? Just think about it: one Allahu Akbar," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0180 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1639.21 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0181 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 180 ;
    minaret:startTime 1629.01 ;
    minaret:text "and everyone assembles themselves in beautiful rows, and another Allahu Akbar, everyone bends down—even though they don't understand each" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0181 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1651.15 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0182 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 181 ;
    minaret:startTime 1639.21 ;
    minaret:text "other's languages, even though they don't understand what's going on around them, SubhanAllah, many times—but they follow these instructions beautifully, and it shows a beautiful picture of Muslim Ummah, SubhanAllah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0182 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1661.97 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0183 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 182 ;
    minaret:startTime 1652.11 ;
    minaret:text "And opportunities to earn halal are many there, SubhanAllah—we have talked about business opportunities the other day as well—and people, they increase in their" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0183 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1672.27 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0184 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 183 ;
    minaret:startTime 1661.97 ;
    minaret:text "knowledge because they learn from each other, they also learn from the scholars, and there are a lot of halaqat going on there when you are there. And also the Jumu'ah khutbah is usually very amazing, and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0184 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1682.37 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0185 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 184 ;
    minaret:startTime 1672.27 ;
    minaret:text "alhamdulillah they have these tools now that whatever is going on in Arabic, especially the khutbahs, they are translated for you on the spot in English if you have" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0185 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1692.71 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0186 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 185 ;
    minaret:startTime 1682.37 ;
    minaret:text "your gadgets with you, you can just tune in and listen to the same khutbah which is going on in Arabic, you can listen to that in your own language, SubhanAllah. There are a few languages they are Alhamdulillah" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0186 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1700.23 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0187 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 186 ;
    minaret:startTime 1692.71 ;
    minaret:text "worked on for khutbahs, and Insha'Allah it will be available for Hajj khutbah as well. So Insha'Allah don't miss that this year!" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0187 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1710.81 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0188 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 187 ;
    minaret:startTime 1700.81 ;
    minaret:text "And familiarity with different regions of the world, because you know people from all of the world are there, so you get to meet new people, different people, and you get to talk to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0188 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1718.07 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0189 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 188 ;
    minaret:startTime 1710.81 ;
    minaret:text "them, you learn new experiences, you learn how they do different things. And SubhanAllah it's a very beneficial trip. If you talk about" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0189 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1726.57 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0190 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 189 ;
    minaret:startTime 1718.61 ;
    minaret:text "benefits, it's a never-ending lecture, right? There are tons of benefits—just to be on the safer side we can say that, right?—there are tons of benefits, a lot" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0190 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1737.03 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0191 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 190 ;
    minaret:startTime 1727.23 ;
    minaret:text "of spiritual benefits as well. You know, you feel so good when you come back, you keep remembering all of that, and you are feeling the iman boost, you're feeling that you are" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0191 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1749.07 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0192 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 191 ;
    minaret:startTime 1737.03 ;
    minaret:text "more guided, SubhanAllah. And then what are we supposed to do when we are there in Baytullah? Allah says: لِيَشْهَدُوا مَنَافِعَ لَهُمْ وَيَذْكُرُوا اسْمَ اللَّهِ فِي أَيَّامٍ مَعْلُومَاتٍ." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0221 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2033.13 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0222 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 221 ;
    minaret:startTime 2030.75 ;
    minaret:text "ثُمَّ لْیَقْضُوا تَفَثَهُمْ. It" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0222 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2046.81 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0223 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 222 ;
    minaret:startTime 2033.1299999999999 ;
    minaret:text "has two understandings: one is that remove the dirt. How are we going to remove the dirt? Because when people are, you know, they live in Mina, you know, they get dirty sometimes and, you know, it's a lot of walking and all of that. So remove the dirt would be: clean yourself," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0223 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2048.47 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0224 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 223 ;
    minaret:startTime 2047.4099999999999 ;
    minaret:text "and, you know, cut" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0224 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2067.03 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0225 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 224 ;
    minaret:startTime 2048.47 ;
    minaret:text "also would mean to come out of ihram, and also would mean to shave the head for the brothers, and all. Another meaning is: complete Hajj rituals, complete the rest of the Hajj rituals. So once sacrifice is done, then complete the rest of the rituals, so that you can complete your" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0225 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2072.17 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0226 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 225 ;
    minaret:startTime 2067.03 ;
    minaret:text "Hajj, and after pretty much the main Hajj rites are done," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0234 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2170.47 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0235 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 234 ;
    minaret:startTime 2157.69 ;
    minaret:text "So scholars say it is Tawaf of Ifadah. And the word, it could have been وَلْيَطُوفُوا, but there is a shaddah on ṭā' (وَلْیَطَّوَّفُوا), which shows" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0235 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2181.81 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0236 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 235 ;
    minaret:startTime 2171.41 ;
    minaret:text "the struggle in it. So Tawaf Ifadah sometimes is very hard for people. Why is it hard for people? Because, you know, they're tired for all of these days" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0236 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2192.91 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0237 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 236 ;
    minaret:startTime 2181.81 ;
    minaret:text "and they just want to, you know, just complete their Hajj tasks and they want to come out of ihram; but now they have to go for tawaf after sacrificing" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0237 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2204.05 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0238 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 237 ;
    minaret:startTime 2192.91 ;
    minaret:text "their animal. Usually people go for tawaf, and just imagine everyone goes for tawaf at the same time, so it's sometimes hot, sometimes it's crowded. So it's okay, even" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0238 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2214.05 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0239 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 238 ;
    minaret:startTime 2204.05 ;
    minaret:text "if you have to put in some effort, do it. Another understanding of this is that why this shaddah is used or this form of this word is used, is that after" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0239 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2224.09 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0240 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 239 ;
    minaret:startTime 2214.05 ;
    minaret:text "you do Tawaf Ifadah, still do more tawaf if you get an opportunity, do as many tawafs as possible! Because as we have already mentioned, tawaf cannot be done elsewhere in" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0240 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2234.15 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0241 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 240 ;
    minaret:startTime 2224.09 ;
    minaret:text "the world. So while you're there, grab the opportunity, because tawaf is something which is beautiful, you're going to just love it, Insha'Allah, when you get there and when you actually make proper du'as" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0241 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2244.33 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0242 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 241 ;
    minaret:startTime 2234.15 ;
    minaret:text "and when you avail this opportunity happily, you're gonna, Insha'Allah, find a lot of benefits in tawaf. And the word الْعَتِيْقِ—why doesn't" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0242 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2254.53 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0243 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 242 ;
    minaret:startTime 2244.33 ;
    minaret:text "Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala call it Baytullah here? Allah knows best, right? That's one. And Atiq also has two meanings, you can say it gives us another angle to understand" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0243 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2256.95 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0244 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 243 ;
    minaret:startTime 2254.53 ;
    minaret:text "built, so that's why it's al-atiq. Another" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0244 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2266.73 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0245 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 244 ;
    minaret:startTime 2256.95 ;
    minaret:text "Baytullah: one is that al-atiq means ancient, so it's the ancient house, the old house—remember we talked about it that it's the first house built." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0245 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2278.09 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0246 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 245 ;
    minaret:startTime 2266.73 ;
    minaret:text "Another meaning is that it's a free house. What does that mean by free? It's not under anyone's possession, like it's not owned by people. Kaaba" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0257 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2388.15 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0258 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 257 ;
    minaret:startTime 2383.23 ;
    minaret:text "be halal? What can we sacrifice? What can we eat from? So all the an'am are" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0258 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2398.17 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0259 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 258 ;
    minaret:startTime 2388.15 ;
    minaret:text "halal. We have talked about them already: camels, cows, sheep, and goat, etc. Why is it mentioned? Because mushrikeen of Makkah, they made their own" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0259 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2408.03 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0260 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 259 ;
    minaret:startTime 2398.17 ;
    minaret:text "criterias: they made an'am haram on them, but they had some other different types of, you know, categories of animals they made halal. So Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala is" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0260 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2418.05 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0261 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 260 ;
    minaret:startTime 2408.03 ;
    minaret:text "reminding them what's halal and what's not. And then Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala gives us a very clear command: فَاجْتَنِبُوا الرِّجْسَ مِنَ الْأَوْثَانِ وَاجْتَنِبُوا قَوْلَ الزُّورِ—stay away, avoid rits" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0267 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2486.85 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0268 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 267 ;
    minaret:startTime 2476.83 ;
    minaret:text "So what are some of the lessons we have learned from all of these verses? Let's just look at them quickly. First one: going for Hajj and Umrah is actually responding to the call of Allah, even" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0268 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2494.53 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0269 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 268 ;
    minaret:startTime 2486.85 ;
    minaret:text "though that adhan was given or that call was given by Ibrahim, we call it call of Allah why? Because Allah told" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0269 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2504.53 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0270 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 269 ;
    minaret:startTime 2495.0699999999997 ;
    minaret:text "him to call us. It is permissible to go for Hajj on foot or on a ride, both are fine. Ibrahim visits to the House of Allah" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0270 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2514.81 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0271 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 270 ;
    minaret:startTime 2504.53 ;
    minaret:text "in every Hajj season—that's an indication, that's something we learn indirectly from all of these narrations because people would come to him, right?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0271 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2524.97 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0272 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 271 ;
    minaret:startTime 2514.81 ;
    minaret:text "So he would go to Hajj as well every Hajj season, and Allah knows best. Hajj days should be made the most of: so if you talked about the first 10 days, they" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0272 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2535.57 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0273 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 272 ;
    minaret:startTime 2525.6099999999997 ;
    minaret:text "should be made the most of even if you are not at Makkah. So Insha'Allah these days are around the corner, so Insha'Allah plan ahead and make sure that you do a lot of good deeds" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0273 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2549.29 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0274 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 273 ;
    minaret:startTime 2535.57 ;
    minaret:text "during these 10 days. You can also fast—not of course on Eid, but the rest of the days Insha'Allah for the first nine days you can memorize Qur'an, you can do charity, Insha'Allah many more things, and of course remember Allah much." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0274 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2563.41 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0275 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 274 ;
    minaret:startTime 2549.87 ;
    minaret:text "And dhikr of Allah should be done in abundance during Hajj days. So there was a very beautiful advice by Ustadha Dr. Farhat Hashmi that usually when people are going for Hajj, they ask you, like, you know, 'Give me a tip, tell me something I should" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0275 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2579.47 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0276 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 275 ;
    minaret:startTime 2563.41 ;
    minaret:text "do there, so give them this tip: that when you are there, remember Allah much. Don't waste your time, don't waste your energies there, just focus on your ibadah and make sure you remember Allah much. And then entering the House of Allah:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0276 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2589.47 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0277 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 276 ;
    minaret:startTime 2579.4700000000003 ;
    minaret:text "when you are entering Kaaba, entering Baytullah near it, realize the greatness of this beautiful house. Think about the history—we have talked about many things to do with it, right? Who" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0277 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2599.33 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0278 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 277 ;
    minaret:startTime 2589.47 ;
    minaret:text "built it, foundations were already there—and all of these things, if you keep them in your mind, Insha'Allah you will remember the greatness. And of course remember that Allah called it 'My" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0278 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2609.35 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0279 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 278 ;
    minaret:startTime 2599.33 ;
    minaret:text "House', so remember that as well. And it is not permissible to spread disobedience and filth in the House of Allah. Just remember this point:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0279 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2619.49 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0280 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 279 ;
    minaret:startTime 2609.35 ;
    minaret:text "that how can we be filthy in the House of Allah? How can we drop our used tissues, napkins there? How can we make it messy? How can we eat there" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0280 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2629.47 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0281 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 280 ;
    minaret:startTime 2619.49 ;
    minaret:text "and drop food particles there? Just imagine it's a House of Allah, and now try to just put yourself in a situation where you have guests over and your guests are" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0281 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2641.85 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0282 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 281 ;
    minaret:startTime 2629.47 ;
    minaret:text "really untidy and they drop things all over the place, how would you feel? Would you invite them again? So it's a House of Allah, respect it, keep it clean, even if you have to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0282 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2657.15 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0283 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 282 ;
    minaret:startTime 2641.85 ;
    minaret:text "use, you know, some napkins and tissues or whatnot or your masks, please keep them with you, discard them properly, don't keep the house dirty. Even though Alhamdulillah for the services, they keep cleaning them, but we're" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0283 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2664.73 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0284 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 283 ;
    minaret:startTime 2657.15 ;
    minaret:text "not supposed to become a burden on them, Insha'Allah. So take care of the cleanliness of Allah's house more than your own house." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0284 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2675.45 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0285 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 284 ;
    minaret:startTime 2665.43 ;
    minaret:text "Do qiyam, ruku, and sujood more as mentioned in these verses of Surah Al-Hajj. And Insha'Allah when are we going to do qiyam, ruku, and sujood more? If you're going to pray in the masajid, if you're going" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0285 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2685.49 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0286 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 285 ;
    minaret:startTime 2675.45 ;
    minaret:text "to pray our tahajjud, if you're going to pray our, Insha'Allah, duha there, and all these beautiful nawafil and salawat. And we can also eat from our own sacrificial" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0286 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2696.15 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0287 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 286 ;
    minaret:startTime 2685.49 ;
    minaret:text "animals—no problem with that. And vows were also prescribed in the Shariah of Ibrahim, that's a fact we learned from here, and fulfilling vows is a worship and it's also an obligation," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0287 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2701.97 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0288 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 287 ;
    minaret:startTime 2696.71 ;
    minaret:text "right? It wasn't an obligation before you made it a vow, but now because it's a vow, now it's an obligation." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0288 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2712.75 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0289 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 288 ;
    minaret:startTime 2702.63 ;
    minaret:text "It is also an obligation to fulfill the vows of slaughtering an animal. You know, sometimes people make these vows as well that: 'Every day I'm going to give one animal as a slaughter" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0289 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2719.57 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0290 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 289 ;
    minaret:startTime 2712.75 ;
    minaret:text "if Allah calls me here and there,' whatever, or 'If Allah gives me success.' So if people have made such vows, they are supposed to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0290 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2729.59 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0291 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 290 ;
    minaret:startTime 2719.57 ;
    minaret:text "fulfill them as well. So we are okay or we are allowed to eat from our own sacrificial animals if they are for Hajj, all right? Or if they are for qurban for Eid al-Adha. But we are not supposed to eat from the animal slaughtered in" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0291 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2739.61 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0292 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 291 ;
    minaret:startTime 2729.59 ;
    minaret:text "fulfill. But we are not supposed to eat from the animal slaughtered in fulfillment of a vow or as fidya, okay? This is not okay" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0292 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2749.59 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0293 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 292 ;
    minaret:startTime 2739.61 ;
    minaret:text "for us to eat, this is not allowed for us to eat, these two types of slaughtered animals by us. And it is not correct to perform tawaf" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0293 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2759.51 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0294 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 293 ;
    minaret:startTime 2749.59 ;
    minaret:text "from inside Hateem. So you know that half-circle type of construction on one side of the Kaaba, we're not supposed to bypass it or go through it because" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0294 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2769.61 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0295 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 294 ;
    minaret:startTime 2759.51 ;
    minaret:text "that was actually part of Kaaba, so if we're going to go through it, our that cycle is not complete. So we have to be extremely cautious, and Alhamdulillah they have blocked" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0295 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2779.69 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0296 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 295 ;
    minaret:startTime 2769.61 ;
    minaret:text "it, so we cannot really go through. But let's say if they open it for cleaning purposes, don't just think that you're smart enough to go inside and make your cycle shorter, because your cycle won't be" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0296 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2789.67 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0297 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 296 ;
    minaret:startTime 2779.69 ;
    minaret:text "valid anymore if you go through it, SubhanAllah. And tawaf is an important part of Hajj, tawaf can be done at any time, so there is no forbidden timings for tawaf," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0297 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2802.61 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0298 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 297 ;
    minaret:startTime 2789.67 ;
    minaret:text "you know, like for salah there are some forbidden timings, but for tawaf there is none. So you can, Insha'Allah, do tawaf whenever you can, and Hajj ends with Tawaf Ifadah, and it is a wajib. So, Insha'Allah, we will" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0298 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2810.55 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0299 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 298 ;
    minaret:startTime 2802.61 ;
    minaret:text "talk about all different types of tawaf and their names and definitions, so don't worry too much about it, just jot down the points at this point. So what are some of the" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0299 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2820.59 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0300 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 299 ;
    minaret:startTime 2810.55 ;
    minaret:text "aims and objectives of Hajj. First of all: to establish pure tawheed. Aim and objective of Hajj is to establish pure tawheed. Second benefit," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0300 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2830.51 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0301 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 300 ;
    minaret:startTime 2820.59 ;
    minaret:text "second aim and objective: taqwa. The way we achieve taqwa from fasting, Alhamdulillah with Hajj we also achieve that. And" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0301 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2840.59 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0302 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 301 ;
    minaret:startTime 2830.51 ;
    minaret:text "the aim and objective is that we remember Allah much, we do a lot of dhikr of Allah. And in Talbiyah as well you would notice that it's pure tawheed in Talbiyah, right? We don't" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0303 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2860.13 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0304 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 303 ;
    minaret:startTime 2851.85 ;
    minaret:text "Then we are also told in Surah Al-Baqarah that when we are done with our Hajj rites, then what should we do? Remember" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0305 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2888.57 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0306 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 305 ;
    minaret:startTime 2873.75 ;
    minaret:text "Do dhikr of Allah. And how should you remember Allah? Remember Allah the way Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala has guided you. So we can remember Allah in many ways: we can remember Allah in salah, we can remember Allah in tawaf, we can remember Allah by reciting Qur'an, and much more." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0306 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2895.23 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0307 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 306 ;
    minaret:startTime 2889.41 ;
    minaret:text "Other objectives and aims of Hajj are that we do istighfar and we get forgiveness. So Insha'Allah keep doing istighfar," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0307 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2903.99 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0308 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 307 ;
    minaret:startTime 2895.23 ;
    minaret:text "A lot of times people think that we're already at Hajj, we will be forgiven, what's the point of doing istighfar? Remember, we are human beings, so we make mistakes. So it is possible that while doing" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0308 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2914.29 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0309 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 308 ;
    minaret:startTime 2903.9900000000002 ;
    minaret:text "a lot of Hajj we make mistakes in Hajj rites, so it's a very good idea to keep doing istighfar, keep asking Allah for forgiveness for our shortcomings. And then tazkiyah" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0309 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2928.53 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0310 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 309 ;
    minaret:startTime 2914.29 ;
    minaret:text "is a beautiful objective of Hajj: that we should come back with a pure heart, we should come back with a better heart, with a good heart. May Allah enable us to do that, Ameen! And we should not fight there, and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0310 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2935.29 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0311 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 310 ;
    minaret:startTime 2928.53 ;
    minaret:text "we should not disobey Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala there. Another objective is that we" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0311 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2945.21 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0312 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 311 ;
    minaret:startTime 2935.29 ;
    minaret:text "learn to respect the Hajj months and Hajj sites. So everything about Hajj is respectable—for example, all sites, so think about Kaaba, think about" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0312 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2955.35 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0313 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 312 ;
    minaret:startTime 2945.21 ;
    minaret:text "Mina, Muzdalifah, Arafat—we should respect all Hajj sites, and we should respect all Hajj rituals and rites, and we should also respect all hujjaj there" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0313 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2961.05 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0314 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 313 ;
    minaret:startTime 2955.35 ;
    minaret:text "insha'Allah, because they all are there to worship Allah. So we should not" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0314 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2965.29 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0315 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 314 ;
    minaret:startTime 2961.05 ;
    minaret:text "make it difficult for them to do Hajj because of us. Another aim and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0315 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2979.07 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0316 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 315 ;
    minaret:startTime 2965.29 ;
    minaret:text "objective of Hajj is the sense of gratitude: that Alhamdulillah Allah called us, Alhamdulillah Allah gave me the opportunity that I can walk and do Hajj, or even if I'm not able to walk, I can sit and do Hajj on a wheelchair or on a cart." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0316 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2989.49 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0317 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 316 ;
    minaret:startTime 2979.57 ;
    minaret:text "So Alhamdulillah when people reach there, so this sense of gratitude develops automatically, but we also need to remind ourselves that we have to be more grateful that Allah called" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0317 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2999.75 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0318 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 317 ;
    minaret:startTime 2989.49 ;
    minaret:text "us here. And we also need to instill the quality of patience in us, and there's a reminder at Hajj which we get pretty much at every location," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0318 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3008.21 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0319 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 318 ;
    minaret:startTime 2999.75 ;
    minaret:text "at every Hajj, right? And that is standing before Allah on the Day of Judgment. A lot of people from different backgrounds," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0319 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3016.43 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0320 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 319 ;
    minaret:startTime 3008.87 ;
    minaret:text "you know, maybe some are rich, maybe some are poor, maybe some are tall, maybe some are short, but all of them are there standing to worship Allah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0320 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3025.93 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0321 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 320 ;
    minaret:startTime 3017.09 ;
    minaret:text "All of them are standing in Arafat. So it's a good reminder for all of us that one day we will be standing in front of Allah on the Day of Judgment." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0321 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3031.11 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0322 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 321 ;
    minaret:startTime 3027.57 ;
    minaret:text "And then let's just talk about Hajj rulings quickly, Insha'Allah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0322 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3037.67 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0323 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 322 ;
    minaret:startTime 3031.11 ;
    minaret:text "will build on them, so don't worry too much about the details, just jot down important points at this point. So when it comes" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0364 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3446.19 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0365 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 364 ;
    minaret:startTime 3432.09 ;
    minaret:text "Michelle, good question: 'Is there a particular dress for men doing Umrah?' Yes, yes, same ihram is the same for Umrah, it's the same ihram which we wear for Hajj, it's the same for Umrah as well." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0365 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3450.79 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0366 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 365 ;
    minaret:startTime 3446.19 ;
    minaret:text "It's just Umrah is shorter, we're done in a few hours; Hajj is longer," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0366 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3459.77 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0367 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 366 ;
    minaret:startTime 3450.79 ;
    minaret:text "It goes over a few days. Sister Subal was asking: 'How long does it take for Hajj to complete?' So roughly five to six days, all right? And Allah knows best." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0367 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3473.05 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0368 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 367 ;
    minaret:startTime 3460.43 ;
    minaret:text "You know, if we are going for Hajj, Sister Michelle, right? So if you're going for Hajj, then we are to wear the ihram for Hajj during Hajj months; but if you're going for Umrah, let's say in November or" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0368 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3480.53 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0369 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 368 ;
    minaret:startTime 3473.05 ;
    minaret:text "if you're going for Umrah, let's say in Muharram, so then we will get in the ihram for that Umrah only." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0000 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 10.06 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0001 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 0 ;
    minaret:startTime 0.0 ;
    minaret:text "نَحْمَدُهُ وَنُصَلِّيَ لَا رَسُولِهِ الْكَرِيمِ أَمَّا بَعَدْ فَأَعُوذُ بِاللَّهِ مِنَ الشَّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيمِ بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَنِ الرَّحِيمِ رَبِّ شْرَحْلِي صَدْرِي" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0002 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 31.34 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0003 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 2 ;
    minaret:startTime 22.4 ;
    minaret:text "Inshallah today we're going to focus on the ayat from Surah Al-Baqarah. And inshallah we'll learn about what Allah subhanahu wa ta'ala mentions in these ayat for us." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0003 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 38.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0004 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 3 ;
    minaret:startTime 31.62 ;
    minaret:text "So let's begin inshallah, let's listen to the recitation and remember when the recitation is going on we are supposed to listen quietly." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0025 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 269.0 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0026 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 25 ;
    minaret:startTime 259.78 ;
    minaret:text "So subhanAllah, when you look at these verses, just by going over the translation of these verses, we realize that these verses are the most comprehensive verses," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0026 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 280.16 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0027 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 26 ;
    minaret:startTime 270.12 ;
    minaret:text "explaining the etiquettes of Hajj and also some rulings to do with Hajj. The rites of Hajj and Umrah were well-known among Arabs even before Islam." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0027 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 287.86 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0028 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 27 ;
    minaret:startTime 280.42 ;
    minaret:text "But they included some acts which contained a lot of, you can say, shirk and many false and superstitious things." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0028 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 298.68 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0029 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 28 ;
    minaret:startTime 287.86 ;
    minaret:text "But what Islam did was, the best deeds were added in Umrah and Hajj, which were highly rewardable. So this made Hajj and Umrah a super special ibadah for us." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0080 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 816.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0081 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 80 ;
    minaret:startTime 806.64 ;
    minaret:text "So based on this, a lot of people or a lot of scholars also discuss this factor that does it mean the way Hajj is mandatory? Umrah is also mandatory?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0081 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 826.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0082 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 81 ;
    minaret:startTime 816.72 ;
    minaret:text "What do you guys think? Is Umrah mandatory just like Hajj is? So is Umrah wajib? Wajib is a term which refers to something which is mandatory, right?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0082 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 837.2 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0083 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 82 ;
    minaret:startTime 827.1 ;
    minaret:text "Because this ayah says complete Hajj in Umrah for Allah, a lot of people, they assume that it is because maybe both are equal in status and both are supposed to be performed." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0083 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 850.84 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0084 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 83 ;
    minaret:startTime 837.8399999999999 ;
    minaret:text "So let's see, there is a difference of opinion on this and Imam Bukhari also, he brings a chapter in his book about it and we learned that Ibn Umar, the son of Umrah r.a, his opinion was that Hajj and Umrah are obligatory on everyone." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0084 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 859.66 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0085 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 84 ;
    minaret:startTime 851.18 ;
    minaret:text "Ibn Abbas r.a, he said, they are companions in the book of Allah, like they come together. Imam Bukhari, he used to support this position that it is wajib." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0085 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 870.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0086 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 85 ;
    minaret:startTime 859.84 ;
    minaret:text "Ibn Baas, rahimahullah, he said like Hajj, Umrah is an obligation once in a lifetime. Ibn Uthaymeen said what appears to be that Umrah is an obligation." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0086 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 881.34 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0087 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 86 ;
    minaret:startTime 870.72 ;
    minaret:text "Subhanallah. So from this, what did we learn? The thing is, a lot of people, you know, they don't really think of Umrah like that because whenever they go for Hajj, they do Umrah anyways, right? So both are fulfilled." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0087 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 891.14 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0088 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 87 ;
    minaret:startTime 881.54 ;
    minaret:text "But let's look at another aspect. Some people are too scared of going to Umrah because they think if you go for Umrah, then your Hajj becomes wajid." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0088 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 898.3 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0089 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 88 ;
    minaret:startTime 891.14 ;
    minaret:text "Did you ever hear this? This is actually, you know, you can say it's a myth. Your Hajj is wajib when you're rich enough. Okay?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0089 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 906.7 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0090 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 89 ;
    minaret:startTime 898.76 ;
    minaret:text "Your Hajj is wajib when you're rich enough, when you're able enough, when you're physically able, when you're financially able, then Hajj is wajib on you." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0090 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 914.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0091 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 90 ;
    minaret:startTime 906.88 ;
    minaret:text "So your Umrah doesn't have anything to do with the wujub of Hajj. So it's not linked like that." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0091 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 923.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0092 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 91 ;
    minaret:startTime 914.82 ;
    minaret:text "But if we have enough resources to go for Umrah, we should not delay. Let's say this person is saving up for Hajj. But Hajj is getting expensive every year." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0092 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 935.42 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0093 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 92 ;
    minaret:startTime 923.8 ;
    minaret:text "So this person is not able to go for Hajj, but he has enough money to go for Umrah. So based on this opinion that Umrah is quite important and maybe it is an obligation, so what should this person do?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0093 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 946.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0094 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 93 ;
    minaret:startTime 935.5 ;
    minaret:text "What do you guys think? This person should go for Umrah. Exactly. And remember that beautiful Hadith that when a person goes to Hajj and Umrah frequently, that person doesn't stay destitute." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0094 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 956.24 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0095 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 94 ;
    minaret:startTime 947.04 ;
    minaret:text "Right? That the poverty is removed from that person. So Inshallah, when we go for Umrah, Umrah upon Umrah, Inshallah, Allah will make us rich enough that one day we can also go for Hajj." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0095 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 966.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0096 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 95 ;
    minaret:startTime 956.66 ;
    minaret:text "So this is a myth that if you do Umrah, Hajj becomes wajib. Hajj is already wajib if you're rich enough. If you're not, then it's not even wajib. So there is no such connection as such." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0096 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 977.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0097 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 96 ;
    minaret:startTime 967.12 ;
    minaret:text "But let's say you were not able to go for Umrah before, but now you have enough means to go for Hajj, then Inshallah, when you go for Hajj, you do perform Umrah as well. And that's what a lot of people do when they go from the other countries." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0097 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 988.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0098 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 97 ;
    minaret:startTime 977.62 ;
    minaret:text "They do Hajj tamadur. It's a combination of both Umrah and Hajj. Alhamdulillah. Okay, the next part of the ayah tells us that if something stops you, right, if there's a hurdle, then what should a person do?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0135 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1388.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0136 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 135 ;
    minaret:startTime 1378.64 ;
    minaret:text "So we should not become so sad and we should not feel like a letdown or what not when anything of this sort happens because subhanallah policies keep on changing things are changing subhanallah this" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0136 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1403.42 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0137 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 136 ;
    minaret:startTime 1388.62 ;
    minaret:text "year as well a lot of people were going for hajj but now because of the new system people are really worried but inshallah just take it as you know Allah subhanahu wa ta'ala's will and accept it there must be khayr in it and Allah only knows what's the best for all of us." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0138 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1423.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0139 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 138 ;
    minaret:startTime 1412.94 ;
    minaret:text "until and unless you're done with sacrifice. So shaving part should not be done before sacrifice this is something we learn from this ayah it also includes" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0139 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1434.22 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0140 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 139 ;
    minaret:startTime 1424.2 ;
    minaret:text "cutting the nails it also includes shaving off any hair from any part of the body unwanted hair so all of this comes under this so what is usually done when" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0140 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1444.06 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0141 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 140 ;
    minaret:startTime 1434.22 ;
    minaret:text "it comes to Umrah and Hajj for women what is done just taqseer you know trimming and for the men what's the best that they" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0141 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1454.32 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0142 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 141 ;
    minaret:startTime 1444.06 ;
    minaret:text "actually shave their heads and trim is okay as well it's allowed but what is better is that they shave and they should do that after they're done with" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0142 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1464.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0143 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 142 ;
    minaret:startTime 1454.32 ;
    minaret:text "their hadhi after they're done with their sacrificial animal and there are two timings of that one is that the Eid day comes and when sacrificial animals" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0143 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1474.42 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0144 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 143 ;
    minaret:startTime 1464.36 ;
    minaret:text "are slaughtered right so that is the tenth of Dulhijjah or the sacrificial animal is slaughtered so it is possible that Eid" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0144 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1484.04 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0145 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 144 ;
    minaret:startTime 1474.42 ;
    minaret:text "day was so busy for many Hujjaj and their sacrificial animal wasn't slaughtered on Eid day maybe it was slaughtered on eleventh right and sometimes it is sacrificed on" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0145 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1494.16 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0146 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 145 ;
    minaret:startTime 1484.04 ;
    minaret:text "twelfth and sometimes because of this you know hurdle on the way maybe it is sacrificed on the first of the Hujjah so whenever the sacrificial animal is slaughtered a person" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0146 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1504.22 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0147 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 146 ;
    minaret:startTime 1494.16 ;
    minaret:text "can shave after that not before that so let's understand the time of sacrifice and Hajj Qiran Hafsa the wife of Rasulullah ﷺ said Ya" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0150 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1547.1599999999999 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0151 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 150 ;
    minaret:startTime 1534.58 ;
    minaret:text "Ihram till I have slaughtered my animal subhanallah so what do we learn from this so this was a different type of Hajj the rest of Sahaba and some of Sahaba actually not all of them some of them were also doing the Hajj" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0151 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1557.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0152 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 151 ;
    minaret:startTime 1547.66 ;
    minaret:text "which is when you're done Umrah you can come out of Ihram restrictions you can do whatever you want to do after that but when Hajj days enter starting from 8th of Dhul" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0152 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1565.14 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0153 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 152 ;
    minaret:startTime 1557.64 ;
    minaret:text "Hijjah then a person can go back in Ihram and that is Hajj but because Rasulullah ﷺ he was doing Hajj" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0153 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1575.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0154 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 153 ;
    minaret:startTime 1565.82 ;
    minaret:text "that's why he did not come out of his Ihram restrictions so when a person is supposed to shave or trim before or after the sacrifice let's see there is" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0154 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1585.86 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0155 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 154 ;
    minaret:startTime 1575.72 ;
    minaret:text "no harm if one gets his hair shaved or trimmed before the sacrifice and it is more virtuous to get it done after the sacrifice so what is better after the sacrifice so" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0155 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1595.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0156 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 155 ;
    minaret:startTime 1585.86 ;
    minaret:text "why are we learning about this because a lot of people go for Hajj these days right and it is not possible to get all the animals slaughtered on one day like the 10th" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0156 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1605.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0157 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 156 ;
    minaret:startTime 1595.78 ;
    minaret:text "so sometimes they have to slaughter animals on 11th 12th as well but as long as we know that animal will be slaughtered so inshallah both options are" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0157 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1615.82 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0158 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 157 ;
    minaret:startTime 1605.78 ;
    minaret:text "there to be exact so one can do the good part as well or if you want to go for the best and inshallah most virtuous is to get it done after the sacrifice so the words" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0160 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1651.2 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0161 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 160 ;
    minaret:startTime 1641.22 ;
    minaret:text "Mushrikeen of Makkah they would dislike this act that you know you do Umrah and Hajj in the same trip so they did not like that and they used to think that it was wrong" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0161 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1661.28 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0162 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 161 ;
    minaret:startTime 1651.2 ;
    minaret:text "so Imran bin Hussain he is mentioning that here that it is mentioned in the Quran it's allowed for us to do it that we can do Umrah and Hajj in the same trip and that Alhamdulillah" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0162 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1671.34 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0163 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 162 ;
    minaret:startTime 1661.28 ;
    minaret:text "makes it easy for the Muslims they don't have to take two trips to do their Umrah and Hajj they can just go for one trip and they can do both inshallah in that and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0163 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1681.24 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0164 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 163 ;
    minaret:startTime 1671.34 ;
    minaret:text "when it comes to Hajj rites and rituals Rasulullah he was you know mashallah very easy going in that regard so let's look at this beautiful narration Rasulullah" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0168 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1736.22 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0169 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 168 ;
    minaret:startTime 1726.3 ;
    minaret:text "everything you're good and subhanAllah when we are going to go over the steps of the Hajj you will notice that on 10th of Dhul Hijjah a lot of things are going on you know for a" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0169 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1746.32 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0170 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 169 ;
    minaret:startTime 1736.22 ;
    minaret:text "haji so it's sometimes very hard to keep track of everything in order so Alhamdulillah for this ease from our deen Alhamdulillah there's another narration which talks" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0170 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1756.28 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0171 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 170 ;
    minaret:startTime 1746.32 ;
    minaret:text "about this similar Rasulullah was asked about slaughtering and shaving of the head and doing a furami before or after the due times he said there is no harm" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0171 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1766.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0172 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 171 ;
    minaret:startTime 1756.28 ;
    minaret:text "in that subhanAllah next part of the ayah talks about another situation when there is a person who is marid or has some type of hurt or harm" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0201 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2078.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0202 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 201 ;
    minaret:startTime 2068.62 ;
    minaret:text "let's say this person was stopped and is not able to go for umrah or hajj but inshaallah whenever there is safety whenever" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0202 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2085.4 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0203 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 202 ;
    minaret:startTime 2078.54 ;
    minaret:text "a person is able to go back should go back and complete the hajj and umrah that's what we learned from this part of the verse whenever" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0203 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2096.4 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0204 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 203 ;
    minaret:startTime 2086.42 ;
    minaret:text "you are safe then what do you do then go for umrah and hajj and complete it and also give tahadi the sacrificial animal and another thing we need to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0204 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2102.74 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0205 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 204 ;
    minaret:startTime 2096.4 ;
    minaret:text "remember is that ihram is to be observed in hajj months and ihram is not only ihram clothing" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0205 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2113.38 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0206 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 205 ;
    minaret:startTime 2103.32 ;
    minaret:text "ihram when we say it's about the state so ihram clothing can be changed many times while you are in the state of ihram because a lot of times people think that okay when i'm wearing" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0206 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2124.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0207 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 206 ;
    minaret:startTime 2113.38 ;
    minaret:text "this ihram this outfit is stuck to me and i have to keep wearing it till the end of my hajj journey that's not true so in that state we can take showers we can do many things and it" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0207 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2139.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0208 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 207 ;
    minaret:startTime 2124.72 ;
    minaret:text "doesn't harm our ihram, Insha'Allah. So when we are going for Hajj, we cannot go in ihram in Ramadan. Remember that point, Insha'Allah? So let's say some people, they are there in Makkah for six months," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0208 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2149.42 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0209 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 208 ;
    minaret:startTime 2139.52 ;
    minaret:text "and they do their umrah in ramadan they do their umrah even before ramadan and now they want to perform hajj but they want to make it tamattu they just come to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0209 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2159.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0210 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 209 ;
    minaret:startTime 2149.42 ;
    minaret:text "minna on 8th of dhu hijj and they assume that they are doing tamattu that won't be correct because their umrah should be done in hajj months in order for their hajj to be" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0210 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2173.68 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0211 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 210 ;
    minaret:startTime 2159.36 ;
    minaret:text "tamattu so inshallah something to remember so ihram in hajj months will be considered for hajj before that would be umrah inshallah but not for hajj and when it comes to hajj days we have learned about that these" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0211 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2189.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0212 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 211 ;
    minaret:startTime 2173.68 ;
    minaret:text "are the three months: Shawwal, Dhu al-Qa'dah, and Dhu al-Hijjah—these are the Hajj months. But when it comes to Dhu al-Hijjah, there is a difference of opinion: some scholars say the whole of Dhu al-Hijjah is a Hajj month, some scholars say only the first 10 days of Dhu al-Hijjah are Hajj months, like those first" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0247 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2523.06 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0248 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 247 ;
    minaret:startTime 2515.58 ;
    minaret:text "of what to be done. So sacrifice is mandatory in Hajj Tamattu', that's what we have learned. But when it comes to the people" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0248 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2533.22 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0249 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 248 ;
    minaret:startTime 2523.06 ;
    minaret:text "who are locals they live in haram boundaries then they don't have to worry about the sacrificial animal so while we are talking about haram boundaries we need to remember" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0249 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2543.22 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0250 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 249 ;
    minaret:startTime 2533.22 ;
    minaret:text "haram boundaries are not just al-masjid al-haram that's why you must have heard scholars saying that you know these hotels they come under haram bounds or these areas they come under" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0250 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2553.16 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0251 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 250 ;
    minaret:startTime 2543.22 ;
    minaret:text "haram bounds so if you pray anywhere there even outside masjid you get the reward of praying 100,000 prayers another point to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0251 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2563.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0252 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 251 ;
    minaret:startTime 2553.16 ;
    minaret:text "remember that when you pray in al-masjid al-haram not only you get the reward of one prayer which is 100,000 prayers elsewhere but time it by 27" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0252 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2573.22 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0253 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 252 ;
    minaret:startTime 2563.44 ;
    minaret:text "right because praying in jama'ah gets you 27 times more reward so subhanallah praying in masjid al-haram behind the imam" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0253 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2578.6 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0254 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 253 ;
    minaret:startTime 2573.22 ;
    minaret:text "is very rewardable so that should not be missed subhanallah and know" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0255 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2593.42 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0256 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 255 ;
    minaret:startTime 2581.82 ;
    minaret:text "that Allah is shadeed al-iqab so what are some of the lessons we learn from this verse we learn about the proof of the obligation of we learn about fulfilling the duties and obligations of and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0256 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2604.2 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0257 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 256 ;
    minaret:startTime 2594.26 ;
    minaret:text "we should complete the hajj when it started we should complete the umrah when it started and we should perform hajj and umrah properly with its given rights and the ihraam of hajj and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0257 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2615.98 ;
