minaret:QuranVerse_22_27 a minaret:QuranVerse ;
    minaret:juz 17 ;
    minaret:surahNumber 22 ;
    minaret:textClean "وأذن في الناس بالحج يأتوك رجالا وعلى كل ضامر يأتين من كل فج عميق" ;
    minaret:textIndopak "وَاَذِّنْ فِی النَّاسِ بِالْحَجِّ یَاْتُوْكَ رِجَالًا وَّعَلٰی كُلِّ ضَامِرٍ یَّاْتِیْنَ مِنْ كُلِّ فَجٍّ عَمِیْقٍ ۟ۙ" ;
    minaret:textUthmani "وَأَذِّن فِي ٱلنَّاسِ بِٱلۡحَجِّ يَأۡتُوكَ رِجَالًا وَعَلَىٰ كُلِّ ضَامِرٍ يَأۡتِينَ مِن كُلِّ فَجٍّ عَمِيقٍ" ;
    minaret:translationEn "And proclaim to the people the Hajj [pilgrimage]; they will come to you on foot and on every lean camel; they will come from every distant pass -" ;
    minaret:translationUr "" ;
    minaret:verseNumber 27 ;
    skos:exactMatch qur:quran22-27,
        tafsir:V022_027 .

minaret:QuranVerse_22_29 a minaret:QuranVerse ;
    minaret:juz 17 ;
    minaret:surahNumber 22 ;
    minaret:textClean "ثم ليقضوا تفثهم وليوفوا نذورهم وليطوفوا بالبيت العتيق" ;
    minaret:textIndopak "ثُمَّ لْیَقْضُوْا تَفَثَهُمْ وَلْیُوْفُوْا نُذُوْرَهُمْ وَلْیَطَّوَّفُوْا بِالْبَیْتِ الْعَتِیْقِ ۟" ;
    minaret:textUthmani "ثُمَّ لۡيَقۡضُواْ تَفَثَهُمۡ وَلۡيُوفُواْ نُذُورَهُمۡ وَلۡيَطَّوَّفُواْ بِٱلۡبَيۡتِ ٱلۡعَتِيقِ" ;
    minaret:translationEn "Then let them end their untidiness and fulfill their vows and perform Tawaf around the ancient House.\"" ;
    minaret:translationUr "" ;
    minaret:verseNumber 29 ;
    skos:exactMatch qur:quran22-29,
        tafsir:V022_029 .

minaret:QuranVerse_22_30 a minaret:QuranVerse ;
    minaret:juz 17 ;
    minaret:surahNumber 22 ;
    minaret:textClean "ذلك ومن يعظم حرمات الله فهو خير له عند ربه ۗ وأحلت لكم الأنعام إلا ما يتلى عليكم ۖ فاجتنبوا الرجس من الأوثان واجتنبوا قول الزور" ;
    minaret:textIndopak "ذٰلِكَ ۗ وَمَنْ یُّعَظِّمْ حُرُمٰتِ اللّٰهِ فَهُوَ خَیْرٌ لَّهٗ عِنْدَ رَبِّهٖ ؕ وَاُحِلَّتْ لَكُمُ الْاَنْعَامُ اِلَّا مَا یُتْلٰی عَلَیْكُمْ فَاجْتَنِبُوا الرِّجْسَ مِنَ الْاَوْثَانِ وَاجْتَنِبُوْا قَوْلَ الزُّوْرِ ۟ۙ" ;
    minaret:textUthmani "ذَٰلِكَۖ وَمَن يُعَظِّمۡ حُرُمَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ فَهُوَ خَيۡرٌ لَّهُۥ عِندَ رَبِّهِۦۗ وَأُحِلَّتۡ لَكُمُ ٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمُ إِلَّا مَا يُتۡلَىٰ عَلَيۡكُمۡۖ فَٱجۡتَنِبُواْ ٱلرِّجۡسَ مِنَ ٱلۡأَوۡثَٰنِ وَٱجۡتَنِبُواْ قَوۡلَ ٱلزُّورِ" ;
    minaret:translationEn "That [has been commanded], and whoever honors the sacred ordinances of Allah - it is best for him in the sight of his Lord. And permitted to you are the grazing livestock, except what is recited to you. So avoid the uncleanliness of idols and avoid false statement," ;
    minaret:translationUr "" ;
    minaret:verseNumber 30 ;
    skos:exactMatch qur:quran22-30,
        tafsir:V022_030 .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0001 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 20.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0002 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 1 ;
    minaret:startTime 10.62 ;
    minaret:text "لَكَ وَالْمُلْكَ، لَاشَرِیْكَ لَكَ۔ لَبَّیْكَ اَللّٰهُمَّ لَبَّیْكَ، لَبَّیْكَ لَا شَرِیْكَ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0002 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 29.06 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0003 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 2 ;
    minaret:startTime 20.94 ;
    minaret:text "لَكَ لَبَّیْكَ، اِنَّ الْحَمْدَ، وَالنِّعْمَةَ لَكَ وَالْمُلْكَ، لَاشَرِیْكَ لَكَ۔" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0003 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 44.28 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0004 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 3 ;
    minaret:startTime 29.06 ;
    minaret:text "لَبَّیْكَ اَللّٰهُمَّ لَبَّیْكَ، لَبَّیْكَ لَا شَرِیْكَ لَكَ لَبَّیْكَ، اِنَّ الْحَمْدَ، وَالنِّعْمَةَ لَكَ وَالْمُلْكَ، لَاشَرِیْكَ لَكَ۔" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0012 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 141.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0013 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 12 ;
    minaret:startTime 131.98000000000002 ;
    minaret:text "وَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُهٗ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ۔ اَعُوْذُ بِاللّٰهِ مِنَ الشَّیْطٰنِ الرَّجِیْمِ۔ بِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِیْمِ۔ رَبِّ اشْرَحْ لِیْ صَدْرِیْ ۙ وَیَسِّرْ لِیْۤ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0013 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 152.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0014 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 13 ;
    minaret:startTime 141.94 ;
    minaret:text "اَمْرِیْ ۙ وَاحْلُلْ عُقْدَةً مِّنْ لِّسَانِیْ ۙ یَفْقَهُوْا قَوْلِیْ۔ اَللّٰهُمَّ فَقِّهْنَا فِی الدِّیْنِ. May Allah give us the correct understanding of our deen, Ameen. So with that," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0030 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 319.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0031 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 30 ;
    minaret:startTime 308.54 ;
    minaret:text "رَحْمَة (rahmat), فَضْل (fadl), and رِزْق (rizq). اَللّٰهُمَّ ابْسُطْ عَلَيْنَا مِنْ بَرَكَاتِكَ، وَرَحْمَتِكَ، وَفَضْلِكَ، وَرِزْقِكَ. O Allah, give us in abundance—what?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0042 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 446.74 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0043 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 42 ;
    minaret:startTime 436.7 ;
    minaret:text "Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala's promises are true. So to fulfill the most important journey of one's life with sincerity for the sake of Allah, this should be our goal:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0043 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 456.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0044 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 43 ;
    minaret:startTime 446.74 ;
    minaret:text "to fulfill the most important journey of one's life. You may travel here and there, but this is going to be Insha'Allah the best journey of your life, most important journey of your" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0044 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 466.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0045 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 44 ;
    minaret:startTime 456.76 ;
    minaret:text "life. So how are we supposed to take this journey? With sincerity, with ikhlas. Why? For the sake of Allah, only for the sake of Allah. Not for fame," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0045 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 477.56 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0046 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 45 ;
    minaret:startTime 466.94 ;
    minaret:text "not for name, not for some games, not for some business. We should Insha'Allah keep it as pure as possible. Why? Because Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala commanded us to do that:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0047 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 497.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0048 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 47 ;
    minaret:startTime 488.08 ;
    minaret:text "do it for Allah, don't do it for any other reason. So Insha'Allah our goal is that we will Insha'Allah perform Hajj and Umrah whenever we get a chance only for the" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0048 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 509.28 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0049 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 48 ;
    minaret:startTime 497.94 ;
    minaret:text "pleasure of Allah, not the pleasure of people. Only for the pleasure of Allah, only we want Allah to be happy with us, only we want the approval of Allah, we don't want the approval of people." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0049 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 520.2 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0050 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 49 ;
    minaret:startTime 510.21999999999997 ;
    minaret:text "So in order to do this, we need to ask ourselves a few questions, and one of them is: why am I going for Hajj? Like why? Why am I saving" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0050 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 530.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0051 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 50 ;
    minaret:startTime 520.2 ;
    minaret:text "up for Hajj? Why do I yearn to go for Hajj? What is the intention? And Insha'Allah we have to be truthful to ourselves in order to fix our intention. If" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0051 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 540.38 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0052 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 51 ;
    minaret:startTime 530.36 ;
    minaret:text "it's any other reason—and it sometimes is—then Insha'Allah this is the time to fix it before it's too late, before we perform it, right? So Insha'Allah if you" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0052 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 545.84 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0053 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 52 ;
    minaret:startTime 540.38 ;
    minaret:text "did not do your Hajj yet, and if you're going this year, then Insha'Allah this is the time to fix your intention." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0053 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 556.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0054 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 53 ;
    minaret:startTime 546.56 ;
    minaret:text "And we've got to Insha'Allah make it a habit that we actually ask ourselves before doing other actions as well that: why am I praying? Why am I fasting?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0054 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 566.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0055 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 54 ;
    minaret:startTime 556.76 ;
    minaret:text "Why am I giving sadaqah? All of these questions are going to help us keep our intentions purely for Allah, and this is a way to keep a check on our" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0055 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 576.92 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0056 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 55 ;
    minaret:startTime 566.72 ;
    minaret:text "intentions. So Insha'Allah just make it a habit: keep asking and keep giving yourself honest answers. Honest answers will help you Insha'Allah fix the intention issues," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0056 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 586.74 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0057 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 56 ;
    minaret:startTime 576.92 ;
    minaret:text "because intention is something which is very risky; it keeps changing because shaytan is there, our nafs is there, right? And our influences are there, our company sometimes," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0057 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 596.68 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0058 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 57 ;
    minaret:startTime 586.74 ;
    minaret:text "you know, they make us think something which is not correct. So Insha'Allah in order to keep ourselves away from all of this, and above and beyond from petty" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0058 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 606.74 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0059 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 58 ;
    minaret:startTime 596.68 ;
    minaret:text "reasons and petty purposes, we need to keep asking ourselves these questions so that we can fix our intention before it gets too late. And why the intention is so" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0061 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 640.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0062 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 61 ;
    minaret:startTime 630.58 ;
    minaret:text "a double intention. So when people are going for Hajj, they need to remind themselves that it should only be for Allah, it should only be to please Allah, it" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0062 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 650.74 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0063 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 62 ;
    minaret:startTime 640.72 ;
    minaret:text "should not be to please people, it should not be for any other reason, it should not be for fame. So may Allah protect us from all wrong intentions. So" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0084 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 871.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0085 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 84 ;
    minaret:startTime 862.18 ;
    minaret:text "اَللّٰهُمَّ اَسْئَلُكَ لَذَّةَ النَّظَرِ اِلٰی وَجْهِكَ، وَالشَّوْقَ اِلٰی لِقَائِكَ فِیْ غَيْرِ ضَرَّاءَ مُضِرَّةٍ وَّلَا فِتْنَةٍ مُّضِلَّةٍ۔" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0116 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1191.88 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0117 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 116 ;
    minaret:startTime 1181.96 ;
    minaret:text "number four: give sadaqah. Try to give daily sadaqah while you're there. So take some extra money with you, and then Insha'Allah try to give as much sadaqah as" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0117 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1201.86 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0118 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 117 ;
    minaret:startTime 1191.88 ;
    minaret:text "possible to different people, and Insha'Allah may Allah accept all of it from you. And when you're giving daily sadaqah, don't just forget about other" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0118 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1211.88 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0119 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 118 ;
    minaret:startTime 1201.86 ;
    minaret:text "forms of sadaqah. So give money as well for sure, for sure, even if it's not a lot; but give every time you come across someone you think you should give to that person." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0119 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1221.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0120 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 119 ;
    minaret:startTime 1211.88 ;
    minaret:text "Otherwise you can buy meals and give people meals. A lot of people are waiting there hungry and it's very hard for them to go and grab food. So if you notice someone" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0120 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1236.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0121 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 120 ;
    minaret:startTime 1221.78 ;
    minaret:text "who's hungry sitting outside the masjid and is not even able to go inside for whatever reason—sometimes there are some restrictions, children sometimes are not allowed to go to the masjid so the mothers they have to wait outside with the kids—so Insha'Allah if you have some snacks you can share with them." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0121 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1247.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0122 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 121 ;
    minaret:startTime 1236.62 ;
    minaret:text "You can give them energy bars, you can give them food packs, whatever you can, Insha'Allah, that's a very good opportunity while you are going to get a lot of other rewards for your" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0122 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1258.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0123 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 122 ;
    minaret:startTime 1247.76 ;
    minaret:text "other types of acts of worship might as well for sadaqah Insha'Allah, and other forms of sadaqah would include giving Hajj gifts. So Insha'Allah your Hajj gift can include method:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0123 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1268.06 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0124 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 123 ;
    minaret:startTime 1258.02 ;
    minaret:text "how to perform Hajj. Because sadly it has been seen many people—not few, many people—when they reach there, they don't know what to do and they're just relying on their groups," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0124 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1278.34 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0125 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 124 ;
    minaret:startTime 1268.06 ;
    minaret:text "they're relying on their agents, they're relying on their group leads, they're relying on their scholars. It's good that you have a group lead, it's good that you have a good group you're with, but" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0125 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1288.7 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0126 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 125 ;
    minaret:startTime 1278.34 ;
    minaret:text "you also need to know what to do, because sometimes people actually do get lost there from their group, and then they're very lost because they were just relying on their" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0126 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1298.9 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0127 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 126 ;
    minaret:startTime 1288.7 ;
    minaret:text "leads; if leads are not there, then they are lost. So it's good that we know. But let's say the people around us, if they don't know, we can give them small pamphlets of authentic" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0127 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1308.92 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0128 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 127 ;
    minaret:startTime 1298.9 ;
    minaret:text "ones: how to perform Hajj and whatnot. That would be a very beneficial gift. Also the du'a books are a very good idea; make sure they're authentic du'as. So Insha'Allah whatever you share, it should" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0128 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1319.4 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0129 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 128 ;
    minaret:startTime 1308.92 ;
    minaret:text "be authentic. So sometimes it's not allowed for us to share literature inside the masjid, but it's okay to share outside the masjid or it's okay to share with the people you know. So" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0129 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1328.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0130 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 129 ;
    minaret:startTime 1319.4 ;
    minaret:text "the people who are with you in your group, or the people who are from your country, or the people you're friends with, or new friends you make at the masjid. So Insha'Allah you can" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0130 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1338.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0131 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 130 ;
    minaret:startTime 1328.46 ;
    minaret:text "share such information with them, such gifts with them. And other things you can also give them, not just the books, but Insha'Allah anything else you buy from there you can give it to them; you can buy from your" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0131 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1348.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0132 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 131 ;
    minaret:startTime 1338.52 ;
    minaret:text "homeland or wherever you're living and you can take the stuff with you and you give them as gifts. Also you will see that even though Zamzam water is right there, but you know some people are" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0132 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1354.2 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0133 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 132 ;
    minaret:startTime 1348.52 ;
    minaret:text "so old and you know sometimes it's very tiring to go to the cooler, get the water. So what you can" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0133 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1373.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0134 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 133 ;
    minaret:startTime 1354.2 ;
    minaret:text "do is whenever you go drink Zamzam water, you can just take some extra and then extra back to your row or anywhere you see some elderly ladies or elderly men, if you're a brother, then you can Insha'Allah share that water with them, and that will be Insha'Allah another act of charity on your behalf. Very interesting" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0135 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1396.98 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0136 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 135 ;
    minaret:startTime 1387.14 ;
    minaret:text "And then point number five: ask for forgiveness often in the morning and evening. Why? Because istighfar makes things easy, isn't it? So Insha'Allah don't ever" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0136 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1407.04 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0137 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 136 ;
    minaret:startTime 1396.98 ;
    minaret:text "forget to ask for forgiveness. Don't ever think that: 'I'm here because I'm so noble and so holy; rest of the family members they never got a chance or they didn't get a chance" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0137 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1416.9 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0138 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 137 ;
    minaret:startTime 1407.04 ;
    minaret:text "this year, so I'm better.' Never ever, right? So don't ever become arrogant and always stay humble and keep asking Allah for forgiveness, that" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0138 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1422.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0139 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 138 ;
    minaret:startTime 1416.9 ;
    minaret:text "you know, with all our faults, with all our shortcomings, still" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0139 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1428.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0140 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 139 ;
    minaret:startTime 1422.58 ;
    minaret:text "Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala invited us, so O Allah forgive us, because we can make mistakes there as well," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0140 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1433.96 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0141 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 140 ;
    minaret:startTime 1428.02 ;
    minaret:text "so we need to keep asking Allah for forgiveness. When you're asking for forgiveness, when you're saying, then" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0141 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1436.92 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0142 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 141 ;
    minaret:startTime 1433.96 ;
    minaret:text "Astaghfirullah, or Allahummaghfirli, or Rabbighfirli," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0142 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1446.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0143 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 142 ;
    minaret:startTime 1436.92 ;
    minaret:text "think about your shortcomings, think about your faults, think about your sins, and then remember the blessings and the benefits of istighfar when" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0144 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1463.26 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0145 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 144 ;
    minaret:startTime 1456.76 ;
    minaret:text "So where do we stand when we try to compare ourselves with this amazing action of our Prophet?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0145 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1474.24 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0146 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 145 ;
    minaret:startTime 1464.24 ;
    minaret:text "So 'Astaghfirullah' is the easiest way to ask Allah for forgiveness, but Alhamdulillah there are many beautiful adhkar, many beautiful du'as to ask Allah for forgiveness. So" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0150 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1515.08 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0151 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 150 ;
    minaret:startTime 1514.44 ;
    minaret:text "O" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0151 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1526.56 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0152 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 151 ;
    minaret:startTime 1516.58 ;
    minaret:text "Allah, You are the Foremost and the Final; there is no deity except You. Such a beautiful du'a, Alhamdulillah, from Sahih Muslim. So if you can memorize it, you" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0152 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1534.5 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0153 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 152 ;
    minaret:startTime 1526.56 ;
    minaret:text "can make it anywhere, it's not just for Hajj. It's just a beautiful way to ask Allah for forgiveness. And you all must have heard about Sayyid al-Istighfar, the" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0153 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1547.74 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0154 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 153 ;
    minaret:startTime 1535.14 ;
    minaret:text "Chief of Istighfar. I hope you all already make it every morning and every evening, so Insha'Allah that's a very beautiful du'a for forgiveness. Point number six: bring yourself in" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0157 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1602.06 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0158 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 157 ;
    minaret:startTime 1588.1 ;
    minaret:text "اَلْحَجُّ اَشْهُرٌ مَّعْلُوْمٰتٌ ۚ Hajj is during well-known months. Which months are the Hajj months? Also Shawwal is a Hajj month, which is this month, the current month. Actually it is over in some of the countries, so it's already Dhul-Qa'dah. So" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0161 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1647.0 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0162 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 161 ;
    minaret:startTime 1638.6 ;
    minaret:text "things to pack are taqwa and sabr, before anything else, because you will need that at every step; you will need that a lot." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0162 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1657.9 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0163 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 162 ;
    minaret:startTime 1647.8999999999999 ;
    minaret:text "And you know your sabr is tested at every level. Your sabr is tested starting from the day when you make the intention to go for Hajj, SubhanAllah. Many things happen," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0163 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1668.18 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0164 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 163 ;
    minaret:startTime 1657.9 ;
    minaret:text "and you know things happen which never happened before; very new situations you come across. It's a test for you that" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0164 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1678.18 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0165 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 164 ;
    minaret:startTime 1668.18 ;
    minaret:text "how good you are, how much you can handle. And SubhanAllah, sabr is required at every level: at when your flights are delayed, when the" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0165 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1689.88 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0166 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 165 ;
    minaret:startTime 1679.82 ;
    minaret:text "food is not that yum, or when you start comparing your package with other people's packages, when you start comparing your Mina tent with other people's Mina tents, when" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0166 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1699.88 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0167 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 166 ;
    minaret:startTime 1689.88 ;
    minaret:text "you start comparing this with that, then of course it will be a lot of chaos. So first of all remember: we are not going there to find out who got the" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0167 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1705.08 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0168 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 167 ;
    minaret:startTime 1699.88 ;
    minaret:text "best package, all right? And also remember: we are not going there to see who is doing what." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0168 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1715.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0169 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 168 ;
    minaret:startTime 1705.72 ;
    minaret:text "You're required to do sabr, and sabr requires so many things from you. Your focus: Insha'Allah if you're focused, Insha'Allah you will be able to do" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0169 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1725.96 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0170 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 169 ;
    minaret:startTime 1715.72 ;
    minaret:text "sabr. If you have goals, then Insha'Allah you won't waste your life away there, because sabr is also on obedience. So stay obedient there. Sabr is" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0170 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1731.32 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0171 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 170 ;
    minaret:startTime 1725.96 ;
    minaret:text "also staying away from disobedience, so you will Insha'Allah try your best to avoid" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0171 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1741.34 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0172 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 171 ;
    minaret:startTime 1731.3200000000002 ;
    minaret:text "anything which is wrong and haram. You will remove extra things from your phone, you will not even get involved in anything which is unnecessary. There's" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0172 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1751.48 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0173 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 172 ;
    minaret:startTime 1741.34 ;
    minaret:text "no need to argue, there's no need to fight; that's not the place, that's not the time, Insha'Allah. And taqwa: taqwa Insha'Allah will help you make" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0173 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1758.8 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0174 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 173 ;
    minaret:startTime 1751.48 ;
    minaret:text "the matters easy for you, as it comes in Surah at-Talaq: and whoever fears Allah, whoever has taqwa of Allah," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0175 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1771.74 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0176 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 175 ;
    minaret:startTime 1761.3600000000001 ;
    minaret:text "Allah will make his matters easy. And Allah will also make ways out for such a person who has taqwa. So how will you implement taqwa there? That" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0176 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1782.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0177 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 176 ;
    minaret:startTime 1771.74 ;
    minaret:text "you will remind yourself that Allah is watching. You will remind yourself that even if my group people are not around, even if my group leader is not watching me, Allah is watching; I cannot do wrong." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0177 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1793.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0178 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 177 ;
    minaret:startTime 1783.66 ;
    minaret:text "If people around me are unknown to me, I still cannot be mean to them, I still cannot hurt them and harm them, because Allah is watching me. And I cannot" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0178 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1804.0 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0179 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 178 ;
    minaret:startTime 1793.46 ;
    minaret:text "gossip and backbite, because Allah is watching me, Insha'Allah. So all of this is going to make matters very easy for you. Another beautiful du'a from Surah Al-Mu'minoon, ayah number 29:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0179 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1806.74 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0180 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 179 ;
    minaret:startTime 1804.0 ;
    minaret:text "رَبِّ اَنْزِلْنِیْ مُنْزَلًا مُّبٰرَكًا وَّاَنْتَ خَیْرُ الْمُنْزِلِیْنَ ۟" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0181 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1820.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0182 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 181 ;
    minaret:startTime 1809.58 ;
    minaret:text "Lord, let me land at a blessed landing place, and You are the best to accommodate us.' SubhanAllah. So this du'a is very beautiful for any new place:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0186 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1874.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0187 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 186 ;
    minaret:startTime 1860.5600000000002 ;
    minaret:text "wasiyah, right? What is wasiyah? What is will? Will is something which we should write anyways, right? Especially before going for Hajj, because we are doing a very noble task and we don't want to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0187 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1876.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0188 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 187 ;
    minaret:startTime 1874.02 ;
    minaret:text "leave away any duty which is, you know," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0188 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1886.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0189 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 188 ;
    minaret:startTime 1876.46 ;
    minaret:text "on us. So Insha'Allah a proper legal will which is workable in your country wherever you are. So Insha'Allah find a way, ask" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0189 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1895.34 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0190 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 189 ;
    minaret:startTime 1886.52 ;
    minaret:text "around, ask the people like: how did they do it? How did they do it for Muslims? And Insha'Allah do it accordingly. And then comes our ninth point:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0190 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1906.24 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0191 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 190 ;
    minaret:startTime 1895.98 ;
    minaret:text "make a du'a diary and start writing your du'as in it. Why do we need to make a du'a diary? Why can't we just use masnoon du'as and Qur'anic du'as?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0191 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1918.6 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0192 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 191 ;
    minaret:startTime 1907.0 ;
    minaret:text "They're amazing for sure, they cover pretty much everything anyways; but you know, we have a lot of our own customized du'as, isn't it? We have a lot of desires, wishes, goals, aspirations." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0192 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1929.42 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0193 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 192 ;
    minaret:startTime 1919.3999999999999 ;
    minaret:text "We want to do so much in life, isn't it? So how about we ask Allah to fulfill all of our goals? So the easiest way to make" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0193 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1939.56 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0194 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 193 ;
    minaret:startTime 1929.42 ;
    minaret:text "a beautiful—and you can see a long—list of du'as is that first make a list of your goals. Make a list of your life goals, make a list of" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0194 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1945.2 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0195 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 194 ;
    minaret:startTime 1939.56 ;
    minaret:text "your spiritual goals, your health goals, your financial goals," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0195 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1955.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0196 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 195 ;
    minaret:startTime 1945.2 ;
    minaret:text "all types of goals. So once you make a very long list of all your goals, now turn all those goals into du'as. For example, you" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0196 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1968.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0197 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 196 ;
    minaret:startTime 1955.46 ;
    minaret:text "have a goal to go for Hajj, right? So how are you going to turn it into a du'a? 'O Allah, call me for Hajj,' right? Any language, whatever is easy for you. You also make it interesting. So let's say some sisters are" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0197 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1975.2 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0198 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 197 ;
    minaret:startTime 1968.02 ;
    minaret:text "making du'a to get married as well, and they also want to go for Hajj, and they also want money. So if they just combine all three," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0198 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1985.18 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0199 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 198 ;
    minaret:startTime 1975.2 ;
    minaret:text "it will become a very nice du'a that: 'O Allah, enable me to go for Hajj Mabroor with my righteous husband,' right? Or with my righteous wife, if there's a brother" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0199 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1996.16 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0200 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 199 ;
    minaret:startTime 1985.18 ;
    minaret:text "who's making du'a for such. So this is how we're going to turn du'as—this is how we're going to turn our goals and aspirations and wishes and desires into du'as, because we can ask Allah for everything, and Allah" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0200 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1997.4 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0201 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 200 ;
    minaret:startTime 1996.16 ;
    minaret:text "can grant all our wishes. So why not ask Him, especially when we are going to be there exclusively for Him," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0201 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2005.9 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0202 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 201 ;
    minaret:startTime 1997.4 ;
    minaret:text "worshipping Him day in and day out, worshipping Him throughout the day, and trying our best to stay away from all haram? Then Insha'Allah this will be an amazing thing. Now Alhamdulillah there are some suggestions" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0202 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2019.14 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0203 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 202 ;
    minaret:startTime 2006.52 ;
    minaret:text "that how you can make some du'as for Hajj and you can include them in your du'a list. You can also make your own. So a few of them are: 'O Allah, make every good deed" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0203 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2030.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0204 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 203 ;
    minaret:startTime 2020.34 ;
    minaret:text "of mine purely for You, and place no share for anyone in it.' So total exclusive worship and deed for Allah—this is what we want. Everything we do is only for Allah, not for any other" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0204 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2044.28 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0205 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 204 ;
    minaret:startTime 2030.44 ;
    minaret:text "reason." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0205 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2077.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0206 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 205 ;
    minaret:startTime 2044.28 ;
    minaret:text "Another du'a: 'O Allah, grant me opportunity and call me to perform Hajj.' So let's just turn into us so that we all benefit: 'O Allah, grant us opportunity and call us to perform Hajj Mabroor, Ameen. O Allah, facilitate everything for us, remove all hindrances, and put ease in our journeys for Your pleasure, Ameen. Ya Allah, O Allah, we have intended to perform Hajj, make it easy for us to perform it, accepted and blessed, Ameen.'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0206 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2086.26 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0207 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 206 ;
    minaret:startTime 2077.72 ;
    minaret:text "'O Allah, make us among those who will do tawaf of Your House this year, Ameen.' This is a beautiful du'a, right?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0207 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2096.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0208 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 207 ;
    minaret:startTime 2087.1 ;
    minaret:text "These are just personal du'as; we don't need Arabic for them, right? So whichever language you speak, you can just make these du'as. These are not masnoon du'as, these are personal du'as." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0208 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2108.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0209 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 208 ;
    minaret:startTime 2096.94 ;
    minaret:text "So these are just some ideas; you can also make your own Insha'Allah. 'O Allah, forgive our sins, big and small, major and minor, and save us from negligence in the matters of our deeds.'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0209 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2115.66 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0210 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 209 ;
    minaret:startTime 2109.42 ;
    minaret:text "So save us from negligence in the matters of our deeds. 'O Allah, bless us with the ability to perform Hajj Mabroor.'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0228 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2301.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0229 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 228 ;
    minaret:startTime 2291.52 ;
    minaret:text "about Hajj, because knowledge about Hajj will help us perform Hajj beautifully, as you all mentioned initially, SubhanAllah. So when we seek knowledge about" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0229 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2308.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0230 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 229 ;
    minaret:startTime 2301.58 ;
    minaret:text "Hajj, how are we going to do that? So Alhamdulillah one is that you guys are taking this course, that's beautiful, brilliant, may Allah reward you." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0230 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2321.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0231 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 230 ;
    minaret:startTime 2308.58 ;
    minaret:text "May Allah enable us to convey the correct knowledge to you, may Allah enable us to only convey the Haqq, Ameen, and may Allah forgive us for our shortcomings. So when we have the knowledge, knowledge brings confidence in us and we're" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0231 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2331.48 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0232 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 231 ;
    minaret:startTime 2321.52 ;
    minaret:text "able to fulfill our rites of this beautiful worship in a better way, and then we don't have any regrets. Because it has been seen that many people when" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0232 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2340.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0233 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 232 ;
    minaret:startTime 2331.48 ;
    minaret:text "they come back from Hajj have a lot of regrets; they're like: 'Oh, I didn't do that. Oh, no one ever told me that. Oh, I missed that step.' And SubhanAllah, it's too late to go back and fix" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0233 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2351.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0234 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 233 ;
    minaret:startTime 2340.72 ;
    minaret:text "it many times, right? So Insha'Allah when we have the knowledge, when we make our own notes—if you're going for Hajj this year, I would highly recommend that from this course make your own" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0234 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2365.92 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0235 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 234 ;
    minaret:startTime 2351.52 ;
    minaret:text "maps, make your own Hajj day planners. This will really help you because it's your own writing or it's your own typing, so you would know what you were trying to do. Because many times when you are just holding the books their first time when you" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0235 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2381.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0236 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 235 ;
    minaret:startTime 2365.92 ;
    minaret:text "are at Hajj and you are asking people: 'Oh please give me a book, please give me a book,' and you open it, a lot of time you're lost about some points because you never understood that point. When you never understood that point, how can you now implement it? You know what I mean? So Alhamdulillah that's a very good" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0236 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2391.4 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0237 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 236 ;
    minaret:startTime 2381.52 ;
    minaret:text "step by you if you're taking this course. Even if you're not going this year, please make your planners; whenever you go, you can take them along. Let's say you're not going this year, but someone in your family," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0237 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2397.12 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0238 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 237 ;
    minaret:startTime 2391.4 ;
    minaret:text "someone from your friends, they're going for Hajj. So how about you do this for them? You can also help them" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0238 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2411.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0239 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 238 ;
    minaret:startTime 2397.12 ;
    minaret:text "prepare. So that is the goal for these courses: the course in Urdu by Ustadha Dr. Farhat Hashmi, we're going to try to translate it starting from tomorrow Insha'Allah, right? So today we are covering whatever Sister Shazia taught us" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0239 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2423.24 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0240 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 239 ;
    minaret:startTime 2411.52 ;
    minaret:text "last week about the orientation day of this course, but Insha'Allah from tomorrow onwards we're going to try to translate whatever Dr. Farhat Hashmi teaches in Urdu, we're going to translate in English." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0240 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2434.82 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0241 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 240 ;
    minaret:startTime 2424.7000000000003 ;
    minaret:text "So anyone who doesn't understand Urdu can join this. If you can understand Urdu, it's highly recommended that you learn from a scholar, all right? Okay, let's" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0241 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2444.8 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0242 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 241 ;
    minaret:startTime 2434.82 ;
    minaret:text "move on. So how are we going to gain knowledge apart from this course? Insha'Allah there are a lot of books: there are some Darussalam books, there are some Al-Huda books. Insha'Allah we highly" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0242 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2454.88 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0243 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 242 ;
    minaret:startTime 2444.8 ;
    minaret:text "recommend you to get these books and start reading them and listen to them. And if you are not going for Hajj, please whenever you're giving these as gifts, one tip: you can highlight" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0243 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2464.86 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0244 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 243 ;
    minaret:startTime 2454.88 ;
    minaret:text "some points. That really, really helps. This book is very amazing and very short and very easy to carry. So if anyone is going for Hajj" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0244 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2476.0 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0245 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 244 ;
    minaret:startTime 2464.86 ;
    minaret:text "or Umrah, you can get this book, you can highlight some points, you can actually go and show them that: 'I have highlighted these points for you,' because a lot of times people miss these. So that would be a big favor that you" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0269 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2749.96 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0270 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 269 ;
    minaret:startTime 2736.54 ;
    minaret:text "our proper beginning. So where is Hajj mentioned in the Qur'an? Many times, but a lot of ayat and steps are mentioned in Surah Al-Baqarah, right in the beginning SubhanAllah, where we have learned about:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0271 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2774.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0272 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 271 ;
    minaret:startTime 2765.3799999999997 ;
    minaret:text "okay, secondly, performing Hajj rituals without any deficiency, right? Without reducing anything, that's completion;" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0272 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2788.04 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0273 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 272 ;
    minaret:startTime 2775.2400000000002 ;
    minaret:text "that's how we're going to complete it. And then leaving home with the intention of Hajj and Umrah only, nothing else, nothing else, only for that. And completing Hajj and Umrah after making an intention for them," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0273 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2797.74 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0274 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 273 ;
    minaret:startTime 2789.06 ;
    minaret:text "Insha'Allah. So may Allah enable us to complete this intention, because Alhamdulillah many of us are intending to go, so may Allah enable us to complete. So" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0274 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2803.48 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0275 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 274 ;
    minaret:startTime 2797.74 ;
    minaret:text "complete it. So what's the definition? We're going to Insha'Allah cover definition tomorrow as well, but just for now a little bit of it: so" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0275 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2810.86 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0276 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 275 ;
    minaret:startTime 2803.48 ;
    minaret:text "what's the literal meaning of Hajj and Umrah? Literal meaning, the dictionary meaning of Umrah is to visit a populated place," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0276 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2823.74 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0277 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 276 ;
    minaret:startTime 2811.72 ;
    minaret:text "and literal meaning of Hajj is to intend to go to a respectable thing, SubhanAllah, right? So both are to do with journey, both are to do with place, both are to visit," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0277 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2834.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0278 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 277 ;
    minaret:startTime 2824.3 ;
    minaret:text "SubhanAllah. So what is the shar'i meaning? Istilahi meaning is for Umrah: to visit Allah's House in a special manner. And Hajj" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0278 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2847.22 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0279 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 278 ;
    minaret:startTime 2834.44 ;
    minaret:text "is visiting special places on the specified days to do special acts of worship. Visiting special places on the specified days to do special acts of worship," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0279 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2852.18 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0280 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 279 ;
    minaret:startTime 2847.98 ;
    minaret:text "SubhanAllah, right? So it's not only just going to Ka'bah, but other" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0280 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2856.9 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0281 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 280 ;
    minaret:startTime 2852.18 ;
    minaret:text "places as well: other places including Mina, Muzdalifah, Arafat," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0281 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2865.34 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0282 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 281 ;
    minaret:startTime 2856.9 ;
    minaret:text "you know about them, right? You have heard about them. Okay, let me ask you a quick question: is a visit to Masjid an-Nabawi part of Hajj or Umrah?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0282 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2878.2 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0283 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 282 ;
    minaret:startTime 2866.02 ;
    minaret:text "No, it's not, right? But why do we go there? Because while we are there, why not we go there, right? And we benefit from Masjid an-Nabawi as well, and we can also enjoy Seerah more when we go there" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0283 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2882.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0284 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 283 ;
    minaret:startTime 2878.2 ;
    minaret:text "and visit places there. And Alhamdulillah there is a place which" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0284 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2892.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0285 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 284 ;
    minaret:startTime 2882.64 ;
    minaret:text "is called Rawdah / Riyad al-Jannah, right? The Garden of Jannah in Masjid an-Nabawi where we can pray and benefit from that, right? It's highly recommended." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0285 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2902.38 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0286 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 285 ;
    minaret:startTime 2892.46 ;
    minaret:text "But if a person is not able to go there, that person's Hajj and Umrah is totally valid, okay? If someone is taking a short trip and has only, let's say, two days or in" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0286 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2917.3 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0287 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 286 ;
    minaret:startTime 2902.38 ;
    minaret:text "transit reaches Jeddah, that person can go to Makkah perform Umrah, come back; that person doesn't need to go to Madinah in order for his Umrah to be valid, all right? So that's something to remember Insha'Allah. So Hajj is a very" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0289 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2953.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0290 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 289 ;
    minaret:startTime 2942.98 ;
    minaret:text "worship; we need this worship. We need to fulfill this due of Allah, it's Allah's right we need to fulfill. Rasulullah gave" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0291 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2969.1 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0292 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 291 ;
    minaret:startTime 2962.76 ;
    minaret:text "So it's a command of Allah, and also Rasulullah commanded us to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0293 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2985.98 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0294 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 293 ;
    minaret:startTime 2980.0 ;
    minaret:text "What do you think about that person's state of iman? It is not considered complete." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0294 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2996.68 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0295 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 294 ;
    minaret:startTime 2986.88 ;
    minaret:text "The one who doesn't believe that Hajj is mandatory, that person is not even considered a Muslim. So may Allah save us and protect us from these weird" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0295 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3004.7 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0296 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 295 ;
    minaret:startTime 2996.68 ;
    minaret:text "ideas. Not even low, it doesn't count, because remember Hajj is a pillar of Islam; one pillar is missing, the person's Islam is" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0296 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3009.92 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0297 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 296 ;
    minaret:startTime 3004.7 ;
    minaret:text "missing. And Ibn Umar Radiyallahu Anhuma, the son of Umar Radiyallahu Anhu," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0297 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3019.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0298 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 297 ;
    minaret:startTime 3009.92 ;
    minaret:text "he said there is no one upon him except Hajj and Umrah, like everyone is supposed to do that. Again, it depends on if a person is able to afford it" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0302 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3062.1 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0303 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 302 ;
    minaret:startTime 3052.12 ;
    minaret:text "And we should not delay Hajj for petty reasons, we should not delay Hajj for worldly reasons, we should not delay Hajj once" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0303 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3076.26 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0304 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 303 ;
    minaret:startTime 3062.1 ;
    minaret:text "we can afford it. That's it, Hajj is mandatory on us. So let's say you were not that rich back then, but now Allah has given you enough: the moment you get enough, then Insha'Allah you should plan your Hajj journey. So we learned from Musnad Ahmad" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0304 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3079.26 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0305 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 304 ;
    minaret:startTime 3076.88 ;
    minaret:text "that Rasulullah said:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0307 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3102.38 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0308 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 307 ;
    minaret:startTime 3092.58 ;
    minaret:text "one knows what will happen to the world: COVID can happen, right? And anything and everything can get stopped, and the people with a lot of money, they" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0308 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3107.96 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0309 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 308 ;
    minaret:startTime 3102.38 ;
    minaret:text "were also not able to go for Hajj; the people with full health, they were not able to go for Hajj. So we" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0311 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3138.3 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0312 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 311 ;
    minaret:startTime 3133.08 ;
    minaret:text "go and fulfill this obligation. And SubhanAllah we also know about the benefit of Hajj and Umrah:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0319 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3217.14 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0320 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 319 ;
    minaret:startTime 3207.2 ;
    minaret:text "for very weird reasons: some people delay their Hajj because they want to enjoy their life to the fullest first; some people delay their Hajj because they think they need to get their" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0320 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3224.28 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0321 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 320 ;
    minaret:startTime 3217.14 ;
    minaret:text "kids married, then they can go for Hajj; some people think that Hajj should be done only when they are old. But who said so?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0321 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3235.24 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0322 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 321 ;
    minaret:startTime 3224.96 ;
    minaret:text "Hajj is for when you are rich enough, whenever you are rich enough, that's all. So you don't have to delay it and you should not delay it, and you should fulfill this obligation the way you fulfill your" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0322 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3251.9 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0323 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 322 ;
    minaret:startTime 3235.24 ;
    minaret:text "other obligations. Because when salah time comes, you don't say: 'I'm gonna pray salah when all my kids are married.' You don't say: 'I'm gonna pray salah when all my important tasks are done.' You don't say that: 'I'm gonna pray salah when, you know, I'm done with all my sins" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0331 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3345.0 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 331 ;
    minaret:startTime 3330.16 ;
    minaret:text "Right, so let's make du'a together: سُبْحَانَكَ اللّٰهُمَّ وَبِحَمْدِكَ، اَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَّاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ، اَسْتَغْفِرُكَ وَاَتُوْبُ اِلَیْكَ۔ بَارَكَ اللّٰهُ فِیْكُمْ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكُمْ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهُ۔" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0015 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 175.92 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0016 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 15 ;
    minaret:startTime 160.92 ;
    minaret:text "the ones who cannot go, they keep wishing and yearning for it. So, let's see what the Qur'an tells us about Hajj, verse 1: اِنَّ اَوَّلَ بَیْتٍ وُّضِعَ لِلنَّاسِ لَلَّذِیْ بِبَكَّةَ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0016 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 186.34 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0017 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 16 ;
    minaret:startTime 176.98 ;
    minaret:text "مُبٰرَكًا وَّهُدًی لِّلْعٰلَمِیْنَ ۟ۚ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0017 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 197.28 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0018 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 17 ;
    minaret:startTime 188.04 ;
    minaret:text "فِیْهِ اٰیٰتٌۢ بَیِّنٰتٌ مَّقَامُ اِبْرٰهِیْمَ ۚ۬" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0018 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 207.98 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0019 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 18 ;
    minaret:startTime 197.28 ;
    minaret:text "وَمَنْ دَخَلَهٗ كَانَ اٰمِنًا ؕ وَلِلّٰهِ عَلَی النَّاسِ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0019 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 212.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0020 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 19 ;
    minaret:startTime 207.98 ;
    minaret:text "حِجُّ الْبَیْتِ مَنِ اسْتَطَاعَ اِلَیْهِ سَبِیْلًا ؕ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0020 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 222.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0021 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 20 ;
    minaret:startTime 214.56 ;
    minaret:text "وَمَنْ كَفَرَ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَنِیٌّ عَنِ الْعٰلَمِیْنَ ۟" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0042 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 453.26 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0043 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 42 ;
    minaret:startTime 443.32 ;
    minaret:text "So, when did the Hajj begin? So, let's just talk about the beginning of Hajj a bit. So, Hajj actually began or the Baytullah was actually there since" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0043 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 463.26 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0044 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 43 ;
    minaret:startTime 453.26 ;
    minaret:text "the time of Adam A.S. It was built by angels first, and all the prophets that we know of performed Hajj. And of" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0044 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 475.48 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0045 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 44 ;
    minaret:startTime 463.26 ;
    minaret:text "course we learn about a few prophets which are mentioned exclusively in the Qur'an to do with Baytullah and Hajj. So, let's look at this narration which gives us an idea that other prophets were also doing Hajj and whatnot." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0045 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 482.0 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0046 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 45 ;
    minaret:startTime 476.21999999999997 ;
    minaret:text "So, Abu Al-A'aliyah narrated on the authority of Ibn Abbas that Rasulullah" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0046 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 492.74 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0047 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 46 ;
    minaret:startTime 482.71999999999997 ;
    minaret:text "passed through the valley of Azraq and he asked, 'Which valley is this?' Sahaba said, 'This is the valley of Azraq.' And he observed and he" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0047 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 502.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0048 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 47 ;
    minaret:startTime 492.74 ;
    minaret:text "said, 'I perceive as if I'm seeing Musa coming down from the mountain track, and he's calling upon Allah loudly saying Talbiyah,' right?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0048 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 509.7 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0049 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 48 ;
    minaret:startTime 502.62 ;
    minaret:text "saying, 'Here I am at Your service.' Then he came to the mountain track of Harsha; he asked," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0049 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 520.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0050 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 49 ;
    minaret:startTime 510.46 ;
    minaret:text "'Which is this mountain track?' They said, 'It is the mountain track of Harsha.' He said, 'I feel as if I'm seeing Yunus on a well-" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0050 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 530.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0051 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 50 ;
    minaret:startTime 520.94 ;
    minaret:text "built red camel with the cloak of wool around him, and the rein of his camel is made of the fibers of date palm," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0051 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 540.9 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0052 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 51 ;
    minaret:startTime 530.72 ;
    minaret:text "and he's calling upon Allah with Talbiyah.' So, this is what Rasulullah told Sahaba. So, this shows that even Yunus and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0052 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 550.8 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0053 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 52 ;
    minaret:startTime 540.9 ;
    minaret:text "Musa performed their Hajj. And we learn about Ibrahim and Ismail when they actually raised" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0053 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 560.5 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0054 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 53 ;
    minaret:startTime 550.8 ;
    minaret:text "the Kaaba, right? And mentioned when Ibrahim was raising the foundations of the house with his son Ismail, saying—what were they saying?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0054 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 570.42 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0055 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 54 ;
    minaret:startTime 560.5 ;
    minaret:text "رَبَّنَا تَقَبَّلْ مِنَّا ؕ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ السَّمِیْعُ الْعَلِیْمُ. Even though they were doing this amazing task, this noble act of worship building the house of" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0057 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 600.96 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0058 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 57 ;
    minaret:startTime 590.72 ;
    minaret:text "مُسْلِمَیْنِ لَكَ. 'Our Lord, and make us Muslims in submission to You, and from our descendants a Muslim nation in submission to You, and show us our rites like" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0058 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 611.22 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0059 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 58 ;
    minaret:startTime 600.96 ;
    minaret:text "teach us how to worship, and accept our repentance, indeed You are the Accepting of repentance, the Merciful.' SubhanAllah, this is a very beautiful" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0059 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 621.34 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0060 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 59 ;
    minaret:startTime 611.22 ;
    minaret:text "example of: they did what they could, but they wanted Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala's acceptance; they did not rely on their actions." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0060 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 631.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0061 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 60 ;
    minaret:startTime 621.34 ;
    minaret:text "They did what they could, they did the best, but they were now asking Allah for help—such a beautiful example for us. And we also learn about Ibrahim" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0061 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 641.42 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0062 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 61 ;
    minaret:startTime 631.64 ;
    minaret:text "that once he was done building the Kaaba, he was commanded by Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala to call the people. And from a narration, from a hadith, we learned that Ibrahim" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0062 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 651.32 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0063 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 62 ;
    minaret:startTime 641.42 ;
    minaret:text "was concerned: 'Who's going to come here?' Because the Kaaba was built in just a very barren area, not very many people used to live around" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0063 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 661.34 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0064 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 63 ;
    minaret:startTime 651.32 ;
    minaret:text "there. So, he was very concerned: 'We have built it, but who's going to come?' So, Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala He gave a very beautiful command, He said: 'And proclaim to the" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0064 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 671.3 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0065 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 64 ;
    minaret:startTime 661.34 ;
    minaret:text "people the Hajj, they will come to you on foot and on every lean camel, they will come from every distant pass.' So, the job is only to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0065 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 681.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0066 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 65 ;
    minaret:startTime 671.3 ;
    minaret:text "give a call, just call, and people will come. Our job is not the result, our job is our effort—that" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0066 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 691.6 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0067 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 66 ;
    minaret:startTime 681.72 ;
    minaret:text "is something we learned from this verse. And that is exactly what Ibrahim did when he called. Maybe for a few years not a lot of people turned" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0067 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 701.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0068 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 67 ;
    minaret:startTime 691.6 ;
    minaret:text "up, maybe no one turned up—we don't have those details, right? But what we know is there were not a lot of people there. But SubhanAllah now when we" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0068 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 713.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0069 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 68 ;
    minaret:startTime 701.64 ;
    minaret:text "all go, we are actually doing what? We are actually responding to the call of Ibrahim when he called us for Hajj. So, may Allah enable us to accept this call and respond to it!" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0074 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 779.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0075 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 74 ;
    minaret:startTime 767.7199999999999 ;
    minaret:text "we learn that Rasulullah Sallallahu Alayhi wa Sallam was asked about the masjid which was first set up on the earth. He Sallallahu Alayhi wa Sallam responded: 'It was Al-Masjid al-Haram.'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0075 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 790.24 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0076 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 75 ;
    minaret:startTime 780.24 ;
    minaret:text "Then he was asked, 'Which one was the next after that?' So, he said, 'Al-Masjid al-Aqsa.' So, the first masjid: Masjid al-Haram on the face of the" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0080 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 846.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0081 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 80 ;
    minaret:startTime 836.5600000000001 ;
    minaret:text "understandings from different tafaseer. Also in this verse we learn that Makkah is Mubarak. What does that mean? So, we're going to Insha'Allah learn" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0081 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 856.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0082 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 81 ;
    minaret:startTime 846.44 ;
    minaret:text "about 10 different points—there can be so many different points about Makkah being Mubarak, but Insha'Allah we're going to learn about 10 points for our today's session." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0082 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 866.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0083 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 82 ;
    minaret:startTime 856.36 ;
    minaret:text "First one: why is Makkah Mubarak? Because Rasulullah, he was sent there, revelation started there, the best Shariah which was given to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0083 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 877.7 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0084 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 83 ;
    minaret:startTime 866.36 ;
    minaret:text "the mankind was descended there first, right? It started off from there, SubhanAllah. And another reason that Makkah is Mubarak is because it's always busy with worship." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0084 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 888.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0085 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 84 ;
    minaret:startTime 878.84 ;
    minaret:text "Isn't it, SubhanAllah? No matter when you turn the TV on—and before COVID it was like very crowded, SubhanAllah—so it's always busy with worship, that's why it's Mubarak." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0085 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 898.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0086 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 85 ;
    minaret:startTime 888.72 ;
    minaret:text "And the reward of worship in Makkah is many times more. So, it's just all sorts of worship, not just salah, remember that. Scholars" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0086 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 908.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0087 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 86 ;
    minaret:startTime 898.64 ;
    minaret:text "say that every act of worship you get more reward for that in Makkah, SubhanAllah. So, that's why it's Mubarak, it's Mubarak land. Whatever you do: you do charity, you" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0087 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 918.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0088 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 87 ;
    minaret:startTime 908.58 ;
    minaret:text "get more rewards; you're nice to people around you, you get more reward; you show sabr there, you get more reward; you avoid sins, you get more reward; you don't harm people, you get more reward;" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0088 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 933.5 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0089 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 88 ;
    minaret:startTime 918.52 ;
    minaret:text "you help people, you get more rewards, SubhanAllah. So, more rewards for the same deeds done elsewhere. And then of course this famous hadith about reward of salah in Masjid al-Haram—let's look at the narration today." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0089 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 944.1 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0090 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 89 ;
    minaret:startTime 934.3 ;
    minaret:text "Rasulullah said: 'And one prayer in the sacred masjid—Al-Masjid al-Haram, which is in Makkah—is better than 100,000" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0090 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 954.42 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0091 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 90 ;
    minaret:startTime 944.1 ;
    minaret:text "prayers elsewhere,' SubhanAllah. So, whenever you get an opportunity, whenever you get a chance, please don't ever miss any salah in Masjid al-Haram." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0091 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 964.12 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0092 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 91 ;
    minaret:startTime 954.42 ;
    minaret:text "So, some people sometimes, you know, they kind of go around for ziyarat at salah timings—that's not a good idea. So, Insha'Allah you can always pick after Isha time" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0092 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 973.92 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0093 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 92 ;
    minaret:startTime 964.12 ;
    minaret:text "or maybe after Fajr time to travel if you want to see some other places in Makkah, but come back before the next fard prayer" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0093 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 983.9 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0094 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 93 ;
    minaret:startTime 973.92 ;
    minaret:text "so that you don't miss this amazing opportunity. So, just praying 100,000 prayers—it should not be missed and it should not be ignored, it should not be taken casually. Another" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0094 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 994.1 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0095 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 94 ;
    minaret:startTime 983.9 ;
    minaret:text "reason why Makkah is Mubarak is because we get forgiveness of our sins, we get forgiveness of our sins, SubhanAllah! And it removes" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0095 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1004.12 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0096 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 95 ;
    minaret:startTime 994.1 ;
    minaret:text "poverty every time we go there; it's a means of becoming rich. Interesting, right? Such a beautiful concept: apparently we're spending money, but" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0096 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1013.4 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0097 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 96 ;
    minaret:startTime 1004.12 ;
    minaret:text "what's happening? Barakah in our wealth, because we're going to a Mubarak land! Where's the hadith? From Sahih Ibn Majah we learn:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0098 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1041.32 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0099 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 98 ;
    minaret:startTime 1029.5 ;
    minaret:text "SubhanAllah, just like these bellows they remove the filth, the extras from the iron and purifies it, Hajj and Umrah purify us from our sins." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0099 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1052.96 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0100 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 99 ;
    minaret:startTime 1042.24 ;
    minaret:text "Another reason that Makkah is Mubarak is because we get the reward for every step we take towards it. Let's look at the hadith Rasul said:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0100 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1063.9 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0101 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 100 ;
    minaret:startTime 1053.88 ;
    minaret:text "'Not that—hadith: camel lifts its foot or places its hand except Allah the Exalted writes for him a good deed for it" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0101 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1074.1 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0102 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 101 ;
    minaret:startTime 1063.9 ;
    minaret:text "and removes from him an evil deed, or raises with it his rank,' SubhanAllah. So, with every step what's happening? Good" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0102 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1080.08 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0103 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 102 ;
    minaret:startTime 1074.1 ;
    minaret:text "deed is written, evil deed is removed, or a person is getting a raised rank." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0103 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1090.82 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0104 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 103 ;
    minaret:startTime 1080.74 ;
    minaret:text "So, even if you live really far away from Makkah, whenever you travel you benefit from it. The farther you are, the better it is for you, SubhanAllah, in terms" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0104 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1100.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0105 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 104 ;
    minaret:startTime 1090.82 ;
    minaret:text "of your book of deeds. And then blessed water is there. Which water is that? Which water is called blessed water? And SubhanAllah, it's just mind-blowing" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0105 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1115.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0106 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 105 ;
    minaret:startTime 1100.94 ;
    minaret:text "if you read about it, if you research about it: exactly, Zamzam water! It's blessed water. So, Insha'Allah one tip while we are talking about Zamzam water here: that when you are there, try to drink only Zamzam water, right?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0106 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1131.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0107 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 106 ;
    minaret:startTime 1116.26 ;
    minaret:text "Don't drink any other water because you have access to it and you can drink it. So, what's the point of drinking mineral water there or spring water there when you have Zamzam water there, Insha'Allah? What's the benefit of Zamzam water? Rasulullah was" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0107 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1141.82 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0108 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 107 ;
    minaret:startTime 1131.9199999999998 ;
    minaret:text "heard saying: 'The water of Zamzam is for whatever it is drunk for. If it is drunk for food, it acts as food;" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0108 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1151.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0109 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 108 ;
    minaret:startTime 1141.82 ;
    minaret:text "if it's drunk for quenching one's thirst, it acts like that; if it is drunk for shifa, then it acts as one," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0109 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1161.9 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0110 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 109 ;
    minaret:startTime 1151.76 ;
    minaret:text "like it cures people as well,' SubhanAllah. Yes, of course, we can do wudu with it as well wherever they allow us, right? Because of course when we go to any masjid we" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0110 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1172.18 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0111 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 110 ;
    minaret:startTime 1161.9 ;
    minaret:text "follow their rules; if they allow you, then Insha'Allah you do. Some places outside the masjid they allow you, from inside the masjid, you know, of course we can create a lot of mess there if we do that." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0111 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1186.14 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0112 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 111 ;
    minaret:startTime 1180.98 ;
    minaret:text "opportunities as well. And it's allowed to do business there even when you are on your Hajj trip," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0112 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1197.1 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0113 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 112 ;
    minaret:startTime 1187.4 ;
    minaret:text "given that that is not your main goal, right? Your business is not your main goal, Hajj is your main goal, but you're allowed to do your business there if you want, SubhanAllah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0113 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1208.1 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0114 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 113 ;
    minaret:startTime 1198.04 ;
    minaret:text "And abundance of sustenance is there. If you think about it, Makkah is, you know, it's like a dry land, nothing grows there as such; but" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0114 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1218.06 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0115 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 114 ;
    minaret:startTime 1208.1 ;
    minaret:text "you can find every type of fruit, you can find every type of food, every type of cuisine there. And SubhanAllah a lot of people go there and food doesn't run" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0115 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1225.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0116 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 115 ;
    minaret:startTime 1218.06 ;
    minaret:text "out! And think about water as well, Zamzam water: people have been going ever since, right? Ever" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0116 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1244.6 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0117 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 116 ;
    minaret:startTime 1234.56 ;
    minaret:text "homelands, and Zamzam water has reached pretty much every corner of this earth, yet it is there, yet it keeps coming—a big miracle, isn't" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0117 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1258.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0118 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 117 ;
    minaret:startTime 1244.6 ;
    minaret:text "it, SubhanAllah? Such blessed water! But before COVID situations, people were actually bringing back water as well: some countries allow you to fill your own bottles and bring back, some countries want you to have the packed proper" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0118 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1273.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0119 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 118 ;
    minaret:startTime 1258.96 ;
    minaret:text "bottles from Saudi government. So for that, of course, you have to pay a bit, otherwise it's available everywhere in Haram and also in—they have arranged that Zamzam water reaches, so you can even find it there, SubhanAllah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0121 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1299.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0122 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 121 ;
    minaret:startTime 1290.4799999999998 ;
    minaret:text "SubhanAllah, like it is Allah who provided all of this rizq for the people of Makkah because it was not possible otherwise. So that" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0122 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1320.14 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0123 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 122 ;
    minaret:startTime 1310.08 ;
    minaret:text "according to Shaykh Al-Uthaymeen means people, so it's guidance for the people. And SubhanAllah it is, you know, even when non-Muslims they view the footage of Kaaba," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0123 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1334.96 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0124 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 123 ;
    minaret:startTime 1320.14 ;
    minaret:text "they see people going there in white, you know, in submission to Allah, they also feel something. I'm not sure if you have remembered, but you know, a few years back before COVID," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0124 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1339.3 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0125 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 124 ;
    minaret:startTime 1334.96 ;
    minaret:text "you know, some people actually had a Snapchat story about" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0125 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1346.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0126 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 125 ;
    minaret:startTime 1339.3 ;
    minaret:text "27th night of Ramadan in Makkah, and a lot of non-Muslims were writing on it that, you know, 'We wish we were there, we just love it, we want to become Muslims,' SubhanAllah, like so many of" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0126 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1353.4 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0127 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 126 ;
    minaret:startTime 1346.36 ;
    minaret:text "them! It was just mind-blowing that how it is a guidance for the worlds just by looking at it." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0127 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1362.4 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0128 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 127 ;
    minaret:startTime 1353.96 ;
    minaret:text "So how is Makkah or Baitullah guidance for the 'Alamin, for the people?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0159 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1714.42 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0160 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 159 ;
    minaret:startTime 1703.14 ;
    minaret:text "in Qur'an: وَاتَّخِذُوْا مِنْ مَّقَامِ اِبْرٰهٖمَ مُصَلًّی ؕ 'And take for the standing place of Ibrahim a place of prayer.' And Alhamdulillah we do after" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0163 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1754.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0164 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 163 ;
    minaret:startTime 1744.68 ;
    minaret:text "Ibrahim said, 'My Lord, make this city secure and keep me and my sons away from worshipping idols,' his" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0190 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2039.1200000000001 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0191 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 190 ;
    minaret:startTime 2032.4 ;
    minaret:text "People are obliged to do Hajj for Allah, not for any other reason, not for business, not for money, not for fame," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0191 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2052.82 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0192 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 191 ;
    minaret:startTime 2039.1200000000001 ;
    minaret:text "nothing else, just for Allah. مَنِ اسْتَطَاعَ اِلَیْهِ سَبِیْلًا—whoever is able to do it. We are going to talk about the ability, we are going to talk about what is istita'ah in a bit." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0192 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2061.48 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0193 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 192 ;
    minaret:startTime 2053.5 ;
    minaret:text "But before that, let's just revisit the goal: that why do we do Hajj? We do Hajj only for the pleasure of Allah," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0193 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2072.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0194 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 193 ;
    minaret:startTime 2062.08 ;
    minaret:text "only to get His approval, only to please Him, only to obey Him, only to respond to His call. May Allah make us among those people who do that!" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0194 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2085.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0195 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 194 ;
    minaret:startTime 2072.36 ;
    minaret:text "And Hajj is mandatory once in a lifetime, but if we perform more Hajj it's better for us. And Insha'Allah we are going to touch base that point today if time permits, Insha'Allah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0196 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2102.26 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0197 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 196 ;
    minaret:startTime 2095.04 ;
    minaret:text "an obligation for you, so perform Hajj.' Thereupon a person said, 'Is it to be performed every year?'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0197 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2109.82 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0198 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 197 ;
    minaret:startTime 2102.26 ;
    minaret:text "Rasulullah Sallallahu Alayhi wa Sallam, he kept quiet, but this person repeated his question three times." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0198 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2123.2 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0199 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 198 ;
    minaret:startTime 2109.82 ;
    minaret:text "Whereupon Allah's Messenger said: 'If I were to say yes, it would become obligatory and you would not be able to do it.' Then he said: 'Leave me with what I have left to you," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0199 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2133.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0200 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 199 ;
    minaret:startTime 2123.2 ;
    minaret:text "for those who were before you were destroyed because of excessive questioning.' So, Allah He just clarified that it is mandatory only once. So, that's the proof for that." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0200 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2143.66 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0201 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 200 ;
    minaret:startTime 2133.72 ;
    minaret:text "And there's another narration which we have already covered before, and I'm going to show you that today as well. So, Hajj is mandatory for those who are able to go," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0201 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2153.82 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0202 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 201 ;
    minaret:startTime 2143.66 ;
    minaret:text "who have istita'ah. What does that mean? It has three understandings based: first one, when a person has the travel expenses," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0202 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2163.68 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0203 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 202 ;
    minaret:startTime 2153.82 ;
    minaret:text "when a person is able to travel, then he is capable to go for Hajj. And also this person should have enough expenses for the people he's leaving behind." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0203 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2177.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0204 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 203 ;
    minaret:startTime 2163.68 ;
    minaret:text "So, let's say if he is the father of the family and he has family left behind, so he should leave enough funds for them to eat, drink, and survive. So, this means this person is rich enough to go for Hajj, because that person has money to go for Hajj and also his family is not going to suffer." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0204 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2184.48 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0205 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 204 ;
    minaret:startTime 2178.58 ;
    minaret:text "Second point: that it should be safe, it should be safe to go." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0205 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2196.68 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0206 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 205 ;
    minaret:startTime 2185.26 ;
    minaret:text "So, scholars have mentioned in the tafaseer: safe way, when a person's life and property is safe, then it's okay for us to go. But if it's not safe, then" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0206 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2207.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0207 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 206 ;
    minaret:startTime 2197.44 ;
    minaret:text "it's not mandatory for us to go that year if there's a problem. So, Alhamdulillah because of this opinion, the COVID years were okay for us if we were not" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0207 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2217.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0208 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 207 ;
    minaret:startTime 2207.46 ;
    minaret:text "able to go, because it wasn't safe for our life, isn't it, SubhanAllah? And if people were not called for Hajj or they were not allowed to go for Hajj or Umrah," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0208 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2227.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0209 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 208 ;
    minaret:startTime 2217.62 ;
    minaret:text "then it wasn't something so bad, it's totally allowed based on all of these narrations. And then if a person is not physically able to go," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0209 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2234.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0210 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 209 ;
    minaret:startTime 2227.52 ;
    minaret:text "then again that person is not required to go. So, physical capability is also one of the conditions." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0210 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2244.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0211 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 210 ;
    minaret:startTime 2234.02 ;
    minaret:text "So, let's say a person is not able to go, but is rich enough—can that person send someone else on his or her behalf with her money or with his money? Yes, right? And Allah knows best." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0211 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2254.7 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0212 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 211 ;
    minaret:startTime 2244.76 ;
    minaret:text "So, the people who don't perform Hajj in spite of the ability to go for Hajj—you know, they have money, they are healthy enough," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0212 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2263.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0213 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 212 ;
    minaret:startTime 2254.7 ;
    minaret:text "and there is no problem on the way—then it is considered a major sin. Not performing Hajj in spite of one's ability is a major sin." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0213 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2274.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0214 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 213 ;
    minaret:startTime 2264.76 ;
    minaret:text "But there is something to remember: this person believes that Hajj is fard, but not going because of laziness, because of whatever." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0214 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2289.38 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0215 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 214 ;
    minaret:startTime 2274.44 ;
    minaret:text "But believing that Hajj is not mandatory or Hajj is not part of Islam makes a person a non-believer, kicks a person out of the fold of Islam. So, it's something which is very important to remember." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0215 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2296.68 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0216 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 215 ;
    minaret:startTime 2290.06 ;
    minaret:text "So, two things, Insha'Allah, we need to remember, because the next part of the ayah—which is the concluding part of the ayah we have covered: وَمَنْ كَفَرَ—whoever" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0216 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2308.04 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0217 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 216 ;
    minaret:startTime 2296.68 ;
    minaret:text "disbelieves... The beginning part talks about Hajj, it would have mentioned, you know, the one who doesn't do Hajj; but here it is mentioned the one who does kufr." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0217 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2315.08 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0218 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 217 ;
    minaret:startTime 2308.04 ;
    minaret:text "What does that mean? It's the kufr of the blessing: Allah has given you health, Allah has given you wealth, Allah has made" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0218 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2322.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0219 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 218 ;
    minaret:startTime 2315.08 ;
    minaret:text "it easy for you to reach there, and you still are not going." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0219 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2331.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0220 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 219 ;
    minaret:startTime 2322.02 ;
    minaret:text "You are denying the blessing, and this blessing can be denied with heart and with actions. When this blessing is denied with heart, then" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0220 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2346.68 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0221 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 220 ;
    minaret:startTime 2331.72 ;
    minaret:text "the person doesn't believe in Hajj. When this blessing is denied with action, then person doesn't go for Hajj, believes in it but doesn't do it. So, both are wrong. So, whoever doesn't go for Hajj, then they need to remember: فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَنِیٌّ عَنِ الْعٰلَمِیْنَ—" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0221 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2359.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0222 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 221 ;
    minaret:startTime 2346.68 ;
    minaret:text "Allah is Ghani, He doesn't need your Hajj, He doesn't need you. So, we don't do any favor on anyone when we do Hajj, it's a favor on us." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0291 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3134.7 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0292 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 291 ;
    minaret:startTime 3125.02 ;
    minaret:text "So, best deed after iman is Hajj. If you look at the order, then it comes after jihad. So, let's look at this: Rasulullah was asked, 'Which is the best deed?'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0292 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3140.9 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0293 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 292 ;
    minaret:startTime 3134.7 ;
    minaret:text "So, he responded: 'To believe in Allah and His Messenger.'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0293 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3151.22 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0294 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 293 ;
    minaret:startTime 3141.52 ;
    minaret:text "He was then asked, 'Which is next?' Then he said, 'Jihad fi sabilillah.' Then he was asked, 'What is next?' So, he said, 'To perform Hajj Mabroor,'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0294 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3158.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0295 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 294 ;
    minaret:startTime 3151.22 ;
    minaret:text "to perform a Hajj which is Mabroor. Insha'Allah we will talk about Mabroor in detail in one of the future sessions." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0295 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3170.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0296 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 295 ;
    minaret:startTime 3159.7000000000003 ;
    minaret:text "Another virtue of Hajj is that when we are on this way, when we are going, when we are traveling, when we are planning, then we are in the way of Allah. Indeed," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0296 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3182.98 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0297 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 296 ;
    minaret:startTime 3172.98 ;
    minaret:text "Hajj and Umrah are from the way of Allah, and the people who go for Hajj and Umrah, they are called a delegation of Allah, SubhanAllah, such a" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0297 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3196.2 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0298 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 297 ;
    minaret:startTime 3182.98 ;
    minaret:text "beautiful title! 'The soldier in the cause of Allah and the pilgrim performing Hajj and Umrah are a delegation to Allah: He invited them, so they responded to Him, and they asked Him and He gives to them.'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0298 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3206.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0299 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 298 ;
    minaret:startTime 3196.96 ;
    minaret:text "He responds to their du'as as well, and du'as are granted, as we have just talked about, of hajjis and the ones who do Umrah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0299 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3217.12 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0300 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 299 ;
    minaret:startTime 3207.96 ;
    minaret:text "And sins are forgiven for the people who go for Umrah—and we have talked about this before as well, but this is a very beautiful narration, so we just want to touch base this part of it." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0300 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3228.3 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0301 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 300 ;
    minaret:startTime 3220.52 ;
    minaret:text "And verily the pilgrimage wipes out all the previous misdeeds, all the previous misdeeds, all evil deeds, all sins. And Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala, He forgives the one who leaves the home for Hajj," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0301 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3241.18 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0302 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 301 ;
    minaret:startTime 3229.04 ;
    minaret:text "and it's a means to remove poverty and sin, we have talked about that before." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0303 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3262.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0304 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 303 ;
    minaret:startTime 3252.92 ;
    minaret:text "And SubhanAllah about this there was another narration where one person was asking Rasulullah and he was saying that, 'I'm very weak and, you know, I'm very coward," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0304 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3277.28 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0305 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 304 ;
    minaret:startTime 3262.64 ;
    minaret:text "I cannot go for battle, I cannot go to defend Muslims, so what do I do?' So, Rasulullah told him: 'Jihad for the elderly, the young, the weak, and the woman is Hajj and Umrah,'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0305 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3288.16 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0306 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 305 ;
    minaret:startTime 3278.0 ;
    minaret:text "SubhanAllah. So, we need to, Insha'Allah, go there to avail this amazing reward as well." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0306 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3298.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0307 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 306 ;
    minaret:startTime 3289.02 ;
    minaret:text "Aisha, she asked, 'Ya Rasulullah, shall we not go out for jihad with you?' He said, 'For you, the best and most beautiful type of" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0307 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3308.96 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0308 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 307 ;
    minaret:startTime 3298.94 ;
    minaret:text "jihad is Hajj'—and which Hajj? Al-Hajj al-Mabroor. So, Aisha, she said: 'So, I will not leave Hajj ever after hearing this from the" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0308 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3317.6 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0309 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 308 ;
    minaret:startTime 3308.96 ;
    minaret:text "Messenger of Allah Sallallahu Alayhi wa Sallam.' What does that mean? I will not miss the opportunity to perform Hajj. And May Allah also make us like her!" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0309 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3323.84 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0310 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 309 ;
    minaret:startTime 3318.58 ;
    minaret:text "And we also learn that when we travel in the way of Allah, whatever" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0310 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3335.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0311 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 310 ;
    minaret:startTime 3325.1600000000003 ;
    minaret:text "trace whatever mark we experience—maybe a bruise, maybe a cut, whatever happens—it is also something which is of a lot of virtue." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0311 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3348.14 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0312 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 311 ;
    minaret:startTime 3335.54 ;
    minaret:text "So, let's look at this narration: 'A trace resulting in Allah's cause and a trace resulting from one of the duties that Allah made an obligation—they are more beloved to Allah than any other trace,'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0312 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3358.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0313 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 312 ;
    minaret:startTime 3348.82 ;
    minaret:text "SubhanAllah, they are more beloved to Allah. You know, sometimes when you're performing duties, sometimes you do get some marks; for example, when you're sitting for salah, sometimes" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0313 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3367.04 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0314 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 313 ;
    minaret:startTime 3358.76 ;
    minaret:text "you get some marks on your feet because of, you know, sitting in the same position over and over again many times in a day." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0314 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3377.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0315 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 314 ;
    minaret:startTime 3367.7799999999997 ;
    minaret:text "Similarly at Hajj, if you get some cut, some bruise, that is also something which is very rewardable because Allah loves it. And a person who dies on the" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0315 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3387.86 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0316 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 315 ;
    minaret:startTime 3377.78 ;
    minaret:text "way to Hajj and Umrah—let's talk about them: whoever leaves for Hajj and dies, Allah writes for him the reward for Hajj till the Day of Judgment, SubhanAllah, as if he's keep on performing Hajj." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0316 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3396.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0317 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 316 ;
    minaret:startTime 3387.86 ;
    minaret:text "And whoever leaves for Umrah and dies, Allah writes for him the reward for Umrah till the Day of Judgment. It should be Umrah here, and Allah knows best." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0317 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3411.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0318 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 317 ;
    minaret:startTime 3397.5 ;
    minaret:text "And the person who dies while performing Hajj, what will happen to that person on the Day of Judgment? Let's see: Narrated Ibn Abbas: 'While a man was riding in Arafat, he fell down from his ride" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0318 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3414.32 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0319 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 318 ;
    minaret:startTime 3412.2000000000003 ;
    minaret:text "and broke his neck and he passed away.'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0319 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3422.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0320 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 319 ;
    minaret:startTime 3414.9 ;
    minaret:text "Rasulullah Sallallahu Alayhi wa Sallam said: 'Wash him with water and sidr," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0320 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3433.18 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0321 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 320 ;
    minaret:startTime 3422.76 ;
    minaret:text "and shroud him in two pieces of cloth, and neither perfume him nor cover his head, because he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection saying: Labbayka" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0321 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3443.1 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0322 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 321 ;
    minaret:startTime 3433.18 ;
    minaret:text "Allahumma Labbayk, like a pilgrim.' So, leave him like you're leaving him in the state of Ihram, don't cover his head, and he will be raised by saying Labbayk," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0322 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3456.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0323 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 322 ;
    minaret:startTime 3443.1 ;
    minaret:text "SubhanAllah! Beautiful ending and beautiful beginning. And the people who perform Hajj, even if they do a lot of other bad deeds after that, eventually they will be taken out from Hell—that's another virtue of Hajj, SubhanAllah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0323 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3467.06 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0324 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 323 ;
    minaret:startTime 3457.02 ;
    minaret:text "Let's say you're not able to go for Hajj this year or you really want to, but for whatever reason, you know, you feel really sad that you're not" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0324 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3477.08 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0325 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 324 ;
    minaret:startTime 3467.06 ;
    minaret:text "able to go for Hajj and you're missing out on a lot of reward. So, are there any deeds which are going to give you the same reward as Hajj? The answer is yes," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0325 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3486.98 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0326 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 325 ;
    minaret:startTime 3477.08 ;
    minaret:text "Alhamdulillah. So, let's learn about them: when we perform Umrah in Ramadan, we are going to get the reward equal to Hajj." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0326 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3496.7 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0327 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 326 ;
    minaret:startTime 3486.98 ;
    minaret:text "There's another narration which talks about: Umrah during Ramadan is equal to Hajj in terms of rewards—but what kind of Hajj? Hajj with Rasulullah Sallallahu Alayhi wa Sallam." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0327 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3506.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0328 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 327 ;
    minaret:startTime 3496.7 ;
    minaret:text "Another amazing opportunity we can all avail is praying our prayers in the masjid. So, do wudu, go" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0328 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3516.38 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0329 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 328 ;
    minaret:startTime 3506.62 ;
    minaret:text "to masjid and pray your prayers together in jamaah, right? It's for the brothers for sure, but for the sisters it's better for them to pray at home" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0329 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3526.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0330 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 329 ;
    minaret:startTime 3516.38 ;
    minaret:text "except in sacred masajid, right? Except in Haramain, except in Masjid al-Haram and Masjid an-Nabawi. So, Insha'Allah you can" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0330 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3532.26 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0331 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 330 ;
    minaret:startTime 3526.46 ;
    minaret:text "avail this opportunity when you go for Hajj and Umrah that you can go perform prayers there, but wherever you are" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0331 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3537.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0332 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 331 ;
    minaret:startTime 3532.26 ;
    minaret:text "and there is no fitna, you can go to masjid properly." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0332 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3547.26 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0333 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 332 ;
    minaret:startTime 3537.62 ;
    minaret:text "Another opportunity: praying Ishraq after Fajr. If you pray Fajr in jamaah, then sit remembering Allah at your prayer place" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0333 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3558.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0334 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 333 ;
    minaret:startTime 3547.26 ;
    minaret:text "until the sun rises, then you pray two rak'at, and you're going to get the reward like a complete Hajj and complete Umrah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0334 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3569.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0335 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 334 ;
    minaret:startTime 3560.12 ;
    minaret:text "Going to masjid to learn or to teach—that also gives us the reward of Hajj, SubhanAllah. So, what are we supposed to do? Go to the masjid not desiring anything except to learn deen or to teach deen." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0335 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3580.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0336 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 335 ;
    minaret:startTime 3570.42 ;
    minaret:text "What could be anything else? To meet up, to chitchat, to catch up—those should not be the reasons, or to promote your business, those are all wrong reasons, right?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0336 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3590.56 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0337 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 336 ;
    minaret:startTime 3580.46 ;
    minaret:text "Reason to go to the masjid is to desire to learn or teach, and of course to pray and to please Allah, all of that. But based on this narration, to learn or to teach," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0337 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3609.36 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 337 ;
    minaret:startTime 3590.56 ;
    minaret:text "a person is going to get the reward like Hajj. Jazakumullahu Khairan Katheera for paying attention. So, let's Insha'Allah conclude, right? So, let's make du'a together: سُبْحَانَكَ اللّٰهُمَّ وَبِحَمْدِكَ، اَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَّاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ، اَسْتَغْفِرُكَ وَاَتُوْبُ اِلَیْكَ۔ بَارَكَ اللّٰهُ فِیْكُمْ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكُمْ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهُ۔" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0001 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 21.56 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0002 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 1 ;
    minaret:startTime 10.24 ;
    minaret:text "نَحْمَدُهٗ وَنُصَلِّیْ عَلٰی رَسُوْلِهِ الْكَرِیْمِ ؔؕ اَمَّا بَعْدُ فَاَعُوْذُ بِاللّٰهِ مِنَ الشَّیْطٰنِ الرَّجِیْمِ ؔؕ بِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِیْمِ ؔؕ رَبِّ اشْرَحْ لِیْ صَدْرِیْ ۙ وَیَسِّرْ لِیْۤ اَمْرِیْ ۙ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0005 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 61.46 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0006 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 5 ;
    minaret:startTime 50.18 ;
    minaret:text "وَاِذْ بَوَّأْنَا لِاِبْرٰهِیْمَ مَكَانَ الْبَیْتِ اَنْ لَّا تُشْرِكْ بِیْ شَیْـًٔا" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0006 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 62.86 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0007 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 6 ;
    minaret:startTime 61.46 ;
    minaret:text "Ameen." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0007 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 69.8 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0008 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 7 ;
    minaret:startTime 62.86 ;
    minaret:text "اَنْ لَّا تُشْرِكْ بِیْ شَیْـًٔا وَّطَهِّرْ بَیْتِیَ لِلطَّآىِٕفِیْنَ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0008 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 71.2 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0009 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 8 ;
    minaret:startTime 69.8 ;
    minaret:text "Ameen." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0009 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 74.06 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0010 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 9 ;
    minaret:startTime 71.2 ;
    minaret:text "لِلطَّآىِٕفِیْنَ وَالْقَآىِٕمِیْنَ وَالرُّكَّعِ السُّجُوْدِ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0011 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 77.84 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0012 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 11 ;
    minaret:startTime 75.86 ;
    minaret:text "وَاَذِّنْ فِی النَّاسِ بِالْحَجِّ یَاْتُوْكَ رِجَالًا" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0012 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 79.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0013 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 12 ;
    minaret:startTime 77.84 ;
    minaret:text "Ameen, Ameen." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0013 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 81.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0014 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 13 ;
    minaret:startTime 79.94 ;
    minaret:text "رِجَالًا وَّعَلٰی كُلِّ ضَامِرٍ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0014 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 82.26 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0015 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 14 ;
    minaret:startTime 81.44000000000001 ;
    minaret:text "Ameen." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0015 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 89.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0016 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 15 ;
    minaret:startTime 82.26 ;
    minaret:text "یَّاْتِیْنَ مِنْ كُلِّ فَجٍّ عَمِیْقٍ ۟ۙ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0017 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 118.8 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0018 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 17 ;
    minaret:startTime 91.76 ;
    minaret:text "لِّیَشْهَدُوْا مَنَافِعَ لَهُمْ وَیَذْكُرُوا اسْمَ اللّٰهِ فِیْۤ اَیَّامٍ مَّعْلُوْمٰتٍ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0018 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 120.74 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0019 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 18 ;
    minaret:startTime 118.8 ;
    minaret:text "Ameen, Ameen." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0019 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 129.66 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0020 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 19 ;
    minaret:startTime 120.74 ;
    minaret:text "فِیْۤ اَیَّامٍ مَّعْلُوْمٰتٍ عَلٰی مَا رَزَقَهُمْ مِّنْۢ بَهِیْمَةِ الْاَنْعَامِ ۚ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0020 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 130.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0021 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 20 ;
    minaret:startTime 129.66000000000003 ;
    minaret:text "Ameen." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0021 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 132.04 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0022 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 21 ;
    minaret:startTime 130.36 ;
    minaret:text "فَكُلُوْا مِنْهَا" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0022 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 133.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0023 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 22 ;
    minaret:startTime 132.04 ;
    minaret:text "Ameen." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0023 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 135.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0024 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 23 ;
    minaret:startTime 133.44 ;
    minaret:text "وَاَطْعِمُوا الْبَآىِٕسَ الْفَقِیْرَ ۟" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0025 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 144.14 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0026 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 25 ;
    minaret:startTime 136.94 ;
    minaret:text "ثُمَّ لْیَقْضُوْا تَفَثَهُمْ وَلْیُوْفُوْا نُذُوْرَهُمْ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0026 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 145.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0027 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 26 ;
    minaret:startTime 144.14 ;
    minaret:text "Ameen." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0027 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 149.96 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0028 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 27 ;
    minaret:startTime 145.54 ;
    minaret:text "وَلْیَطَّوَّفُوْا بِالْبَیْتِ الْعَتِیْقِ ۟" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0029 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 161.84 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0030 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 29 ;
    minaret:startTime 152.24 ;
    minaret:text "ذٰلِكَ ؕ وَمَنْ یُّعَظِّمْ حُرُمٰتِ اللّٰهِ فَهُوَ خَیْرٌ لَّهٗ عِنْدَ رَبِّهٖ ؕ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0030 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 163.24 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0031 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 30 ;
    minaret:startTime 161.84 ;
    minaret:text "Ameen." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0031 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 165.22 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0032 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 31 ;
    minaret:startTime 163.24 ;
    minaret:text "وَاُحِلَّتْ لَكُمُ الْاَنْعَامُ اِلَّا مَا یُتْلٰی عَلَیْكُمْ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0032 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 166.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0033 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 32 ;
    minaret:startTime 165.22 ;
    minaret:text "Ameen." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0033 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 175.74 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0034 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 33 ;
    minaret:startTime 166.62 ;
    minaret:text "فَاجْتَنِبُوا الرِّجْسَ مِنَ الْاَوْثَانِ وَاجْتَنِبُوْا قَوْلَ الزُّوْرِ ۟ۙ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0035 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 189.32 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0036 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 35 ;
    minaret:startTime 183.74 ;
    minaret:text "وَإِذْ بَوَّأْنَا لِإِبْرَاهِيمَ مَكَانَ الْبَيْتِ أَنْ لَا تُشْرِكْ بِي شَيْئًا وَطَهِّرْ بَيْتِيَ لِلطَّائِفِينَ وَالْقَائِمِينَ وَالرُُكَّعِ السُّجُودِ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0036 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 200.26 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0037 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 36 ;
    minaret:startTime 189.58 ;
    minaret:text "And mention when We designated for Ibrahim the site of the House: 'Do not associate anything with Me and purify My House for those who perform tawaf and those who stand in prayer and those who bow and those who prostrate.'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0037 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 206.82 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0038 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 37 ;
    minaret:startTime 200.46 ;
    minaret:text "وَأَذِّنْ فِي النَّاسِ بِالْحَجِّ يَأْتُوكَ رِجَالًا وَعَلَى كُلِّ ضَامِرٍ يَأْتِينَ مِنْ كُلِّ فَجِّ عَمِيقٍ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0038 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 219.32 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0039 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 38 ;
    minaret:startTime 207.14 ;
    minaret:text "'And proclaim to the people the Hajj; they will come to you on foot and on every lean camel, they will come from every distant pass, that they may witness benefits for themselves and mention the name of Allah on known days over what He has provided for them of sacrificial animals.'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0040 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 243.32 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0041 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 40 ;
    minaret:startTime 229.8 ;
    minaret:text "'So eat of them and feed the miserable and poor. Then let them end their untidiness and fulfill their vows and perform tawaf around the Ancient House.' That has been commanded, and whoever honors the sacred ordinances of Allah, it is best for him in the sight of his Lord. And permitted to you are the grazing livestock except what is recited to you." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0041 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 252.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0042 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 41 ;
    minaret:startTime 243.46 ;
    minaret:text "فَاجْتَنِبُوا الرِّجْسَ مِنَ الْأَوْثَانِ وَاجْتَنِبُوا قَوْلَ الزُّورِ. So avoid the uncleanniness of idols and avoid false statement. These verses give us an overview of Hajj, a picture of Hajj." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0065 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 504.08 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0066 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 65 ;
    minaret:startTime 491.6 ;
    minaret:text "Who was that? Hajar. Had she let the Zamzam flow without trying to control it, Zamzam would have been streaming, or Zamzam would have been a stream flowing on the surface of the earth." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0066 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 515.56 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0067 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 66 ;
    minaret:startTime 504.76 ;
    minaret:text "The Prophet Sallallahu Alayhi wa Sallam further added: 'Then she drank water and suckled her child. The angel said to her: Don't be afraid of being neglected, like don't be afraid of being alone.'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0067 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 524.84 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0068 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 67 ;
    minaret:startTime 515.78 ;
    minaret:text "'Don't be afraid of being neglected, for this is the House of Allah which will be built by this boy and his father.' SubhanAllah, just imagine at that time there was nothing there." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0068 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 538.18 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0069 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 68 ;
    minaret:startTime 525.18 ;
    minaret:text "But the angel gave this glad tiding to Hajar that you will survive, your son will survive, there will be one day that you will have a reunion, and then you will also have a beautiful house of Allah built here." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0069 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 550.56 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0070 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 69 ;
    minaret:startTime 538.5 ;
    minaret:text "And he also mentioned: 'And Allah never neglects His people.' The house at that time was on a high place resembling a hillock, and when torrents came, like floods, they flowed to its right and left." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0070 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 560.84 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0071 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 70 ;
    minaret:startTime 550.88 ;
    minaret:text "She lived in that way till some people from the tribe of Jurhum—or a family from Jurhum—passed by her and her child, and then they of course settled there afterwards, SubhanAllah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0075 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 620.22 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0076 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 75 ;
    minaret:startTime 606.28 ;
    minaret:text "No one should come to Kaaba and perform any shirk, and no one should come to Kaaba and do anything which is vulgar, do anything which is an act of disobedience." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0076 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 632.14 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0077 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 76 ;
    minaret:startTime 620.36 ;
    minaret:text "They should only worship Allah. But what happened? Even though the mushrikeen of Makkah, they claimed that they actually were following Ibrahim Alayhi Salam, they disobeyed this instruction" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0077 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 643.84 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0078 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 77 ;
    minaret:startTime 632.74 ;
    minaret:text "to such an extent that they raised 360 idols there. So in this picture, it's just a depiction, you can see a lot of idols around the Kaaba." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0078 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 654.3 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0079 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 78 ;
    minaret:startTime 644.24 ;
    minaret:text "May Allah save us and protect us from all sorts of shirk, Ameen. And then Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala after telling to build the Kaaba, He" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0079 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 665.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0080 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 79 ;
    minaret:startTime 654.3 ;
    minaret:text "gave another instruction to Ibrahim Alayhi Salam. Another instruction to Ibrahim Alayhi Salam was: وَطَهِّرْ بَيْتِيَ—'And purify My House.' So Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala is referring to Kaaba as 'My House'." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0080 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 677.14 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0081 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 80 ;
    minaret:startTime 665.82 ;
    minaret:text "Referring to Baytullah as 'My House'—which gives it a lot of importance, Subhanahu wa Ta'ala. And then we learn that Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala told them to purify this house. Why?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0081 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 684.4 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0082 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 81 ;
    minaret:startTime 677.82 ;
    minaret:text "Not for any worldly purpose, but for the ones who do tawaf: لِلطَّآىِٕفِیْنَ, and also for those" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0082 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 697.16 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0083 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 82 ;
    minaret:startTime 685.12 ;
    minaret:text "وَالْعٰكِفِیْنَ—the ones who do qiyam, وَالرُّكَّعِ السُّجُوْدِ—and the ones who do ruku and sujood. So the ones who pray and the ones who do tawaf, purify the house for them so it's easy for them to worship Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala there." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0083 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 704.7 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0084 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 83 ;
    minaret:startTime 697.88 ;
    minaret:text "And then when we talk about purification, purification is of two types. So this cleanliness of Baytullah" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0084 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 715.42 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0085 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 84 ;
    minaret:startTime 705.46 ;
    minaret:text "can be done in two ways: one is inwardly, and one is outwardly. So how is it done outwardly? Alhamdulillah we all understand how to clean masajid, how to keep" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0085 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 725.48 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0086 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 85 ;
    minaret:startTime 715.42 ;
    minaret:text "everything clean, so that's the obvious meaning of cleanliness. But there is an inward purification meaning as well, inward cleanliness, and that is to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0086 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 735.74 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0087 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 86 ;
    minaret:startTime 725.48 ;
    minaret:text "clean the Kaaba from shirk, to clean Baytullah from sins, from any type of zulm (injustice), any type of vulgarity, fawahish, and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0087 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 745.82 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0088 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 87 ;
    minaret:startTime 735.74 ;
    minaret:text "bad habits. So this is another way to clean the Baytullah. May Allah enable us that whenever we go there, we remember all of these" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0088 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 752.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0089 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 88 ;
    minaret:startTime 745.82 ;
    minaret:text "points and we don't, Insha'Allah, fall short. So this is how Kaaba is supposed to be cleaned—for who?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0089 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 762.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0090 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 89 ;
    minaret:startTime 752.68 ;
    minaret:text "The ones who do tawaf around it. Tawaf is, SubhanAllah, a beautiful ibadah that can only be done around Kaaba, that can only be done there." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0092 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 790.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0093 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 92 ;
    minaret:startTime 780.6800000000001 ;
    minaret:text "tawaf is like salah, the only difference is that during tawaf you can talk. It doesn't mean that you should talk, it's just if you need to talk, you can talk to someone as well. But rest of" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0115 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1009.97 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0116 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 115 ;
    minaret:startTime 999.8100000000001 ;
    minaret:text "So Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala is giving this command to Ibrahim to call people, to invite people after building it, for Hajj." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0116 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1020.49 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0117 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 116 ;
    minaret:startTime 1010.55 ;
    minaret:text "So Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala says in this ayah: 'And proclaim to mankind the Hajj.' So we learned from Tafseer Ibn Kathir that Ibrahim, he" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0117 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1030.41 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0118 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 117 ;
    minaret:startTime 1020.49 ;
    minaret:text "said, 'O Lord, how can I convey to people when my voice will not reach them?' Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala told him: 'Call, and it is Our duty to convey it.'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0118 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1040.55 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0119 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 118 ;
    minaret:startTime 1030.41 ;
    minaret:text "So Ibrahim, he stood at his maqam, or it was said on a stone, or maybe it was on Safa, or on Abu Qubais—" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0119 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1046.61 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0120 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 119 ;
    minaret:startTime 1040.55 ;
    minaret:text "a mountain near Kaaba—and then he said, 'O mankind, your Lord has built a House," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0120 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1057.31 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0121 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 120 ;
    minaret:startTime 1047.3100000000002 ;
    minaret:text "so come on pilgrimage to it.' It was said that the mountains lowered themselves so that his voice could reach all corners of the earth. So those who were still" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0121 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1067.23 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0122 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 121 ;
    minaret:startTime 1057.31 ;
    minaret:text "in their mothers' wombs and fathers' loins, they heard, and everything that heard him of rocks, cities, trees responded, and those whom Allah" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0122 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1077.21 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0123 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 122 ;
    minaret:startTime 1067.23 ;
    minaret:text "decreed would perform Hajj until the Day of Resurrection, and everyone said: لَبَّيْكَ اللَّهُمَّ لَبَّيْكَ. So this is what is reported by" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0123 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1087.15 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0124 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 123 ;
    minaret:startTime 1077.21 ;
    minaret:text "many narrations, some going back to Ibn Abbas, some going to Mujahid, some going to Ikrimah, and Allah knows best. But we know that Ibrahim, he announced" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0124 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1097.15 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0125 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 124 ;
    minaret:startTime 1087.15 ;
    minaret:text "it to people. So adhin is from adhan, right? It's a call. And different mountains and different stones are mentioned where Ibrahim actually stood" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0125 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1106.93 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0126 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 125 ;
    minaret:startTime 1097.15 ;
    minaret:text "to call. And if you just search for Jabal Abu Qubais, you can still find it—it's not jabal anymore because of construction, but you can still find that area, SubhanAllah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0126 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1114.01 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0127 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 126 ;
    minaret:startTime 1106.93 ;
    minaret:text "So he called from here according to one of the narrations, and everyone heard it, and Allah knows best." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0127 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1125.27 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0128 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 127 ;
    minaret:startTime 1115.15 ;
    minaret:text "And Ibrahim, he not only made the call, he also made du'a for people. And this is something which is very important, and this is a very important" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0128 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1131.83 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0129 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 128 ;
    minaret:startTime 1125.27 ;
    minaret:text "point we need to remember: what is the du'a? Where is the du'a? Du'a is in Surah Ibrahim, ayah number 37. Ibrahim said:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0130 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1145.03 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0131 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 130 ;
    minaret:startTime 1135.25 ;
    minaret:text "'So make hearts among the people inclined towards them,' so their hearts should incline towards Kaaba, their hearts should incline towards this sacred place." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0131 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1154.87 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0132 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 131 ;
    minaret:startTime 1145.03 ;
    minaret:text "And SubhanAllah this is so true, right? Anyone who goes there, they yearn to go there again and again, we cannot stop, we just love it. And all the" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0132 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1166.63 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0133 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 132 ;
    minaret:startTime 1154.87 ;
    minaret:text "believers, they wish to at least go there once, but once they go there, they just want to go there over and over again, SubhanAllah. So another side point from this is, or the lesson we can learn from this point is that" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0133 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1175.63 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0134 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 133 ;
    minaret:startTime 1167.35 ;
    minaret:text "invitation only isn't enough, we also need to make du'as. You know, sometimes when we are trying to call people towards deen, when we are trying to call people towards Qur'an," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0134 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1186.21 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0135 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 134 ;
    minaret:startTime 1176.25 ;
    minaret:text "then we just tell them, 'Okay, come, join us,' and that's it. But that's not enough! Sending a flyer, sending a message is not enough—what should we do? We should" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0135 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1196.25 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0136 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 135 ;
    minaret:startTime 1186.21 ;
    minaret:text "make du'as for the people, we should make du'as that it becomes easy for them to come, we should make du'as for them that they stay steadfast, so even if they come, they" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0136 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1206.63 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0137 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 136 ;
    minaret:startTime 1196.25 ;
    minaret:text "stay steadfast, they enjoy their learning, and they connect with Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala. And even after they're done, we should also make du'as for their guidance and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0137 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1216.45 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0138 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 137 ;
    minaret:startTime 1206.63 ;
    minaret:text "we should also make du'as that they keep doing the right thing, SubhanAllah. So du'a is something which is very, very important. And Insha'Allah this also shows our sincerity: that how" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0138 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1226.51 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0139 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 138 ;
    minaret:startTime 1216.45 ;
    minaret:text "sincere is our call, whatever we are calling people towards, how sincere we are in it. If we are sincere, then we're going to make du'as for them, then we're going to pick" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0139 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1236.59 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0140 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 139 ;
    minaret:startTime 1226.51 ;
    minaret:text "the Hajj time for other people for their guidance, then we're going to not miss any opportunity of any of those times where du'as are accepted, we will make" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0140 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1246.57 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0141 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 140 ;
    minaret:startTime 1236.59 ;
    minaret:text "du'as for all these people we're inviting towards khair, we're inviting towards goodness, we're inviting towards Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala. So we need to, Insha'Allah, remember to remember" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0141 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1259.57 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0142 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 141 ;
    minaret:startTime 1246.57 ;
    minaret:text "people in our du'as, Insha'Allah. And then we learn that after this call, Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala says that people will come to you, O Ibrahim, how? By foot and on rides." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0150 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1353.99 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0151 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 150 ;
    minaret:startTime 1343.81 ;
    minaret:text "And a person is not supposed to put himself or herself in difficulty for no reason; this is not a requirement of our deen that, you know, you suffer yourself, you walk" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0151 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1363.55 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0152 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 151 ;
    minaret:startTime 1353.99 ;
    minaret:text "even though if you can ride, you should just, you know, put yourself in trouble—that's not what Islam demands from us. And there's a hadith about it: Rasulullah, he" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0155 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1401.99 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0156 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 155 ;
    minaret:startTime 1396.09 ;
    minaret:text "ourselves in unnecessary hardship, because Hajj, Insha'Allah, is already filled with a lot of" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0156 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1411.61 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0157 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 156 ;
    minaret:startTime 1402.57 ;
    minaret:text "adventurous steps, right? It's already hard for many, so we should not make it harder for us so that we can, Insha'Allah, fulfill all the rites and rituals properly." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0160 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1450.41 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0161 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 160 ;
    minaret:startTime 1442.61 ;
    minaret:text "said: 'A horse may be kept for one of the three reasons: for a man, it may be a source of reward," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0161 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1456.55 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0162 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 161 ;
    minaret:startTime 1451.03 ;
    minaret:text "second is, for another, it may be a means of living, and for a third, it may be a burden.'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0162 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1467.35 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0163 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 162 ;
    minaret:startTime 1457.33 ;
    minaret:text "'As for the one to whom it is a source of reward, he is the one who keeps his horse for the sake of Allah's cause: he ties it with a long rope on a pasture or in" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0163 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1477.23 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0164 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 163 ;
    minaret:startTime 1467.35 ;
    minaret:text "a garden, so whatever its rope allows it to eat will be regarded as good rewardable deed for its owner. And if it breaks off its rope and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0164 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1492.01 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0165 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 164 ;
    minaret:startTime 1477.23 ;
    minaret:text "jumps over one or two hillocks, even its dung will be considered amongst his good deeds, and if it passes by a river and drinks water from it, that will be considered as good deeds for his benefit, even if he has had no intention of" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0192 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1752.25 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0193 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 192 ;
    minaret:startTime 1750.87 ;
    minaret:text "So remember Allah" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0193 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1764.05 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0194 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 193 ;
    minaret:startTime 1752.25 ;
    minaret:text "in known days. How do you remember Allah? You do tahmeed. What is tahmeed? Can you notice the root letters? Ha Meem Daal, right? So you say Alhamdulillah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0194 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1771.05 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0195 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 194 ;
    minaret:startTime 1764.05 ;
    minaret:text "in—and you do takbir, and that is Allāhu Akbar, and you do tasbih, and that is" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0195 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1783.31 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0196 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 195 ;
    minaret:startTime 1771.95 ;
    minaret:text "Subhānallāh. Okay, what is tahleel then? Tahmeed is Alḥamdulillāh, takbir is Allāhu Akbar, tasbih is Subhānallāh, and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0196 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1793.97 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0197 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 196 ;
    minaret:startTime 1784.11 ;
    minaret:text "tahleel is Lā ilāha illallāh, beautiful! Bāraka llāhu fīkum. And then when it comes to ayyamin ma'lumat, there are two understandings among the scholars:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0197 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1804.35 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0198 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 197 ;
    minaret:startTime 1793.97 ;
    minaret:text "so when do you remember Allah much? During the first ten days of Dhul-Hijjah! So Alhamdulillah when a lot of people reach Hajj, they reach Hajj in Dhul-Hijjah, especially from Western countries." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0198 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1815.07 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0199 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 198 ;
    minaret:startTime 1805.0500000000002 ;
    minaret:text "So sadly it has been seen—sadly it has been seen—that people, they get busy in shopping and everything, and they forget about the importance of the days" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0199 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1821.39 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0200 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 199 ;
    minaret:startTime 1815.07 ;
    minaret:text "of the first 10 days of Dhul-Hijjah. These days are for remembering Allah, right? These are the days" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0200 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1831.41 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0201 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 200 ;
    minaret:startTime 1821.3899999999999 ;
    minaret:text "to do a lot of good deeds. Every good deed we do during the first ten days of Dhul-Hijjah, no matter where we are in the world, we get more rewards for those, right? Those deeds" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0201 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1838.01 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0202 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 201 ;
    minaret:startTime 1831.41 ;
    minaret:text "they get us more rewards, SubhanAllah. So we should seize that opportunity." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0202 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1844.45 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0203 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 202 ;
    minaret:startTime 1838.01 ;
    minaret:text "there at Hajj or we are not there, then in either case we need to, Insha'Allah, give the haqq of" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0203 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1851.85 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0204 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 203 ;
    minaret:startTime 1844.4499999999998 ;
    minaret:text "these ten days by remembering Allah much. Another opinion is that we are referring to the Day of Sacrifice," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0204 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1862.89 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0205 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 204 ;
    minaret:startTime 1852.9699999999998 ;
    minaret:text "which is 10th, and then the three days afterwards. So Insha'Allah even in those days we should remember Allah much. So Insha'Allah if you want" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0205 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1873.31 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0206 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 205 ;
    minaret:startTime 1862.89 ;
    minaret:text "to benefit from both opinions, you can Insha'Allah do from 1st to 13th, Insha'Allah remember Allah much, instead of chitchatting, wasting time, analyzing people's outfits and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0206 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1887.43 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0207 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 206 ;
    minaret:startTime 1873.31 ;
    minaret:text "commenting on others. It's the best time to remember Allah. There are many ways to remember Allah: you can also do istighfar, you can also recite Qur'an, you can also, you know, make the du'as, right? Tasbihat and all, Insha'Allah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0207 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1895.49 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0208 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 207 ;
    minaret:startTime 1888.25 ;
    minaret:text "And another time when we remember the name of Allah or when we mention the name of Allah is when we are slaughtering our animals." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0208 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1898.95 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0209 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 208 ;
    minaret:startTime 1895.49 ;
    minaret:text "So when people go for Hajj, they also slaughter their animals, and even the people" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0209 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1912.23 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0210 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 209 ;
    minaret:startTime 1898.95 ;
    minaret:text "who are not at Hajj, they slaughter their animals on Eid, right? So what do they do? They remember Allah. بَهِيمَةِ الْأَنْعَامِ are mentioned, and who are they? Camels, cows, sheep, and goats, which are slaughtered" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0210 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1921.63 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0211 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 210 ;
    minaret:startTime 1912.77 ;
    minaret:text "for Eid or which are slaughtered for Hajj. So what do you do with this slaughtered meat? فَكُلُوا مِنْهَا—eat from it," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0211 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1932.31 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0212 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 211 ;
    minaret:startTime 1922.3300000000002 ;
    minaret:text "and what else? وَأَطْعِمُوا الْبَائِسَ الْفَقِيرَ—also feed others! Feed who? The poor people." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0212 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1946.11 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0213 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 212 ;
    minaret:startTime 1932.31 ;
    minaret:text "So does it mean that we are only supposed to give this meat to poor people? Not necessarily, right? So we can give meat to rich people as well, but we should first consider the ones who are starving and the ones who are very poor." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0213 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1956.67 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0214 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 213 ;
    minaret:startTime 1946.67 ;
    minaret:text "So faqir are beggars, and ba'is are those who are really in a miserable state and they are starving as well. So it is possible" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0214 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1964.81 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0215 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 214 ;
    minaret:startTime 1956.67 ;
    minaret:text "that faqir is also very poor; ba'is is actually in a worse state than faqir, SubhanAllah. So we should feed the ones who deserve the most." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0215 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1975.43 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0216 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 215 ;
    minaret:startTime 1965.41 ;
    minaret:text "And what's the proof that we can eat from it? First of all, this ayah is the proof Allah is telling us. And the next is that Rasulullah, he" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0216 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1985.71 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0217 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 216 ;
    minaret:startTime 1975.43 ;
    minaret:text "ate from his sacrificial animals. So let's look at this part of the narration from Sahih Muslim: Rasulullah, he went to the place of sacrifice and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0217 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1995.81 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0218 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 217 ;
    minaret:startTime 1985.71 ;
    minaret:text "he sacrificed 63 camels with his own hand, then he gave the remaining number to Ali, who sacrificed them all, and then he shared him" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0218 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2005.79 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0219 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 218 ;
    minaret:startTime 1995.81 ;
    minaret:text "in his sacrifice. He then commanded that a piece of flesh, piece of meat from each animal sacrificed should be put in a pot; when it was cooked, both" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0219 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2015.91 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0220 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 219 ;
    minaret:startTime 2005.79 ;
    minaret:text "of them—who? Rasulullah and Ali—they took some meat out of it and they drank its soup, SubhanAllah, right? So even" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0220 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2030.75 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0221 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 220 ;
    minaret:startTime 2015.91 ;
    minaret:text "though there were a lot of animals, but they still did something to, you know, benefit from all the animals by taking one piece of meat from all of them, SubhanAllah. Then after the sacrifice is done, then what should be done? From this part of the ayah we learn it:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0226 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2083.57 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0227 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 226 ;
    minaret:startTime 2073.73 ;
    minaret:text "it's a reminder from Allah that complete your vows. What is nadhar and what are vows? Let's understand that. Wow is something" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0227 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2093.61 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0228 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 227 ;
    minaret:startTime 2083.57 ;
    minaret:text "when you oblige yourself to do something that is not an obligation on you, but you oblige it on yourself—why? Because of something that you want to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0228 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2103.73 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0229 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 228 ;
    minaret:startTime 2093.61 ;
    minaret:text "happen. For example, some people, they really want to go for Hajj, so they, you know, vow like that: 'O Allah, if You call me for Hajj, then I'm going to do this, this, this, this,' right? 'If You call me" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0229 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2113.77 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0230 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 229 ;
    minaret:startTime 2103.73 ;
    minaret:text "for Hajj, then I'm going to maybe do tawaf every morning, every evening, every night,' things like that, right? 'Or if You call me for Hajj, then I'm going to give this much sadaqah" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0230 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2123.75 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0231 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 230 ;
    minaret:startTime 2113.77 ;
    minaret:text "or I'm going to sacrifice every day in Dhul-Hijjah for the first 10 days,' things like that. So if people have made some vows, then they are supposed to fulfill them. They were not" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0231 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2133.69 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0232 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 231 ;
    minaret:startTime 2123.75 ;
    minaret:text "obligations, but just because we made a vow, now it's an obligation. So we have to be cautious about making big vows, but it's good that if we make good vows, right?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0232 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2142.97 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0233 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 232 ;
    minaret:startTime 2133.69 ;
    minaret:text "To pray more, to do sadaqah more—these are all good vows. So if you make these vows, Insha'Allah fulfill them." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0233 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2156.87 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0234 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 233 ;
    minaret:startTime 2144.75 ;
    minaret:text "And then what do you do? وَلْيَطَّوَّفُوا بِالْبَيْتِ الْعَتِيقِ—then do tawaf around the Kaaba. Which tawaf is it?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0246 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2283.65 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0247 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 246 ;
    minaret:startTime 2278.09 ;
    minaret:text "ذٰلِكَ ؕ وَمَنْ یُّعَظِّمْ حُرُمٰتِ اللّٰهِ فَهُوَ خَیْرٌ لَّهٗ عِنْدَ رَبِّهٖ ؕ—" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0247 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2293.21 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0248 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 247 ;
    minaret:startTime 2283.65 ;
    minaret:text "is no one's property, SubhanAllah, it's not a property of any individual, so it's free, SubhanAllah, that's what it means. Then we also learn from these verses: whoever" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0248 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2303.35 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0249 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 248 ;
    minaret:startTime 2293.21 ;
    minaret:text "honors the sacred ordinances of whoever honors these sacred commands of Allah. What are these hurumat?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0249 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2313.41 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0250 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 249 ;
    minaret:startTime 2303.35 ;
    minaret:text "Some scholars say there are sacred boundaries, and there are also Masjid al-Haram sacred boundaries—Haram area. So it's not only the masjid, but Haram" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0250 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2323.31 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0251 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 250 ;
    minaret:startTime 2313.41 ;
    minaret:text "area has boundary line—you can, Insha'Allah, check on the maps. So honor them, respect them, follow the rules there, don't hurt anyone there. And also sacred" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0251 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2333.59 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0252 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 251 ;
    minaret:startTime 2323.31 ;
    minaret:text "months, we should respect them. And then sacrificial animals, they also should be respected, SubhanAllah, just because they are going there for Hajj in the way of Allah, even the" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0252 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2343.73 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0253 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 252 ;
    minaret:startTime 2333.59 ;
    minaret:text "animals are respected. So whoever honors these hurumat, it is best for that person in the sight of Allah. And also sacred ordinances" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0253 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2353.65 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0254 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 253 ;
    minaret:startTime 2343.73 ;
    minaret:text "of Allah include ihram restrictions: when we are in the state of ihram, we are not supposed to do certain things. So Insha'Allah when we follow those, we also are" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0254 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2363.15 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0255 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 254 ;
    minaret:startTime 2353.65 ;
    minaret:text "actually obeying Allah in this regard, and we should do that wholeheartedly. And when we respect sha'air, when we respect these hurumat," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0256 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2383.23 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0257 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 256 ;
    minaret:startTime 2373.95 ;
    minaret:text "so that we can respect all of these beautiful sha'air of Allah. And then we also learn about that what's halal in terms of an'am—what can" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0261 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2427.71 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0262 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 261 ;
    minaret:startTime 2418.05 ;
    minaret:text "min al-awsaan—of the idols, and wajtani bu qawla al-zur—and stay away from lies! Stay away from shirk and stay away from lies." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0262 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2437.51 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0263 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 262 ;
    minaret:startTime 2427.71 ;
    minaret:text "These two are very important, SubhanAllah. So we understand shirk is bad, we are not supposed to do any shirk there, but we also are not supposed to lie." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0263 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2447.21 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0264 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 263 ;
    minaret:startTime 2437.51 ;
    minaret:text "Rasul was once asked, 'Can a believer be a coward?' Rasul said, 'Yes.' Then he was asked, 'Can a believer be a miser?'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0264 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2457.21 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0265 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 264 ;
    minaret:startTime 2447.21 ;
    minaret:text "He said, 'Yes.' Then he was asked, 'Can a believer be a liar?' Rasul said, 'No.' So a believer cannot be" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0265 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2467.17 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0266 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 265 ;
    minaret:startTime 2457.21 ;
    minaret:text "a liar. Lying is a trait of hypocrisy. May Allah save all of us from lies! This is something we need to take out of our lives, not just" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0266 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2476.01 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0267 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 266 ;
    minaret:startTime 2467.17 ;
    minaret:text "at Hajj time, but forever, Insha'Allah. So make du'as and try your best never ever lie, even for petty things and even big things, of course." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0302 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2850.93 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0303 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 302 ;
    minaret:startTime 2840.59 ;
    minaret:text "say anything extra: لَبَّيْكَ اللَّهُمَّ لَبَّيْكَ، لَبَّيْكَ لَا شَرِيكَ لَكَ لَبَّيْكَ، إِنَّ الْحَمْدَ وَالنِّعْمَةَ لَكَ وَالْمُلْكَ، لَا شَرِيكَ لَكَ." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0304 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2873.17 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0305 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 304 ;
    minaret:startTime 2860.71 ;
    minaret:text "Allah. So Insha'Allah we need to obey Allah like that, also in Surah Al-Baqarah number two or three we learn: وَاذْكُرُوا اللَّهَ فِي أَيَّامٍ مَعْدُودَاتٍ—'And remember Allah during specific number of days.' It's not a lot of days, it's just few days." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0332 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3132.51 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0333 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 332 ;
    minaret:startTime 3129.27 ;
    minaret:text "Sa'ee around Safa and Marwa. And the" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0333 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3140.03 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0334 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 333 ;
    minaret:startTime 3132.51 ;
    minaret:text "Sunnah is to enter ihram for Hajj only during the month of Hajj. So we cannot wear ihram in Ramadan or any other month, it should" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0334 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3144.55 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0335 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 334 ;
    minaret:startTime 3140.03 ;
    minaret:text "be Shawwal, Dhul-Qa'dah, or Dhul-Hijjah, and Allah knows best. What are some of the conditions of" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0335 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3154.47 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0336 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 335 ;
    minaret:startTime 3144.55 ;
    minaret:text "be Hajj. They are seven in total, right? Or if you want to merge it, five in total and two are sub-categories. So the conditions" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0336 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3168.57 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0337 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 336 ;
    minaret:startTime 3154.47 ;
    minaret:text "of Hajj are: the person should be a Muslim, because a non-Muslim's Hajj won't be accepted; a person should be sane with a sound mind; third, person should be an adult for Hajj to be" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0337 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3175.11 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0338 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 337 ;
    minaret:startTime 3168.57 ;
    minaret:text "be the mandatory Hajj, right? So nafl Hajj can be done by children as well, and their parents get the reward for" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0338 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3185.15 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0339 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 338 ;
    minaret:startTime 3175.11 ;
    minaret:text "it, and they also get the reward for it, Insha'Allah, but their mandatory Hajj is not done. When they grow older and when they have enough means, then Hajj" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0339 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3195.51 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0340 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 339 ;
    minaret:startTime 3185.15 ;
    minaret:text "is mandatory on them, then they can do that again, Insha'Allah. Being free is another condition of Hajj: so let's say there's a slave, if that slave does Hajj, that" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0340 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3205.57 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0341 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 340 ;
    minaret:startTime 3195.51 ;
    minaret:text "Hajj is good, it's nafl, of course a lot of rewards and forgiveness and everything, but when this slave becomes free, then he will do his mandatory Hajj" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0341 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3215.39 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0342 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 341 ;
    minaret:startTime 3205.57 ;
    minaret:text "if he's able to financially and physically. And our fifth condition is being able, and that is how? Physically and financially." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0342 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3227.51 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0343 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 342 ;
    minaret:startTime 3215.39 ;
    minaret:text "Is that when a person is able to afford the trip for Hajj and also can leave enough funds for his family back home, so they should not" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0343 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3238.71 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0344 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 343 ;
    minaret:startTime 3228.37 ;
    minaret:text "suffer. It doesn't mean he should leave extra money for them to waste, enough money for them to survive, to have their groceries, to have their bills paid and everything; and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0344 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3248.49 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0345 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 344 ;
    minaret:startTime 3238.71 ;
    minaret:text "then this person also has enough to go. So this is financial ability. What's physical ability? When a person is able to walk, able to do all these, Insha'Allah, Hajj rites" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0345 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3262.93 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0346 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 345 ;
    minaret:startTime 3248.49 ;
    minaret:text "properly. Let's say the person is worried that this person can get sick, then he can make a conditional intention. So there's a fear—it's a genuine fear the person will get sick—so he can just say this: 'اللَّهُمَّ مَحِلِّي حَيْثُ حَبَسْتَنِي—" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0348 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3282.77 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0349 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 348 ;
    minaret:startTime 3277.69 ;
    minaret:text "a male family member like a husband, father, brother, or son, or a nephew," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0349 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3293.45 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0350 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 349 ;
    minaret:startTime 3283.4300000000003 ;
    minaret:text "and she should not be in the state of iddah. So these are the two conditions for women according to different narrations, Insha'Allah we're going to cover them in detail in future." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0350 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3301.89 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0351 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 350 ;
    minaret:startTime 3293.45 ;
    minaret:text "There are three types of Hajj: Tamattu', Qiran, and Ifrad. Tamattu', Qiran, and Ifrad—what's the difference?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0351 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3312.77 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0352 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 351 ;
    minaret:startTime 3302.59 ;
    minaret:text "Hajj Tamattu' is that Hajj which is performed as one Umrah separately and one Hajj separately. So we go in ihram" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0352 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3322.81 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0353 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 352 ;
    minaret:startTime 3312.77 ;
    minaret:text "state for Umrah, we perform the whole Umrah, we come out of ihram state, we trim our hair for the ladies, the brothers they shave their head and they're out" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0353 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3331.97 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0354 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 353 ;
    minaret:startTime 3322.81 ;
    minaret:text "of it, and they do everything else whatever they want to do. And when Hajj begins, they go in another ihram and then they perform their Hajj. So this is Hajj Tamattu'." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0354 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3338.77 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0355 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 354 ;
    minaret:startTime 3332.57 ;
    minaret:text "It's like a very relaxed type of Hajj, you can say. Sister Shabana is asking: 'How about purity for women?' That's not a condition, it's just she's not" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0355 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3349.57 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0356 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 355 ;
    minaret:startTime 3338.77 ;
    minaret:text "able to do only the tawaf; rest of the rituals and rites she can easily perform, and Allah knows best. Second type of Hajj is Hajj Qiran, that is with" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0356 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3359.49 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0357 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 356 ;
    minaret:startTime 3349.57 ;
    minaret:text "one ihram for Umrah and Hajj. So person goes in ihram and does Umrah and stays in the state of ihram till Hajj" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0357 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3374.39 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0358 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 357 ;
    minaret:startTime 3359.49 ;
    minaret:text "begins. Then comes Hajj Ifrad, that is only Hajj, so one ihram for Hajj, no Umrah. Usually people who live in Makkah, they do this because they get to do Umrah every now and then, so they just go for Hajj and they come back." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0358 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3379.57 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0359 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 358 ;
    minaret:startTime 3374.39 ;
    minaret:text "back. But does it mean the people who are coming from other countries, they're not supposed to do Hajj Ifrad? No, it doesn't mean that;" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0359 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3391.71 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0360 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 359 ;
    minaret:startTime 3379.57 ;
    minaret:text "That they can also do that. So Alhamdulillah proof for all three types of Hajj, they are mentioned in Sahih al-Bukhari, hadith number 1562, you can read up more on it. And which Hajj did Rasulullah perform?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0363 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3432.09 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0364 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 363 ;
    minaret:startTime 3421.83 ;
    minaret:text "So based on this, a lot of scholars say Tamattu' is the best type of Hajj, and Allah knows best. So Alhamdulillah we are done with our today's content. Sister" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0369 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3493.59 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 369 ;
    minaret:startTime 3480.53 ;
    minaret:text "so, for Hajj Insha'Allah it will be during Hajj months, all right? So let's conclude here: سُبْحَانَكَ اللّٰهُمَّ وَبِحَمْدِكَ، أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَا إِلٰهَ إِلَّا أَنْتَ، أَسْتَغْفِرُكَ وَأَتُوبُ إِلَيْكَ. Assalamu alaykum wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuh!" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0004 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 74.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0005 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 4 ;
    minaret:startTime 38.46 ;
    minaret:text "وَاَتِمُّوا الْحَجَّ وَالْعُمْرَةَ لِلّٰهِ ؕ فَاِنْ اُحْصِرْتُمْ فَمَا اسْتَیْسَرَ مِنَ الْهَدْیِ ۚ وَلَا تَحْلِقُوْا رُءُوْسَكُمْ حَتّٰی یَبْلُغَ الْهَدْیُ مَحِلَّهٗ ؕ فَمَنْ كَانَ مِنْكُمْ مَّرِیْضًا اَوْ بِهٖۤ اَذًی مِّنْ رَّأْسِهٖ فَفِدْیَةٌ مِّنْ صِیَامٍ اَوْ صَدَقَةٍ اَوْ نُسُكٍ ۚ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0005 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 77.26 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0006 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 5 ;
    minaret:startTime 74.44 ;
    minaret:text "حَتّٰی یَبْلُغَ الْهَدْیُ مَحِلَّهٗ ؕ فَمَنْ كَانَ مِنْكُمْ مَّرِیْضًا اَوْ بِهٖۤ اَذًی مِّنْ رَّأْسِهٖ فَفِدْیَةٌ مِّنْ صِیَامٍ اَوْ صَدَقَةٍ اَوْ نُسُكٍ ۚ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0006 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 94.84 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0007 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 6 ;
    minaret:startTime 77.26 ;
    minaret:text "فَاِذَاۤ اَمِنْتُمْ ٝ فَمَنْ تَمَتَّعَ بِالْعُمْرَةِ اِلَی الْحَجِّ فَمَا اسْتَیْسَرَ مِنَ الْهَدْیِ ۚ فَمَنْ لَّمْ یَجِدْ فَصِیَامُ ثَلٰثَةِ اَیَّامٍ فِی الْحَجِّ وَسَبْعَةٍ اِذَا رَجَعْتُمْ ؕ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0007 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 106.26 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0008 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 7 ;
    minaret:startTime 94.83999999999999 ;
    minaret:text "فَمَنْ لَّمْ یَجِدْ فَصِیَامُ ثَلٰثَةِ اَیَّامٍ فِی الْحَجِّ وَسَبْعَةٍ اِذَا رَجَعْتُمْ ؕ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0008 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 109.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0009 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 8 ;
    minaret:startTime 106.26 ;
    minaret:text "تِلْكَ عَشَرَةٌ كَامِلَةٌ ؕ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0009 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 116.38 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0010 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 9 ;
    minaret:startTime 109.02 ;
    minaret:text "ذٰلِكَ لِمَنْ لَّمْ یَكُنْ اَهْلُهٗ حَاضِرِی الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ ؕ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0010 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 129.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0011 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 10 ;
    minaret:startTime 117.78 ;
    minaret:text "وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ شَدِیْدُ الْعِقَابِ ۟" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0011 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 141.16 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0012 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 11 ;
    minaret:startTime 130.5 ;
    minaret:text "اَلْحَجُّ اَشْهُرٌ مَّعْلُوْمٰتٌ ۚ فَمَنْ فَرَضَ فِیْهِنَّ الْحَجَّ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0012 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 151.04 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0013 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 12 ;
    minaret:startTime 141.16 ;
    minaret:text "فَلَا رَفَثَ وَلَا فُسُوْقَ وَلَا جِدَالَ فِی الْحَجِّ ؕ وَمَا تَفْعَلُوْا مِنْ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0013 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 162.84 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0014 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 13 ;
    minaret:startTime 151.04 ;
    minaret:text "خَیْرٍ یَّعْلَمْهُ اللّٰهُ ؕ وَتَزَوَّدُوْا فَاِنَّ خَیْرَ الزَّادِ التَّقْوٰی ۖ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0014 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 165.82 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0015 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 14 ;
    minaret:startTime 162.84 ;
    minaret:text "وَاتَّقُوْنِ یٰۤاُولِی الْاَلْبَابِ ۟" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0015 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 169.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0016 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 15 ;
    minaret:startTime 165.82 ;
    minaret:text "وَاتَّقُوْنِ یٰۤاُولِی الْاَلْبَابِ ۟" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0016 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 180.82 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0017 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 16 ;
    minaret:startTime 171.44 ;
    minaret:text "And complete the Hajj and Umrah for Allah. But if you are prevented, then offer what can be obtained with ease of sacrificial animals." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0017 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 186.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0018 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 17 ;
    minaret:startTime 181.02 ;
    minaret:text "And do not shave your heads until the sacrificial animal has reached its place of slaughter." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0018 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 199.86 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0019 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 18 ;
    minaret:startTime 186.84 ;
    minaret:text "And whoever among you is ill or has an ailment of the head, making shaving necessary, must offer a ransom of fasting three days, or charity, or sacrifice." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0019 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 210.2 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0020 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 19 ;
    minaret:startTime 200.14 ;
    minaret:text "And when you are secure, then whoever performs Umrah during the Hajj months, followed by Hajj offers what can be obtained with ease of sacrificial animals." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0020 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 219.1 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0021 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 20 ;
    minaret:startTime 210.36 ;
    minaret:text "And whoever cannot find or afford such an animal, then a fast of three days during Hajj and of seven when you have returned home." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0021 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 227.28 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0022 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 21 ;
    minaret:startTime 219.1 ;
    minaret:text "Those are ten complete days. This is for those whose family is not in the area of Al-Masjid Al-Haram." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0022 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 235.4 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0023 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 22 ;
    minaret:startTime 227.76 ;
    minaret:text "And fear Allah and know that Allah is sweer in penalty. Hajj is during well-known months." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0023 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 248.86 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0024 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 23 ;
    minaret:startTime 235.4 ;
    minaret:text "So whoever has made Hajj obligatory upon himself therein, by entering the state of Ihram, there is to be from him no sexual relations and no disobedience and no disputing during Hajj." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0024 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 259.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0025 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 24 ;
    minaret:startTime 248.94 ;
    minaret:text "And whatever good you do, Allah knows it. And take provisions. But indeed, the best provision is fear of Allah. And fear me, O you of understanding." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0029 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 306.98 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0030 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 29 ;
    minaret:startTime 298.94 ;
    minaret:text "Rasulullah ﷺ, he commanded the Muslims to follow the same path that he had followed himself in performing these two duties." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0030 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 319.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0031 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 30 ;
    minaret:startTime 307.36 ;
    minaret:text "And he told the believers to, خُذُوا عَنِّي مَنَاسِكَكُمْ So take these manasik from me. Take these acts, rites and rituals, acts of worship from me." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0031 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 327.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0032 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 31 ;
    minaret:startTime 319.68 ;
    minaret:text "And this is exactly what we are supposed to do when it comes to any ibadah. We are not supposed to make up our own ways. We should learn it from Rasulullah ﷺ." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0032 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 335.96 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0033 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 32 ;
    minaret:startTime 328.84 ;
    minaret:text "So while we are talking about Hajj, something amazing about Hajj is that it is mentioned a lot in the Qur'an." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0033 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 347.9 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0034 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 33 ;
    minaret:startTime 336.18 ;
    minaret:text "Even though it's fard, it's mandatory only once in a lifetime, but it is mentioned a lot in the Qur'an. What does it show? The importance of this amazing act of worship." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0034 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 356.82 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0035 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 34 ;
    minaret:startTime 348.16 ;
    minaret:text "And also the details which are mentioned. And also the different type of case studies which are mentioned about Hajj. It's just mind-blowing." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0035 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 366.04 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0036 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 35 ;
    minaret:startTime 356.98 ;
    minaret:text "Because if you think about fasting, which is every year, it's only mentioned once in the Qur'an. So Allah is mentioned a lot in the Qur'an, but the method isn't mentioned." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0036 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 376.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0037 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 36 ;
    minaret:startTime 366.46 ;
    minaret:text "But Hajj, it's rites, it's rituals, rituals, you know, they're mentioned a lot in the Qur'an. So if you want to learn about Hajj, you can find verses in Surah Al-Baqarah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0037 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 386.32 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0038 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 37 ;
    minaret:startTime 376.78 ;
    minaret:text "If you want to learn about Hajj, you can find verses in Surah Al-Imran. You can also find them in Surah Al-Ma'idah. You can also find them in Surah Al-Hajj. Subhanallah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0038 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 398.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0039 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 38 ;
    minaret:startTime 386.32 ;
    minaret:text "So there are a lot Qur'an offers in order for us to learn and implement these rulings to do with Hajj. So inshallah, we're going to learn it from Qur'an and Sunnah both." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0039 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 406.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0040 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 39 ;
    minaret:startTime 398.28 ;
    minaret:text "Because in order to understand exactly, you'll get the clear picture of something, we need inshallah both. So let's see what Rasulullah s.a.w." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0043 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 450.24 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0044 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 43 ;
    minaret:startTime 440.2 ;
    minaret:text "So after this final Hajj of Rasulullah s.a.w. he passed away after two months. So this final Hajj, whatever Rasulullah s.a.w." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0044 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 460.82 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0045 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 44 ;
    minaret:startTime 450.7 ;
    minaret:text "did on this, Alhamdulillah, it has been reported by many Sahaba and we get a clear picture of Hajj, Alhamdulillah, from the life of Rasulullah s.a.w. as well." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0045 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 467.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0046 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 45 ;
    minaret:startTime 461.5 ;
    minaret:text "And even at that time when Rasulullah s.a.w. was performing Hajj, he was teaching people what to do." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0050 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 517.24 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0051 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 50 ;
    minaret:startTime 507.74 ;
    minaret:text "You don't have to all go towards one point and, you know, create problems for others and yourselves. So subhanallah, this was going on at that time as well." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0051 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 524.06 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0052 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 51 ;
    minaret:startTime 517.38 ;
    minaret:text "The teaching on the side while the Hajj was going on. So from these verses, let's us understand major rulings, inshallah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0053 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 544.82 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0054 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 53 ;
    minaret:startTime 534.18 ;
    minaret:text "We have talked about this ayah before as well, or this part of the ayah before as well. It gives us this comprehensive understanding that whenever we perform Hajj and Umrah, what should we do?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0054 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 554.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0055 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 54 ;
    minaret:startTime 545.0 ;
    minaret:text "We should make sure that pillars, conditions and manners are perfect and they are done purely for Allah subhanahu wa ta'ala. They are done purely to get the pleasure of Allah subhanahu wa ta'ala." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0055 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 567.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0056 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 55 ;
    minaret:startTime 554.94 ;
    minaret:text "So the method should be correct and the intention also should be correct. So how it is done and why is it done? So we should have the answers of why and how and they should be very clear in our mind before we do anything." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0056 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 576.1 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0057 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 56 ;
    minaret:startTime 567.86 ;
    minaret:text "So why are we doing what we are doing? We are doing it for Allah. And how are we doing it? We are doing it the way Rasulullah sallallahu alayhi wa sallam, he taught us to do." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0057 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 583.8 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0058 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 57 ;
    minaret:startTime 576.22 ;
    minaret:text "And when we look at this part of the ayah, it gives us four different understandings. Actually, there are many different understandings. We are going to look at the four major ones." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0058 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 594.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0059 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 58 ;
    minaret:startTime 584.14 ;
    minaret:text "One is completing the arkan pillars and wajibat, which means mandatory acts of Hajj and Umrah according to Sunnah. So this is how we are going to do it." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0059 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 607.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0060 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 59 ;
    minaret:startTime 595.44 ;
    minaret:text "Our Hajj and Umrah should be completed with all the arkan and wajibat. They are based on Sunnah. Another understanding is we should not reduce any rites and rituals of Hajj and Umrah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0060 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 619.56 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0061 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 60 ;
    minaret:startTime 607.8 ;
    minaret:text "It has been seen that people, they find some ihram restrictions very difficult and they don't want to follow them. So this doesn't really, you know, fit in this part of the ayah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0061 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 630.66 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0062 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 61 ;
    minaret:startTime 619.7 ;
    minaret:text "If we really want to obey Allah, then inshallah we need to follow all the restrictions and all the rules. Another understanding of this part of the ayah is that we should complete Hajj and Umrah after making the intention." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0062 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 640.88 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0063 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 62 ;
    minaret:startTime 630.66 ;
    minaret:text "So once you make this intention, you cannot just go back. For example, let's say a person reaches Makkah, is in ihram, but then realizes it's too hot and it's too crowded." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0063 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 651.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0064 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 63 ;
    minaret:startTime 641.24 ;
    minaret:text "It's very hard for this person to do it. And that person says, okay, that's it, over, I'm going back. We cannot do that, right? Even if it's for Nafil Hajj, we cannot do that. We should complete what we start." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0064 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 659.14 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0065 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 64 ;
    minaret:startTime 651.82 ;
    minaret:text "This is like a, you can say a normal general rule for anything. We should complete whatever we start, whatever we begin." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0065 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 668.5 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0066 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 65 ;
    minaret:startTime 659.14 ;
    minaret:text "But in this case, it's a noble act and we have, you know, taken this ihram, we are in this state of ihram. For Allah, we should not just back off just like that." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0066 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 678.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0067 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 66 ;
    minaret:startTime 668.9 ;
    minaret:text "And subhanAllah, it's a beautiful experience. Once we reach there, we forget about everything, alhamdulillah. And fourth is completing Hajj and Umrah purely for Allah, right?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0067 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 685.7 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0068 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 67 ;
    minaret:startTime 678.44 ;
    minaret:text "So all of these meanings, they fit in this beautiful phrase of this ayah. When we say purely for Allah, what does that mean?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0068 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 695.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0069 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 68 ;
    minaret:startTime 686.12 ;
    minaret:text "Not for any praise, not for any parties when we come back, not for any gifts from people, not for trade opportunities, not for any contacts." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0069 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 707.8 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0070 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 69 ;
    minaret:startTime 695.74 ;
    minaret:text "Because back in the day, Mushrikhin of Makkah, they would come for Hajj for business reasons. That we will meet new people, we will tell them about our products, we'll, you know, sign up new business trips and whatnot." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0070 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 716.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0071 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 70 ;
    minaret:startTime 708.22 ;
    minaret:text "So not for contacts, not for trade opportunities. Trade is halal there. When we go there, that can be a side thing, but that should not be the main thing." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0071 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 727.32 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0072 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 71 ;
    minaret:startTime 716.82 ;
    minaret:text "And also, Hajj is not to please people. Some people say, I just wanted to make my parents proud. Or I just wanted them to be happy that I did my Hajj. That's the wrong reason." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0072 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 736.6 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0073 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 72 ;
    minaret:startTime 727.72 ;
    minaret:text "You have just lost it right there, subhanAllah. So it's not to please people. It's not for any worldly benefits. It is only for Allah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0073 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 747.18 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0074 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 73 ;
    minaret:startTime 736.88 ;
    minaret:text "And there was another beautiful narration which tells us about a beautiful du'a by Rasulullah sallallahu alayhi wa sallam. I really want all of you to jot down this du'a and also the translation of it." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0077 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 787.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0078 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 77 ;
    minaret:startTime 776.46 ;
    minaret:text "He was Rasulullah sallallahu alayhi wa sallam, right? So he was teaching us actually that this is what should be on our mind when we are going for Hajj al-Umrah. We should not have any wrong intentions." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0078 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 797.04 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0079 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 78 ;
    minaret:startTime 788.04 ;
    minaret:text "And Umar radiyaullah once said something very profound. He said, there are many who go in groups for Hajj al-Umrah, but only a few are Hajjis." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0079 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 806.32 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0080 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 79 ;
    minaret:startTime 797.76 ;
    minaret:text "Only a few are pilgrims. What does that mean? Only few have the right intention or only few will get acceptance. So may Allah make us among those few." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0098 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1000.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0099 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 98 ;
    minaret:startTime 989.2 ;
    minaret:text "The person should slaughter an animal. So what can stop a person? A person can be stopped because of sickness. Some people get really, really sick that they get hospitalized." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0099 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1011.68 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0100 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 99 ;
    minaret:startTime 1000.86 ;
    minaret:text "So they reach there for Hajj or Umrah, but they're not even able to perform anything of that sort and they are landed in the hospital. So in that case, they won't be able to continue." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0100 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1019.96 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0101 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 100 ;
    minaret:startTime 1011.98 ;
    minaret:text "So they can sacrifice an animal and they can get their head shaved or hair trimmed and they can come out of their ihram restrictions." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0101 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1030.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0102 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 101 ;
    minaret:startTime 1020.36 ;
    minaret:text "Another reason one can be stopped is because of some enemy or sometimes people even get lost. Subhanallah. Some people get lost in Minna 10th. Some people get lost here and there." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0102 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1038.86 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0103 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 102 ;
    minaret:startTime 1030.68 ;
    minaret:text "So it is possible. There are so many possibilities. So whatever stops a person from reaching Makkah and doing the Hajj rites or Umrah rites," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0103 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1049.12 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0104 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 103 ;
    minaret:startTime 1039.1 ;
    minaret:text "then that person should sacrifice the animal that person brought or buy it from there and sacrifice and then get head shaved, hair trimmed and come out of the state of ihram." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0107 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1090.7 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0108 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 107 ;
    minaret:startTime 1079.88 ;
    minaret:text "You may wonder that, you know, when a person just breaks a bone can just get a plaster done and can still do everything. Right? Alhamdulillah it's easier now with the help of wheelchairs and everything." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0108 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1099.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0109 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 108 ;
    minaret:startTime 1091.04 ;
    minaret:text "So if it's a possibility a person is able to do it then that person can do it. But, you know, Umrah is easy because all done in you can say Masjid al-Haram." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0109 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1110.2 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0110 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 109 ;
    minaret:startTime 1100.04 ;
    minaret:text "So a person can, you know, arrange or hire someone to do the wheelchair for that person or get on the cart and do the whole thing on his or her own." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0110 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1120.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0111 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 110 ;
    minaret:startTime 1110.58 ;
    minaret:text "But when it comes to Hajj rites, you know, going to Minad and going to Musdalifad and walking here and there and Jamarat, it's not possible and it's not easy to do everything on a wheelchair." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0111 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1134.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0112 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 111 ;
    minaret:startTime 1121.12 ;
    minaret:text "Right? If a person is totally crippled and it's impossible or is very sick or let's say COVID. Right? So if it's COVID then person should be, you know, away from the people and you know, the new type of virus is coming out every day subhanAllah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0112 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1143.26 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0113 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 112 ;
    minaret:startTime 1135.12 ;
    minaret:text "If a person knows that person is sick, that person should not put other people in danger because of him or her and Allah knows best. Another case study." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0113 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1152.66 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0114 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 113 ;
    minaret:startTime 1143.4 ;
    minaret:text "So let's say there was a person who was coming for Hajj and then he passes away. There was a person who was coming for Hajj and he passes away." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0114 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1164.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0115 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 114 ;
    minaret:startTime 1152.98 ;
    minaret:text "What should be done for that person? His errors should complete it. Somebody should do Hajj Badal for this person. Especially if it's a mandatory Hajj, right?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0115 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1174.56 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0116 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 115 ;
    minaret:startTime 1164.46 ;
    minaret:text "If it's Fard Hajj, this person intended, this person wanted to go but before this person even got on the flight, this person passes away. So like someone is going to do Hajj for this person." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0116 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1184.1 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0117 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 116 ;
    minaret:startTime 1174.84 ;
    minaret:text "Another situation, let's say a person passes away after getting in the state of ihram. Maybe this person has done half the Hajj rites and then passes away." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0117 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1193.82 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0118 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 117 ;
    minaret:startTime 1184.44 ;
    minaret:text "What should be done for this person? The answer is Alhamdulillah. Yes. Nothing. Because this person will be raised saying Talbiya on the Day of Judgment." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0119 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1213.38 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0120 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 119 ;
    minaret:startTime 1203.36 ;
    minaret:text "So it's not considered undone. And it is a must that a person sacrifices an animal and why is this term used here? Istaisara It's from Yusr." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0120 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1226.56 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0121 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 120 ;
    minaret:startTime 1213.66 ;
    minaret:text "Ease. So whichever animal can be found easily. It doesn't have to be of a particular type. So any animal which is found easily in that area in Makkah can be bought and can be sacrificed." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0121 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1238.32 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0122 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 121 ;
    minaret:startTime 1227.32 ;
    minaret:text "And which animals? Again, Alhamdulillah we understand all the Shara'i animals like Bahimatul An'am we have talked about yesterday. So camel, cow, goat, sheep any of them." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0124 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1271.26 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0125 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 124 ;
    minaret:startTime 1258.16 ;
    minaret:text "And then we also learn about this whole situation of getting stopped from reaching Makkah the situation when Rasulullah sallallahu alayhi wa sallam wasn't able to perform Umrah he intended to and he actually was in the state of Ihram." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0125 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1283.5 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0126 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 125 ;
    minaret:startTime 1271.46 ;
    minaret:text "So the example of Rasulullah sallallahu alayhi wa sallam is found in the story of Hudaybiya. So if you remember the story of Hudaybiya inshaAllah you can understand this point very clearly but let me just quickly go over what we know." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0131 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1346.66 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0132 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 131 ;
    minaret:startTime 1334.16 ;
    minaret:text "So this is the ruling that when we are stopped we are still supposed to offer the sacrifices it doesn't mean that we take them back usually people back in the day they would bring their hadhi with them they would bring their sacrificial animals with them for hajj and umrah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0132 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1358.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0133 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 132 ;
    minaret:startTime 1347.04 ;
    minaret:text "So what's the ruling? Let's look at that when Abdullah bin Umar radiallahu anhumah set out for Makkah intending to perform Umrah but it was the time of fitnah after Rasulullah sallallahu alayhi wa sallam." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0137 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1412.22 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0138 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 137 ;
    minaret:startTime 1403.68 ;
    minaret:text "And then let's look at the next part وَلَا تَحْلِقُ رُؤُوسَكُمْ Otherwise don't cut your hair don't trim your hair why?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0147 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1514.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0148 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 147 ;
    minaret:startTime 1504.22 ;
    minaret:text "Rasulullah why have the people finished their Ihram after performing Umrah but you have not finished your Ihram after performing Umrah he replied I" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0148 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1524.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0149 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 148 ;
    minaret:startTime 1514.54 ;
    minaret:text "have matted my hair and I have garlanded my hadith like my sacrificial animal has that type of tag or that type of necklace to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0149 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1534.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0150 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 149 ;
    minaret:startTime 1524.52 ;
    minaret:text "show that it was for sacrifice and hair was you know stuck on the head in a way that you know they don't fall off so Rasulullah ﷺ said so I will not finish my" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0158 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1626.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0159 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 158 ;
    minaret:startTime 1615.82 ;
    minaret:text "of Hajj Tamattu was revealed in Allah's book so Sahaba mentioned like Imran bin Hussain is saying so we performed it with Rasul Allah and nothing" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0159 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1640.6 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0160 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 159 ;
    minaret:startTime 1626.02 ;
