    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0275 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 274 ;
    minaret:startTime 2757.8 ;
    minaret:text "fisk and all sorts of disobediences any act which is considered disobedience like wasting your time is also disobedience of Allah especially there when you are in" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0275 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2778.18 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0276 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 275 ;
    minaret:startTime 2767.86 ;
    minaret:text "haramain and watching youtube videos sadly with gadgets a lot of people they misuse their time a lot and they waste their time a lot and sacrificing for" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0276 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2788.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0277 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 276 ;
    minaret:startTime 2778.18 ;
    minaret:text "idols that is also wrong a lot of people they don't really sacrifice for idols especially like believers the ones who go there but they sacrifice for some saints or some religious" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0277 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2798.42 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0278 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 277 ;
    minaret:startTime 2788.52 ;
    minaret:text "figures so we have to be very cautious about that as well so what's the reward of performing hajj without rafas and fusuq whoever performs hajj to this kaaba" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0279 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2819.14 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0280 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 279 ;
    minaret:startTime 2808.18 ;
    minaret:text "newborn child, just delivered by his mother, SubhanAllah. And another thing which is not supposed to be done during Hajj is jidal: لَا جِدَالَ—no jidal. What is jidal? Fighting." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0280 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2828.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0281 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 280 ;
    minaret:startTime 2819.14 ;
    minaret:text "what kind of fighting all of this arguments and also ikhtilaf during hajj days what is ikhtilaf it is possible that some people traveling with you follow" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0281 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2838.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0282 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 281 ;
    minaret:startTime 2828.94 ;
    minaret:text "you know another scholar right and they're following their own ways and they're doing what they're taught so if they're doing all of that don't start fighting" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0282 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2851.74 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0283 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 282 ;
    minaret:startTime 2838.94 ;
    minaret:text "with them don't start giving them dalail at that point because it won't be easy for them to take it right so don't do any type of fighting not even arguments not even respectful arguments right if you really want to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0283 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2871.98 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0284 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 283 ;
    minaret:startTime 2851.74 ;
    minaret:text "help them, you can give them something to read and that's all. There will be a lot of differences, exactly. So we have to be extremely cautious about how we behave in those situations: no abusive language in fighting, and first of all no fighting. And sometimes people, they taunt with their tone, sometimes they're very condescending in their behavior and in their words," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0284 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2885.06 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0285 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 284 ;
    minaret:startTime 2871.98 ;
    minaret:text "so we should avoid anything which can lead to fight and anything which is considered sin or anything which is not from good akhlaq that should be avoided at all costs and there should be no argument on hajj rights do" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0285 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2901.98 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0286 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 285 ;
    minaret:startTime 2885.06 ;
    minaret:text "it like this, why did you do it like that? None of that. And Insha'Allah don't fight over Hajj days. Some people start assuming and start saying things like: 'Oh, it seems like government did not really sight the moon properly, seems like it's not the 9th yet, or it seems like it's not the 10th yet, look at the" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0286 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2912.16 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0287 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 286 ;
    minaret:startTime 2901.98 ;
    minaret:text "sides of the moon and all of that this is none of our business right so we are there to worship focus on what you are supposed to do don't worry about what's happening around you and Allah knows best" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0287 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2922.7 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0288 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 287 ;
    minaret:startTime 2912.16 ;
    minaret:text "even though it's mentioned clearly in the Quran but people still fight people fight over petty things like why did you move my bag why did you touch my stuff and you know" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0288 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2932.28 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0289 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 288 ;
    minaret:startTime 2922.7 ;
    minaret:text "people living together in a tent and camp, it's not very easy to stay away from everything of everyone, right, SubhanAllah? So we have to be more patient" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0289 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2942.16 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0290 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 289 ;
    minaret:startTime 2932.2799999999997 ;
    minaret:text "with other things and don't worry too much about worldly belongings forget it inshallah exactly we have to pack our taqwa and sabr with us so if you really want hajj mabroor" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0290 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2953.28 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0291 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 290 ;
    minaret:startTime 2942.16 ;
    minaret:text "then the definition is there should be no rafas no fusuq and no jidal so inshallah then our hajj will be al-hajj al-mabroor subhanallah a lot of times people say right may Allah grant you hajj al-mabroor and we" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0292 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2974.6 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0293 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 292 ;
    minaret:startTime 2964.78 ;
    minaret:text "said and the reward of hajj mabroor is nothing except jannah and whatever good you do there Allah knows it subhanallah you don't need to tell people about it whatever" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0295 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3005.22 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0296 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 295 ;
    minaret:startTime 2995.1 ;
    minaret:text "so when we are at hajj there's a beautiful advice by Dr. Farid Hashmi that try to do three types of good deeds one type of good deeds are your personal ibadat" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0296 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3019.34 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0297 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 296 ;
    minaret:startTime 3005.22 ;
    minaret:text "so pray more do more adhkar recite Quran more and do everything beautifully and properly that's one type of good deeds the second type of good deeds are when you do social work so help others do anything for" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0297 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3024.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0298 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 297 ;
    minaret:startTime 3019.34 ;
    minaret:text "them to make their Hajj easy for them, you know, help them, you know, if they are on a wheelchair, maybe" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0298 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3037.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0299 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 298 ;
    minaret:startTime 3024.78 ;
    minaret:text "help them with that if they want something water or anything get it for them buy food for people do whatever to make things easy for them so do social work there as well insha'Allah and third is" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0299 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3049.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0300 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 299 ;
    minaret:startTime 3038.9 ;
    minaret:text "so tell people about what's right and stop them from doing something wrong but again remember it should not turn into jidal so you have to be extremely wise and nice to" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0300 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3054.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0301 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 300 ;
    minaret:startTime 3049.78 ;
    minaret:text "do that. So let's say if you notice that someone is doing something so wrong, let's say someone's praying," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0301 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3064.48 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0302 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 301 ;
    minaret:startTime 3054.78 ;
    minaret:text "but her hair are coming out and her ankles are showing her feet are showing and her arms are showing then you can nicely tell her after she's done praying" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0302 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3077.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0303 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 302 ;
    minaret:startTime 3064.48 ;
    minaret:text "that would you allow me to tell you something about this part of you know and what not so insha'Allah this is a nice way to ask first and then if they're ready and willing to learn then tell them subhanallah a lot" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0303 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3084.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0304 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 303 ;
    minaret:startTime 3077.76 ;
    minaret:text "of times people tell you: 'Don't tell us!' So recently what happened was, you know, in Haram it has been seen, especially ladies, a lot of" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0304 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3094.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0305 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 304 ;
    minaret:startTime 3084.78 ;
    minaret:text "ladies they don't pray funeral prayer for whatever reason so you know I just asked a lady that should I tell you about the benefits of funeral prayer she said no I was like it's" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0305 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3106.96 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0306 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 305 ;
    minaret:startTime 3094.78 ;
    minaret:text "very rewardable she said no I don't want to know subhanallah so yeah if they're not willing to learn so it's okay leave them alone but you can insha'Allah try your best subhanallah so take advantage of opportunities for doing good days during Hajj" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0309 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3149.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0310 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 309 ;
    minaret:startTime 3136.06 ;
    minaret:text "you and subhanallah if you look at this beautiful hadith we can do pretty much all of this there at Hajj and pack with you taqwa the best travel fund you should have with you is insha'Allah taqwa" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0310 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3158.38 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0311 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 310 ;
    minaret:startTime 3150.82 ;
    minaret:text "and it doesn't mean that you should not have money because this part of the ayah was revealed about the people who used to come from yaman" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0311 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3168.98 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0312 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 311 ;
    minaret:startTime 3159.02 ;
    minaret:text "so the people of yaman used to come for hajj and they would not bring enough provisions with them and they used to say that they are trusting allah they are doing tawakkul on allah" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0312 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3175.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0313 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 312 ;
    minaret:startTime 3168.98 ;
    minaret:text "but on their arrival in Mecca they used to beg to people so allah revealed this ayah and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0314 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3187.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0315 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 314 ;
    minaret:startTime 3177.68 ;
    minaret:text "take a provision with you for the journey but the best provision is the fear of allah so take the provision for your body and also take the provision for your soul so" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0315 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3197.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0316 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 315 ;
    minaret:startTime 3187.94 ;
    minaret:text "food for the body for that you need money and food for soul you need taqwa and once you have taqwa you won't beg to people for resources or for anything and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0316 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3208.28 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0317 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 316 ;
    minaret:startTime 3197.94 ;
    minaret:text "what is taqwa obedience to allah's commands and staying away from allah's prohibitions to stay safe from allah's punishment so from this verse of surah we learn not" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0317 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3216.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0318 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 317 ;
    minaret:startTime 3208.28 ;
    minaret:text "entering the state of iram before the month of hajj is something to be observed respecting the iram of hajj when we respect" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0318 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3223.5 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0319 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 318 ;
    minaret:startTime 3217.88 ;
    minaret:text "all its restrictions and purifying good deeds only for Allah and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0319 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3234.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0320 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 319 ;
    minaret:startTime 3224.64 ;
    minaret:text "create peace in the soul and subhanallah it happens when we don't fight there right we feel at peace you know it is possible that you would have this urge of telling this" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0320 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3245.98 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0321 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 320 ;
    minaret:startTime 3234.58 ;
    minaret:text "person off or you would have this urge to tell this person that person is wrong but you stop yourself when you stop yourself you will feel a lot of peace in yourself inshaallah and hajj is a great opportunity" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0321 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3264.7 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0322 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 321 ;
    minaret:startTime 3254.64 ;
    minaret:text "to attain taqwa. So how are we going to achieve taqwa by Hajj? Few things Insha'Allah before we conclude: putting the command of Allah before every" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0322 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3274.88 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0323 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 322 ;
    minaret:startTime 3264.7 ;
    minaret:text "command so if someone tells you it's in the quran right so put allah's command before every other command and then a person does not" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0323 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3286.1 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0324 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 323 ;
    minaret:startTime 3274.88 ;
    minaret:text "show weakness and laziness to do any good deeds during hajj and especially after hajj if a person takes hajj as a boot camp if a person takes hajj as a training trip" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0324 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3293.04 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0325 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 324 ;
    minaret:startTime 3286.1 ;
    minaret:text "that person comes back you know filled with this strength for doing good deeds filled with this happiness and this eagerness to do more and more because we" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0325 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3311.06 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0326 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 325 ;
    minaret:startTime 3293.04 ;
    minaret:text "know we have to do it, SubhanAllah, right? And we do it happily. And love of dunya will not make such a person resort to haram earning. And SubhanAllah about this, you know, I remember there was one time when we were traveling to another country, and the taxi drivers were not all very honest there, SubhanAllah, majority of them." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0326 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3320.9 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0327 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 326 ;
    minaret:startTime 3311.06 ;
    minaret:text "so we got into a taxi and we asked the person about the rate and everything and that person says I will not cheat you because whatever I earn I'm saving it for hajj subhanallah and that was so beautiful" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0327 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3327.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0328 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 327 ;
    minaret:startTime 3320.9 ;
    minaret:text "so this is something which hajj teaches us we cannot earn haram because we cannot really go for hajj with haram earnings" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0328 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3338.2 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0329 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 328 ;
    minaret:startTime 3328.28 ;
    minaret:text "and such a person will avoid haram desires because this person actually in ihram even stayed away from halal desires so this person will have" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0329 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3346.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0330 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 329 ;
    minaret:startTime 3338.2 ;
    minaret:text "this strong self control after hajj and will not even go for haram desires and this person will prefer the pleasure of Allah over his pleasure may Allah make us" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0330 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3361.24 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0331 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 330 ;
    minaret:startTime 3346.58 ;
    minaret:text "among those who actually come back like this after Hajj, Ameen. Jazakumullahu Khayran Katheera everyone, Barakallahu feekum. Subhanakallahumma wa bihamdika, ashhadu alla ilaha illa anta, astaghfiruka wa atoobu ilayk. Assalamu alaykum wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuh." .

minaret:Topic_Obligation_of_Hajj_Fardiyyat_al_Hajj a minaret:Topic ;
    minaret:descriptionEn "The doctrinal status of Hajj as an indispensable pillar of Islam incumbent once in a lifetime upon capable individuals." ;
    minaret:descriptionUr "صاحبِ استطاعت مسلمانوں پر زندگی میں ایک بار حج کی قطعی فرضیت اور ارکانِ اسلام میں اس کا بنیادی مقام۔" ;
    minaret:nameEn "Obligation of Hajj (Fardiyyat al-Hajj)" ;
    minaret:nameUr "فرضیتِ حج" ;
    skos:closeMatch hadith:PillarsOfIslam ;
    skos:related minaret:Topic_Historical_Origins_of_Hajj .

