minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0040 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 426.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0041 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 40 ;
    minaret:startTime 416.42 ;
    minaret:text "So what's the benefit of going for Umrah or Hajj? Rasulullah Sallallahu Alayhi wa Sallam said: The performance of Umrah is an expiation for the sins committed between one" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0041 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 436.7 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0042 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 41 ;
    minaret:startTime 426.62 ;
    minaret:text "Umrah and the next, right? And the reward of Hajj Mabroor is nothing except Jannah, SubhanAllah. Like it's like guaranteed, and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0059 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 619.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0060 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 59 ;
    minaret:startTime 606.74 ;
    minaret:text "important, this Hadith gives us a very good idea about it: A man came to Rasulullah and said: 'What do you think of a man who fights seeking reward and fame, what will he have?' Rasulullah" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0060 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 630.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0061 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 60 ;
    minaret:startTime 620.5400000000001 ;
    minaret:text "said: 'He will not have anything.' SubhanAllah, think about it: this person is putting his life at stake, yet he's not going to get anything out of it because he had" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0143 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1456.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0144 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 143 ;
    minaret:startTime 1446.76 ;
    minaret:text "you're doing that. And remember Rasulullah, he also would ask Allah to forgive him 70 to 100 times a day, SubhanAllah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0146 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1485.12 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0147 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 146 ;
    minaret:startTime 1474.24 ;
    minaret:text "Insha'Allah if you know more that's even better. And this is another beautiful one: اَللّٰهُمَّ—O Allah—اغْفِرْ لِیْ مَا قَدَّمْتُ—forgive for me whatever I have sent ahead—" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0147 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1496.74 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0148 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 147 ;
    minaret:startTime 1486.18 ;
    minaret:text "وَمَا اَخَّرْتُ—and whatever I have delayed—وَمَا اَسْرَرْتُ—whatever I have hidden—وَمَا اَعْلَنْتُ—and whatever I have disclosed—وَمَا اَسْرَفْتُ—whatever I exceeded in—" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0148 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1511.8 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0149 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 148 ;
    minaret:startTime 1499.76 ;
    minaret:text "وَمَا اَنْتَ اَعْلَمُ بِهِ مِنِّیْ—and whatever You know more than me. This part is very important: many times we don't realize our mistakes, many times we don't know what we did, so this is Insha'Allah going to cover all of that." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0149 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1514.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0150 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 149 ;
    minaret:startTime 1511.8 ;
    minaret:text "اَنْتَ الْمُقَدِّمُ وَاَنْتَ الْمُؤَخِّرُ، لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ۔" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0174 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1761.36 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0175 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 174 ;
    minaret:startTime 1758.8 ;
    minaret:text "یَّجْعَلْ لَّهٗ مِنْ اَمْرِهٖ یُسْرًا ۟" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0270 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2764.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0271 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 270 ;
    minaret:startTime 2751.4799999999996 ;
    minaret:text "وَاَتِمُّوا الْحَجَّ وَالْعُمْرَةَ لِلّٰهِ ؕ 'Complete your Hajj and Umrah for Allah.' So what does that mean by complete your Hajj and Umrah for Allah? There are four understandings: completing Hajj and Umrah according to the Sunnah way is for Allah;" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0287 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2933.0 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0288 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 287 ;
    minaret:startTime 2917.3 ;
    minaret:text "important obligation. How do we know that? It comes in Surah Aal-e-Imran ayah number 97: وَلِلّٰهِ عَلَی النَّاسِ حِجُّ الْبَیْتِ مَنِ اسْتَطَاعَ اِلَیْهِ سَبِیْلًا ؕ وَمَنْ كَفَرَ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَنِیٌّ عَنِ الْعٰلَمِیْنَ ۟ And due to Allah from the people is a pilgrimage to the House" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0288 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2942.98 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0289 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 288 ;
    minaret:startTime 2933.0 ;
    minaret:text "'For whoever is able to find thereto a way. But whoever disbelieves, then indeed Allah is free from need of the worlds.' Allah doesn't need our" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0290 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2962.18 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0291 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 290 ;
    minaret:startTime 2953.44 ;
    minaret:text "a khutbah and he said: 'O people, Allah has made Hajj an obligation for you, so perform Hajj.'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0292 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2980.0 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0293 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 292 ;
    minaret:startTime 2969.1 ;
    minaret:text "perform Hajj because it is fard: قَدْ فَرَضَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْكُمُ الْحَجَّ فَحُجُّوا. So anyone who says Hajj is not fard after looking at this ayah and this hadith, what do you think?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0298 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3031.0 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0299 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 298 ;
    minaret:startTime 3019.78 ;
    minaret:text "and can physically visit. And Hajj is an obligation once in a lifetime. Ibn Abbas said that he asked Rasulullah:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0299 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3032.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0300 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 299 ;
    minaret:startTime 3031.0 ;
    minaret:text "that Ya Rasulullah, Hajj is to be performed annually or only once?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0300 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3042.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0301 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 300 ;
    minaret:startTime 3032.52 ;
    minaret:text "Rasulullah said: 'Only once, and if anyone performs it" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0301 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3052.12 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0302 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 301 ;
    minaret:startTime 3042.44 ;
    minaret:text "more often, he performs a nafl,' right? It becomes a nafl act, something which is a voluntary act. So obligation is only once." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0305 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3082.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0306 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 305 ;
    minaret:startTime 3079.26 ;
    minaret:text "تَعَجَّلُوا إِلَى الْحَجِّ:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0306 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3092.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0307 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 306 ;
    minaret:startTime 3082.44 ;
    minaret:text "'Hasten to do Hajj, for no one of you knows what will happen to him.' SubhanAllah, such a beautiful advice: no one knows what will happen to him, and we have seen it. No" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0309 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3118.1 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0310 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 309 ;
    minaret:startTime 3107.96 ;
    minaret:text "should not delay this beautiful obligation. Rasulullah said: 'Whoever intends to perform Hajj, let him hasten to do so, for he may fall" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0310 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3133.08 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0311 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 310 ;
    minaret:startTime 3118.1 ;
    minaret:text "sick, lose his mount, or be faced with some need.' It is possible that you were rich last year, but now you are not rich anymore, right? It is possible that we are rich this year, but we may not be rich next year. So whenever Allah gives you enough," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0312 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3149.32 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0313 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 312 ;
    minaret:startTime 3138.3 ;
    minaret:text "that when we perform Hajj and Umrah, then what happens? We don't become poor, that's a Hadith. And we should try to perform Hajj and Umrah before anything else." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0313 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3159.32 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0314 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 313 ;
    minaret:startTime 3150.08 ;
    minaret:text "So let's look at this beautiful narration: he said: 'I came to Umar and said to him: I" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0314 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3170.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0315 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 314 ;
    minaret:startTime 3160.34 ;
    minaret:text "was a Christian Bedouin and I have embraced Islam. I am eager to do jihad, and I found that both Hajj and Umrah were due from me. So I came to a man" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0315 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3180.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0316 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 315 ;
    minaret:startTime 3170.44 ;
    minaret:text "of my tribe who said to me: 'Combine both of them and sacrifice the animal easily available for you.'' What sacrifice? The sacrifice for Hajj, right? 'And" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0316 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3193.02 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0317 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 316 ;
    minaret:startTime 3180.64 ;
    minaret:text "I have raised my voice in Talbiyah for both of them.' So like this person, he had two opportunities: he picked Hajj. So he said: 'I'm already saying,' so like he made the" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0317 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3197.32 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0318 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 317 ;
    minaret:startTime 3193.02 ;
    minaret:text "intention he was going for Hajj and Umrah. Umar Radiyallahu Anhu when he heard that, he said:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0318 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3207.2 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0319 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 318 ;
    minaret:startTime 3197.32 ;
    minaret:text "'You have been guided to the practice of your Prophet.' So before anything else, before anything major. Some people delay their Hajj" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0021 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 234.66 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0022 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 21 ;
    minaret:startTime 224.14 ;
    minaret:text "Indeed, the first house of worship established for mankind was that at Makkah—blessed and a guidance for the worlds. In" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0022 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 244.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0023 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 22 ;
    minaret:startTime 234.66 ;
    minaret:text "it are clear signs such as the standing place of Ibrahim, and whoever enters it shall be safe. And due to Allah from the people is a pilgrimage to the House" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0023 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 255.96 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0024 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 23 ;
    minaret:startTime 244.78 ;
    minaret:text "for whoever is able to find thereto a way. But whoever disbelieves, then indeed Allah is free from need of the worlds." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0055 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 580.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0056 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 55 ;
    minaret:startTime 570.42 ;
    minaret:text "Allah, but they still were concerned about acceptance, and their du'a was: رَبَّنَا تَقَبَّلْ مِنَّا." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0056 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 590.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0057 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 56 ;
    minaret:startTime 580.52 ;
    minaret:text "'Our Lord, accept this from us, indeed You are the Hearing and the Knowing.' And this du'a doesn't stop there: رَبَّنَا وَجَعَلْنَا" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0097 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1028.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0098 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 97 ;
    minaret:startTime 1014.34 ;
    minaret:text "Rasulullah said: 'Perform Hajj and Umrah one after the other, for performing them one after the other removes poverty and sin, as the bellows removes impurity from iron.'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0119 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1284.66 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0120 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 119 ;
    minaret:startTime 1274.5 ;
    minaret:text "From Surah Al-Qasas (57) we learned that Allah is questioning: 'Have We not established for them a safe sanctuary to which are brought" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0120 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1289.8 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0121 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 120 ;
    minaret:startTime 1284.66 ;
    minaret:text "the fruits of all things as provision from Us? But most of them do not know.'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0189 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2032.4 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0190 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 189 ;
    minaret:startTime 2018.2 ;
    minaret:text "Again, SubhanAllah, even that is something we have learned before from Surah Al-Baqarah, we learn the same thing: وَلِلّٰهِ عَلَی النَّاسِ حِجُّ الْبَیْتِ. For Allah, what are we supposed to do?" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0195 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2095.04 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0196 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 195 ;
    minaret:startTime 2085.72 ;
    minaret:text "So, what's the proof that Hajj is mandatory for those who are able to go? He was given khutbah and he said: 'O people, Allah has made Hajj" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0302 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3252.26 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7039_0303 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 302 ;
    minaret:startTime 3241.9 ;
    minaret:text "And it's a jihad for the weak ones. Rasulullah said: 'Jihad of the elderly, the young, the weak, and woman is Hajj and Umrah,' SubhanAllah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0002 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 32.04 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0003 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 2 ;
    minaret:startTime 21.72 ;
    minaret:text "وَاحْلُلْ عُقْدَةً مِّنْ لِّسَانِیْ ۙ یَفْقَهُوْا قَوْلِیْ۔ رَبِّ زِدْنِیْ عِلْمًا ؕ اَللّٰهُمَّ فَقِّهْنَا فِی الدِّیْنِ. May Allah give us the correct understanding of Hajj." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0039 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 229.5 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0040 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 39 ;
    minaret:startTime 219.52 ;
    minaret:text "فَكُلُوا مِنْهَا وَأَطْعِمُوا الْبَائِسَ الْفَقِيرَ ٭ ثُمَّ لْيَقْضُوا تَفَثَهُمْ وَلْيُوفُوا نُذُورَهُمْ وَلْيَطَّوَّفُوا بِالْبَيْتِ الْعَتِيقِ" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0113 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 997.5100000000001 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0114 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 113 ;
    minaret:startTime 983.97 ;
    minaret:text "sacred. For them Allah is giving instructions to prophets to keep the masajid clean. And the next part of the ayah tells us about that famous call, that famous adhan for Hajj:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0114 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 999.81 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0115 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 114 ;
    minaret:startTime 997.51 ;
    minaret:text "وَأَذِّنْ فِی النَّاسِ بِالْحَجِّ۔" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0129 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1135.25 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0130 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 129 ;
    minaret:startTime 1131.83 ;
    minaret:text "فَاجْعَلْ اَفْـِٕدَةً مِّنَ النَّاسِ تَهْوِیْۤ اِلَیْهِمْ—" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0152 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1376.83 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0153 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 152 ;
    minaret:startTime 1363.55 ;
    minaret:text "saw an old man walking supported by his two sons, and he asked about him. The people informed Rasulullah that he had vowed to go on foot to the Kaaba." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0153 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1384.81 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0154 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 153 ;
    minaret:startTime 1377.71 ;
    minaret:text "Rasulullah responded, he said: 'Allah is not in need of this old man's torturing himself,'" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0154 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1396.09 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0155 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 154 ;
    minaret:startTime 1385.7900000000002 ;
    minaret:text "and then he ordered him to ride, SubhanAllah. So what does it show? That if we have some ease and comfort, we should take it, and we should not try to put" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0255 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2373.95 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0256 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 255 ;
    minaret:startTime 2363.15 ;
    minaret:text "that is a sign of taqwa in our hearts, as it comes in Surah Al-Hajj, ayah number 32: ذَلِكَ وَمَنْ يُعَظِّمْ شَعَائِرَ اللَّهِ فَإِنَّهَا مِنْ تَقْوَى الْقُلُوبِ—'That is so, and whoever honors the symbols of Allah, indeed it is from the piety of hearts.' So may Allah enable us to have taqwa of our hearts" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0323 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3050.07 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0324 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 323 ;
    minaret:startTime 3037.67 ;
    minaret:text "to Hajj months: there are three. The three Hajj months are Shawwal, Dhu al-Qa'dah, and Dhu al-Hijjah. اَلْحَجُّ أَشْهُرٌ مَعْلُومَاتٌ—so Hajj is during well-known months, and these are the three months." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0324 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3060.67 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0325 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 324 ;
    minaret:startTime 3050.77 ;
    minaret:text "Aisha said: 'We set out with Allah's Messenger in the months of Hajj, and in the nights of Hajj, and at the time and places of Hajj, and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0325 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3067.29 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0326 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 325 ;
    minaret:startTime 3060.67 ;
    minaret:text "in a state of Hajj.' So all of these things were known to Sahaba as well. And Rasulullah, he" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0326 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3075.15 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0327 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 326 ;
    minaret:startTime 3068.21 ;
    minaret:text "left at the end of Shawwal. So Rasulullah with his Sahaba, they started for Medina—they left" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0327 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3086.13 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0328 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 327 ;
    minaret:startTime 3076.09 ;
    minaret:text "from Medina for Makkah, so they were in Medina, they left Medina for Makkah after combing their hair, oiling their hair, and putting on two" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0328 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3096.03 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0329 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 328 ;
    minaret:startTime 3086.13 ;
    minaret:text "sheets of ihram. And so in the early morning Rasulullah, he mounted his mount while in Dhul Hulaifah, the area, and set" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0329 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3105.77 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0330 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 329 ;
    minaret:startTime 3096.03 ;
    minaret:text "out till they reached Baidah, another area where he and his companions recited Talbiyah: لَبَّيْكَ اللَّهُمَّ لَبَّيْكَ. And then they did the ceremony of taqlid," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0330 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3115.99 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0331 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 330 ;
    minaret:startTime 3105.77 ;
    minaret:text "which was to put the colored necklaces around the necks of their sacrificial animals. And all that happened on the 25th of Dhu al-Qa'dah, and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0331 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3129.27 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0332 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 331 ;
    minaret:startTime 3115.99 ;
    minaret:text "when he reached Makkah it was the 4th of Dhu al-Hijjah, SubhanAllah! How many days? Nine days. It took them nine days to reach there. And then he performed tawaf around the Kaaba and the" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0346 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3267.11 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0347 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 346 ;
    minaret:startTime 3262.93 ;
    minaret:text "اَللّٰهُمَّ مَحِلِّيْ حَیْثُ حَبَسْتَنِیْ—O" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0347 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3276.41 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0348 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 347 ;
    minaret:startTime 3267.11 ;
    minaret:text "O Allah, I will exit ihram wherever You stop me.' And then there are two extra conditions for women, and they are that women should have a mahram," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0360 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3401.17 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0361 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 360 ;
    minaret:startTime 3392.29 ;
    minaret:text "So we learned Ibn Abbas said that Abu Talha told me that Rasulullah performed Hajj and Umrah together, so it was Qiran." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0361 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3411.87 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0362 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 361 ;
    minaret:startTime 3401.79 ;
    minaret:text "But Rasulullah, he wished for Tamattu'. He said: 'And if I were to know my affair before what I had to do, I would not" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0362 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3421.83 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7040_0363 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 362 ;
    minaret:startTime 3411.87 ;
    minaret:text "have brought with me the sacrificial animals, and I would have bought them at Makkah and I would have put off ihram as others have done.' So he wished that he would have done Tamattu'." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0001 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 22.26 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0002 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 1 ;
    minaret:startTime 10.06 ;
    minaret:text "وَيَسِرْلِي أَمْرِي وَحْلُ الْأُقْدَةً مِنْ لِسَانِي يَفْقَهُ قَوْلِي رَبَّنَا زِدَنَا عِلْمًا اللَّهُمَّ فَقِّهْنَا فِي الدِّينِ May Allah give us the correct understanding of every deen." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0040 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 418.38 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0041 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 40 ;
    minaret:startTime 407.28 ;
    minaret:text "mentioned about خُذُوا عَنِّي مَنَاسِكَكُمْ Jابir r.a. reported, I saw Rasulullah s.a.w. flinging pebbles while riding his camel on the day of Nahr." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0041 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 429.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0042 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 41 ;
    minaret:startTime 418.64 ;
    minaret:text "So he was doing this act at the place Jamarat. And he was saying, learn your rituals. Learn your rituals, like learn it from me, by seeing me performing them." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0042 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 440.2 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0043 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 42 ;
    minaret:startTime 430.18 ;
    minaret:text "And then Rasulullah s.a.w. also hinted that for I don't know whether I would be performing Hajj after this Hajj of mine or not. And subhanallah, that was true." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0046 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 479.22 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0047 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 46 ;
    minaret:startTime 467.62 ;
    minaret:text "We learn about that from another narration where we learn that it was narrated from Amar bin Abdullah that Yazid bin Shaiban said, we were standing in Arafat in a place far from the place of standing." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0047 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 491.6 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0048 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 47 ;
    minaret:startTime 479.5 ;
    minaret:text "Like they were far away from Rasulullah s.a.w. And then Ibn Mirba' al-Ansari, he came and he said, I am the messenger of the messenger of Rasulullah s.a.w." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0048 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 500.34 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0049 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 48 ;
    minaret:startTime 491.6 ;
    minaret:text "Like he sent him and he said, stay where you are for it is a place of ritual for you are following the legacy of your father Ibrahim alayhi s.a.w." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0049 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 507.52 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0050 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 49 ;
    minaret:startTime 500.56 ;
    minaret:text "So you don't have to all crowd up at one place. You can stay wherever you are because the plane of Arafat is big." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0052 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 533.92 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0053 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 52 ;
    minaret:startTime 524.76 ;
    minaret:text "So Surah Al-Baqarah, ayah number 196 starts with وَأَتِّمُّ الْحَجَّ وَالْعُمْرَةَ لِلَّهِ And complete your Hajj and Umrah for Allah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0074 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 756.16 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0075 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 74 ;
    minaret:startTime 747.46 ;
    minaret:text "We learned that Rasulullah sallallallahu alayhi wa sallam performed Hajj on an old saddle, wearing a cloak that was worth only four dirhams or less." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0076 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 776.16 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0077 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 76 ;
    minaret:startTime 766.86 ;
    minaret:text "SubhanAllah. Not for any riya, not for any sum'a. Not that people say that, oh, he did Hajj like this and not for any shawaf, subhanAllah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0104 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1057.06 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0105 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 104 ;
    minaret:startTime 1049.34 ;
    minaret:text "So Rasulullah sallallahu alayhi wa sallam said, if anyone breaks a bone or leg or becomes lame, he has come out of ihram." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0105 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1067.04 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0106 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 105 ;
    minaret:startTime 1057.18 ;
    minaret:text "He has come out of the sacred state of ihram and must perform Hajj the following year. Right? That person is not sinful because these situations were not in that person's control." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0106 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1079.72 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0107 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 106 ;
    minaret:startTime 1067.24 ;
    minaret:text "So another narration which is of very similar sort is just the one word is added here which is marid. So whoever breaks a bone, falls sick or becomes lame has exited ihram and he has to perform Hajj the following year." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0118 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1203.1 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0119 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 118 ;
    minaret:startTime 1193.96 ;
    minaret:text "This person was performing the Hajj. Alhamdulillah, right? So this person will be raised saying Labbaik Allahuma Labbaik. So Alhamdulillah that person was doing the task." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0122 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1248.66 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0123 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 122 ;
    minaret:startTime 1238.62 ;
    minaret:text "So they should be of mature age except in the case of a ram. What we learned from our hadith is Rasulullah sallallahu alayhi wa sallam said Sacrifice only a grown" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0123 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1257.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0124 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 123 ;
    minaret:startTime 1248.66 ;
    minaret:text "up animal unless it is difficult for you in which case sacrifice a ram which is of even less than a year old but more than six months of age." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0126 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1294.34 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0127 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 126 ;
    minaret:startTime 1283.68 ;
    minaret:text "So when Rasulullah sallallahu alayhi wa sallam he made a peace deal with Quraysh agreeing to go back and not enter Makkah this time and he told his companions get up and offer your sacrifices." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0127 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1303.3 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0128 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 127 ;
    minaret:startTime 1294.62 ;
    minaret:text "So the narrator who is narrating this narration he mentioned that by Allah not one person among them got up until he had said that three times." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0128 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1313.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0129 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 128 ;
    minaret:startTime 1303.5 ;
    minaret:text "When no one got up he went to Um Salamah his wife radiallahu anha and he told her how the people had reacted Um Salamah radiallahu anha" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0129 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1328.14 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0130 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 129 ;
    minaret:startTime 1313.54 ;
    minaret:text "gave a beautiful advice and she said Ya Rasulullah do you want them to do that and then if you do go out and do not say a word to any one of them until you sacrifice your camel and call your barber to shave your head." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0130 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1333.98 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0131 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 130 ;
    minaret:startTime 1328.38 ;
    minaret:text "When he did that they got up sahaba they got up and they offered their sacrifices as well subhanallah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0133 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1371.7 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0134 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 133 ;
    minaret:startTime 1358.82 ;
    minaret:text "So he said if I should be prevented from reaching the Kaaba then I would do the same as Rasulullah sallallahu alayhi wa sallam did so. So I assumed the ihram for Umrah as Rasulullah sallallahu alayhi wa sallam assumed the ihram for Umrah in the ear of Hudaybiyyah." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0134 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 1378.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0135 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 134 ;
    minaret:startTime 1371.9 ;
    minaret:text "So a person should follow the example of Rasulullah sallallahu alayhi wa sallam if anything of this sort arises." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0199 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2058.12 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0200 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 199 ;
    minaret:startTime 2041.2 ;
    minaret:text "shaving head? So there's a story about the whole thing, SubhanAllah: we learn that Ka'b bin Ujrah, he said Rasulullah Sallallahu Alayhi wa Sallam asked him: 'Perhaps your lice have troubled you?' Ka'b replied: 'Yes, ya Rasulullah.' Rasulullah Sallallahu Alayhi wa Sallam said: 'Have your head shaved, then either fast three days," .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0200 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2067.64 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0201 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 200 ;
    minaret:startTime 2058.12 ;
    minaret:text "or feed six poor persons or slaughter one sheep as a sacrifice so all of these three options were given by him to kaff so" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0221 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2273.24 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0222 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 221 ;
    minaret:startTime 2269.22 ;
    minaret:text "فَمَنْ لَّمْ یَجِدْ فَصِیَامُ ثَلٰثَةِ اَیَّامٍ فِی الْحَجِّ—" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0222 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2275.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0223 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 222 ;
    minaret:startTime 2273.2400000000002 ;
    minaret:text "so three days during hajj when" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0223 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2277.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0224 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 223 ;
    minaret:startTime 2275.54 ;
    minaret:text "وَسَبْعَةٍ اِذَا رَجَعْتُمْ ؕ تِلْكَ عَشَرَةٌ كَامِلَةٌ ؕ—and seven when" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0227 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2324.4 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0228 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 227 ;
    minaret:startTime 2310.48 ;
    minaret:text "what not that person can still fast after eid during the days of tashriq so what's the ruling about that aisha and ibn Umar both of them said nobody was allowed to fast on the days" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0228 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2330.1 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0229 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 228 ;
    minaret:startTime 2324.4 ;
    minaret:text "of Tashreeq, like 11th, 12th, and 13th of Dhu al-Hijjah are called days of Tashreeq." .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0229 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2340.22 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0230 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 229 ;
    minaret:startTime 2330.1 ;
    minaret:text "so no one was allowed no one is still allowed to fast on days of tashriq when you're not at hajj when you're back home you're not supposed to fast on 11 12 and 13 because" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0230 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2350.22 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0231 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 230 ;
    minaret:startTime 2340.22 ;
    minaret:text "these are the days of eating and drinking and it's right after eid so they're considered eid days for believers so nobody was allowed to fast on the days of tashriq except" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0234 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2394.86 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0235 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 234 ;
    minaret:startTime 2384.98 ;
    minaret:text "during the last hajjj of rasul allah he performed umrain hajj he drove a hadhi along with him from dhu hulaifah rasul allah started by" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0235 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2404.96 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0236 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 235 ;
    minaret:startTime 2394.86 ;
    minaret:text "assuming ihram from umrain haj like he got in the umrain haj and the people to perform the umrain haj along with rasul allah some of them brought" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0236 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2410.8399999999997 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0237 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 236 ;
    minaret:startTime 2404.96 ;
    minaret:text "their sacrificial animal and drove it along with them while the others did not so when rasul allah" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0237 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2421.5 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0238 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 237 ;
    minaret:startTime 2411.52 ;
    minaret:text "arrived makkah he said to them whoever among you has driven the sacrificial animal with them should not finish their ihram till this person completes" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0238 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2431.62 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0239 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 238 ;
    minaret:startTime 2421.5 ;
    minaret:text "his hajj and whoever among you has not driven the hajj with him should perform tawaf of the ka'bah and tawaf between safa and marwa which is sa'i then cut short" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0239 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2441.54 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0240 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 239 ;
    minaret:startTime 2431.62 ;
    minaret:text "his hair and finish his ihram and should later assume ihram for hajj so this was the method of hajj tamattu but he must offer a sacrifice and" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0240 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2455.78 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0241 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 240 ;
    minaret:startTime 2441.54 ;
    minaret:text "if anyone cannot afford a had he should fast for three days during the hajj and seven days when he returns home rasul allah performed tawaf of the ka'bah on his arrival at makkah he touched the black stone" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0241 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2467.94 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0242 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 241 ;
    minaret:startTime 2457.58 ;
    minaret:text "which is he touched it first of all and then he did ramal fast walking with moving the shoulders like almost like a job during" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0242 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2477.9 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0243 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 242 ;
    minaret:startTime 2467.94 ;
    minaret:text "the first three rounds around the ka'bah and during the last four rounds he walked after finishing tawaf of the ka'bah he offered two rakat prayer at maqam ibrahim and after finishing the prayer" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0243 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2487.84 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0244 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 243 ;
    minaret:startTime 2477.9 ;
    minaret:text "he went to safi and marwah and then he performed seven rounds of sa'i between them and he did not do any deed forbidden because of ihram so he was following the ihram" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0244 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2495.76 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0245 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 244 ;
    minaret:startTime 2487.84 ;
    minaret:text "restrictions till he finished all the ceremonies of his hajj and he sacrificed his hadhi on the day of nahar which is eid day 10th of du hij he" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0245 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2510.84 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0246 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 245 ;
    minaret:startTime 2496.32 ;
    minaret:text "then hastened onwards to makkah and he performed tawaf of the ka'bah and then everything that was forbidden because of ihram became halal like everything was done now so those who took and drove the hadhi with them did the same as rasul allah" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0246 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2515.58 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0247 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 246 ;
    minaret:startTime 2511.4 ;
    minaret:text "did so sahih al-bukhari hadith number 1998 gives us a clear picture" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0264 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2676.82 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0265 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 264 ;
    minaret:startTime 2666.82 ;
    minaret:text "talbiya labbayk allahum labbayk and whoever gets in ihraam mode then this person should do what should not do rafas should not" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0265 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2684.92 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0266 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 265 ;
    minaret:startTime 2676.82 ;
    minaret:text "do fusuq and should not do jidal so should avoid husband wife relationship and should avoid fusuq and should" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0278 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 2808.18 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0279 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 278 ;
    minaret:startTime 2798.42 ;
    minaret:text "and does not get involved in husband wife relationship and nor commit any sins he will come out as sinless as a" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0306 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3117.8 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0307 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 306 ;
    minaret:startTime 3107.58 ;
    minaret:text "your smile is also sadaqah so insha'Allah keep smiling there commanding good and forbidding evil is sadaqah you're giving directions to a person who's lost is" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0307 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3125.44 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0308 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 307 ;
    minaret:startTime 3117.8 ;
    minaret:text "sadaqah you're seeing of a man with bad sight like you know you help that person who's not able to see so you help that person find the way" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0308 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3136.06 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0309 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 308 ;
    minaret:startTime 3126.0 ;
    minaret:text "and your removal of a rock a thorn or a bone from the road is sadaqah for you your pouring water remains from your bucket into the bucket of another brother is charity for" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0313 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 3177.68 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0314 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 313 ;
    minaret:startTime 3175.02 ;
    minaret:text "وَتَزَوَّدُوْا فَاِنَّ خَیْرَ الزَّادِ التَّقْوٰی—" .

minaret:Speaker_maryam_saeed a minaret:Speaker ;
    minaret:nameEn "Maryam Saeed" ;
    minaret:nameUr "مریم سعید" ;
    minaret:speakerCode "maryam_saeed" .

minaret:QuranVerse_3_97 a minaret:QuranVerse ;
    minaret:juz 4 ;
    minaret:surahNumber 3 ;
    minaret:textClean "فيه آيات بينات مقام إبراهيم ۖ ومن دخله كان آمنا ۗ ولله على الناس حج البيت من استطاع إليه سبيلا ۚ ومن كفر فإن الله غني عن العالمين" ;
    minaret:textIndopak "فِیْهِ اٰیٰتٌۢ بَیِّنٰتٌ مَّقَامُ اِبْرٰهِیْمَ ۚ۬ وَمَنْ دَخَلَهٗ كَانَ اٰمِنًا ؕ وَلِلّٰهِ عَلَی النَّاسِ حِجُّ الْبَیْتِ مَنِ اسْتَطَاعَ اِلَیْهِ سَبِیْلًا ؕ وَمَنْ كَفَرَ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَنِیٌّ عَنِ الْعٰلَمِیْنَ ۟" ;
    minaret:textUthmani "فِيهِ ءَايَٰتُۢ بَيِّنَٰتٌ مَّقَامُ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَۖ وَمَن دَخَلَهُۥ كَانَ ءَامِنًاۗ وَلِلَّهِ عَلَى ٱلنَّاسِ حِجُّ ٱلۡبَيۡتِ مَنِ ٱسۡتَطَاعَ إِلَيۡهِ سَبِيلًاۚ وَمَن كَفَرَ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ غَنِيٌّ عَنِ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ" ;
    minaret:translationEn "In it are clear signs [such as] the standing place of Abraham. And whoever enters it shall be safe. And [due] to Allah from the people is a pilgrimage to the House - for whoever is able to find thereto a way. But whoever disbelieves - then indeed, Allah is free from need of the worlds." ;
    minaret:translationUr "" ;
    minaret:verseNumber 97 ;
    skos:exactMatch qur:quran3-97,
        tafsir:V003_097 .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0046 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 488.08 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7038_0047 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 46 ;
    minaret:startTime 478.1 ;
    minaret:text "وَاَتِمُّوا الْحَجَّ وَالْعُمْرَةَ لِلّٰهِ ؕ 'And complete the Hajj and 'Umrah for Allah.' Like it doesn't say complete the Hajj and Umrah and it doesn't stop there, it says لِلّٰهِ:" .

minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0075 a minaret:TranscriptSegment ;
    minaret:endTime 766.38 ;
    minaret:precedesSegment minaret:Segment_HAJJLT22-7041_0076 ;
    minaret:sequenceIndex 75 ;
    minaret:startTime 756.4 ;
    minaret:text "Then he said, Allahumma hijjatun la riya'a fiha wala sum'a. Oh Allah, a Hajj in which there is no showing off nor reputation sought." .

minaret:QuranVerse_2_197 a minaret:QuranVerse ;
    minaret:juz 2 ;
    minaret:surahNumber 2 ;
    minaret:textClean "الحج أشهر معلومات ۚ فمن فرض فيهن الحج فلا رفث ولا فسوق ولا جدال في الحج ۗ وما تفعلوا من خير يعلمه الله ۗ وتزودوا فإن خير الزاد التقوى ۚ واتقون يا أولي الألباب" ;
    minaret:textIndopak "اَلْحَجُّ اَشْهُرٌ مَّعْلُوْمٰتٌ ۚ فَمَنْ فَرَضَ فِیْهِنَّ الْحَجَّ فَلَا رَفَثَ وَلَا فُسُوْقَ ۙ وَلَا جِدَالَ فِی الْحَجِّ ؕ وَمَا تَفْعَلُوْا مِنْ خَیْرٍ یَّعْلَمْهُ اللّٰهُ ؔؕ وَتَزَوَّدُوْا فَاِنَّ خَیْرَ الزَّادِ التَّقْوٰی ؗ وَاتَّقُوْنِ یٰۤاُولِی الْاَلْبَابِ ۟" ;
    minaret:textUthmani "ٱلۡحَجُّ أَشۡهُرٌ مَّعۡلُومَٰتٌۚ فَمَن فَرَضَ فِيهِنَّ ٱلۡحَجَّ فَلَا رَفَثَ وَلَا فُسُوقَ وَلَا جِدَالَ فِي ٱلۡحَجِّۗ وَمَا تَفۡعَلُواْ مِنۡ خَيۡرٍ يَعۡلَمۡهُ ٱللَّهُۗ وَتَزَوَّدُواْ فَإِنَّ خَيۡرَ ٱلزَّادِ ٱلتَّقۡوَىٰۖ وَٱتَّقُونِ يَٰٓأُوْلِي ٱلۡأَلۡبَٰبِ" ;
    minaret:translationEn "Hajj is [during] well-known months, so whoever has made Hajj obligatory upon himself therein [by entering the state of ihram], there is [to be for him] no sexual relations and no disobedience and no disputing during Hajj. And whatever good you do - Allah knows it. And take provisions, but indeed, the best provision is fear of Allah. And fear Me, O you of understanding." ;
    minaret:translationUr "حج کے مہینے معلوم (مقرر)ہیں تو جو شخص ان مہینوں میں حج کو فرض کر لے تو حج کے دوران نہ کوئی بے حیائی کی بات کرے اور نہ کوئی گناہ کرے اور نہ لڑائی جھگڑا کرے اور نیکی میں سے جو کام بھی تم کرو گے اللہ اس کو جان لے گا اورتم زاد ِراہ لے لو ۔ پس بے شک بہترین زادِ راہ تقوٰی ہے اور اے عقل والو!مجھ سے ڈرتے رہو۔" ;
    minaret:verseNumber 197 ;
    skos:exactMatch qur:quran2-197,
        tafsir:V002_197 .

minaret:QuranVerse_2_196 a minaret:QuranVerse ;
    minaret:juz 2 ;
    minaret:surahNumber 2 ;
    minaret:textClean "وأتموا الحج والعمرة لله ۚ فإن أحصرتم فما استيسر من الهدي ۖ ولا تحلقوا رءوسكم حتى يبلغ الهدي محله ۚ فمن كان منكم مريضا أو به أذى من رأسه ففدية من صيام أو صدقة أو نسك ۚ فإذا أمنتم فمن تمتع بالعمرة إلى الحج فما استيسر من الهدي ۚ فمن لم يجد فصيام ثلاثة أيام في الحج وسبعة إذا رجعتم ۗ تلك عشرة كاملة ۗ ذلك لمن لم يكن أهله حاضري المسجد الحرام ۚ واتقوا الله واعلموا أن الله شديد العقاب" ;
    minaret:textIndopak "وَاَتِمُّوا الْحَجَّ وَالْعُمْرَةَ لِلّٰهِ ؕ فَاِنْ اُحْصِرْتُمْ فَمَا اسْتَیْسَرَ مِنَ الْهَدْیِ ۚ وَلَا تَحْلِقُوْا رُءُوْسَكُمْ حَتّٰی یَبْلُغَ الْهَدْیُ مَحِلَّهٗ ؕ فَمَنْ كَانَ مِنْكُمْ مَّرِیْضًا اَوْ بِهٖۤ اَذًی مِّنْ رَّاْسِهٖ فَفِدْیَةٌ مِّنْ صِیَامٍ اَوْ صَدَقَةٍ اَوْ نُسُكٍ ۚ فَاِذَاۤ اَمِنْتُمْ ۥ فَمَنْ تَمَتَّعَ بِالْعُمْرَةِ اِلَی الْحَجِّ فَمَا اسْتَیْسَرَ مِنَ الْهَدْیِ ۚ فَمَنْ لَّمْ یَجِدْ فَصِیَامُ ثَلٰثَةِ اَیَّامٍ فِی الْحَجِّ وَسَبْعَةٍ اِذَا رَجَعْتُمْ ؕ تِلْكَ عَشَرَةٌ كَامِلَةٌ ؕ ذٰلِكَ لِمَنْ لَّمْ یَكُنْ اَهْلُهٗ حَاضِرِی الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ ؕ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ شَدِیْدُ الْعِقَابِ ۟۠" ;
    minaret:textUthmani "وَأَتِمُّواْ ٱلۡحَجَّ وَٱلۡعُمۡرَةَ لِلَّهِۚ فَإِنۡ أُحۡصِرۡتُمۡ فَمَا ٱسۡتَيۡسَرَ مِنَ ٱلۡهَدۡيِۖ وَلَا تَحۡلِقُواْ رُءُوسَكُمۡ حَتَّىٰ يَبۡلُغَ ٱلۡهَدۡيُ مَحِلَّهُۥۚ فَمَن كَانَ مِنكُم مَّرِيضًا أَوۡ بِهِۦٓ أَذًى مِّن رَّأۡسِهِۦ فَفِدۡيَةٌ مِّن صِيَامٍ أَوۡ صَدَقَةٍ أَوۡ نُسُكٍۚ فَإِذَآ أَمِنتُمۡ فَمَن تَمَتَّعَ بِٱلۡعُمۡرَةِ إِلَى ٱلۡحَجِّ فَمَا ٱسۡتَيۡسَرَ مِنَ ٱلۡهَدۡيِۚ فَمَن لَّمۡ يَجِدۡ فَصِيَامُ ثَلَٰثَةِ أَيَّامٍ فِي ٱلۡحَجِّ وَسَبۡعَةٍ إِذَا رَجَعۡتُمۡۗ تِلۡكَ عَشَرَةٌ كَامِلَةٌۗ ذَٰلِكَ لِمَن لَّمۡ يَكُنۡ أَهۡلُهُۥ حَاضِرِي ٱلۡمَسۡجِدِ ٱلۡحَرَامِۚ وَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَٱعۡلَمُوٓاْ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ شَدِيدُ ٱلۡعِقَابِ" ;
    minaret:translationEn "And complete the Hajj and 'umrah for Allah. But if you are prevented, then [offer] what can be obtained with ease of sacrificial animals. And do not shave your heads until the sacrificial animal has reached its place of slaughter. And whoever among you is ill or has an ailment of the head [making shaving necessary must offer] a ransom of fasting [three days] or charity or sacrifice. And when you are secure, then whoever performs 'umrah [during the Hajj months] followed by Hajj [offers] what can be obtained with ease of sacrificial animals. And whoever cannot find [or afford such an animal] - then a fast of three days during Hajj and of seven when you have returned [home]. Those are ten complete [days]. This is for those whose family is not in the area of al-Masjid al-Haram. And fear Allah and know that Allah is severe in penalty." ;
    minaret:translationUr "اور حج اور عمرہ کو اللہ ہی کے لیے پورا کرو پھر اگر تم روک دئیے جاؤ تو قربانی میں سے جو میسر ہو کر دو اور اپنےسر نہ منڈواؤ جب تک قربانی اپنے ٹھکانے پر نہ پہنچ جائے، پھر تم میں سے جو بیما ر   ہو یا اس کے سر میں کسی طرح کی تکلیف ہو(اور وہ سر منڈوا  لے) تو روزے یا صدقے یا قربانی میں سے کوئی ایک فدیہ دے دے۔ پھر جب تم امن میں آ جاؤ، تو جو کوئی حج (کے دنوں) تک عمرے کا فائدہ اٹھائے تو جو قربانی میسر ہو کر لے ۔ پھر جو (قربانی) نہ پائےتوتین دن کے روزے حج کے دوران اور سات دن کے اس وقت رکھے جب تم (گھروں کو) واپس  جاؤ، یہ پورے دس ہیں۔ یہ (حکم) اس شخص کے لیے ہے جس کے اہل و عیال مسجد حرام (مکہ)کے رہنے والے نہ ہوںاور اللہ سے ڈرتے رہو اور جان لو کہ بے شک اللہ سخت سزا والا ہے ۔" ;
    minaret:verseNumber 196 ;
    skos:exactMatch qur:quran2-196,
        tafsir:V002_196 .

